Quid pro quo, then:|Caveat:","open:dutch:z":"Well, ja,|Goed.|Nou,|Kijk,|Ja, so,","open:yankee:z":"Look here,|Ayuh,|Wicked plain:|Say what you will,|Now then,","open:midlands:z":"Right,|Mind you,|Fair play,|Truth be told,|Here's the rub:","open:prairie:z":"Well, now,|Way I see it,|Out our way,|I'll be honest,|Not to put too fine a point on it,","open:delta:z":"I'll tell you,|Bless it,|Now listen,|Down home we'd say|Lord knows,","open:highplains:z":"Plain speaking,|Straight up,|For my money,|Short version:|Fair warning,","open:mountain:z":"Honest to it,|Up our way,|Simple as this:|Not fancy, but|Square with you,","open:pacific:z":"So,|Okay, so,|Real talk,|Bottom line,|Here's my thing:","close:plain:z":"That is all I have.|Make of it what you like.|Do not quote me.|You did not hear it from me.|Anyway.|There it is.|Take it or leave it.|That is the size of it.|I will not say it twice.|Keep it in the room.","close:formal:z":"I yield the remainder of my patience.|The record can say what it likes.|So noted.|With that, I am done.|I leave it with you.","close:latin:z":"Quod erat, and all that.|Sic transit.|Res ipsa loquitur.|Dixi.|Requiescat, the bill.","close:faith:z":"God is the Most High. The rest is staffing.|Christ is King; the House is only the House.|Pray for the count.|Say one for me.","time:any:z":"by Thursday|before the recess|after the roll call|this week|by the weekend|before the markup|before the district work period|by sundown|after Mass on Sunday|in the morning|before the clerk closes the book|by the third reading|before the governor's call|after the dinner|before the cloakroom empties","feel:any:p":"glad|relieved|hopeful|pleased|encouraged|steadier|grateful|lighter|easier","feel:any:n":"tired|worried|sore|uneasy|fed up|angry|weary|wary|sick of it|bruised|rattled","feel:any:z":"curious|unsure|watchful|thoughtful|undecided|careful|patient","n:any:z":"afternoon|morning|evening|night|week|month|season|year|decade|hour|minute|moment|day|weekday|weekend|habit|rule|reason|excuse|problem|question|answer|point|matter|issue|business|trouble|chance|risk|cost|price|bargain|trade|offer|deal|promise|threat|warning|signal|sign|hint|clue|story|version|account|report|letter|note|card|envelope|stamp|pen|pencil|ink|paper|folder|binder|file|drawer|cabinet|shelf|lamp|chair|table|bench|window|door|stair|step|hall|room|corner|wall|floor|ceiling|roof|yard|street|lane|avenue|square|park|garden|fence|gate|path|road|bridge|river|lake|hill|valley|field|meadow|wood|forest|coast|shore|island|harbour|town|city|village|farm|barn|shed|kitchen|parlour|porch|cellar|attic|car|truck|train|bus|tram|ferry|boat|ship|plane|ticket|timetable|platform|station|depot|map|compass|clock|watch|calendar|diary|ledger|list|tally|sum|total|share|part|piece|half|third|quarter|dozen|handful|crowd|line|queue|group|team|crew|club|society|guild|union|league|council|board|panel|court|jury|judge|lawyer|clerk|officer|guard|porter|driver|farmer|miner|fisher|baker|grocer|teacher|nurse|doctor|vet|pastor|widow|veteran|student|neighbour|stranger|friend|enemy|rival|colleague|partner|mentor|protégé|apprentice|boss|landlord|tenant|owner|worker|voter|citizen|resident|taxpayer|pensioner|bachelor|newlywed|toddler|teenager|elder|ancestor|heir|namesake|coat|hat|scarf|glove|boot|shoe|tie|collar|cuff|button|pocket|bag|case|box|crate|barrel|bottle|glass|cup|mug|pot|kettle|plate|bowl|spoon|knife|fork|bread|butter|cheese|coffee|tea|soup|pie|stew|apple|pear|plum|onion|potato|corn|wheat|barley|oats|hay|milk|egg|ham|bacon|fish|oyster|beer|wine|whisky|cider|sugar|salt|pepper|honey|lard|coal|oil|gas|steel|iron|timber|brick|stone|cloth|wool|cotton|leather|rope|wire|nail|hammer|saw|shovel|plough|tractor|engine|motor|pump|valve|pipe|meter|gauge|switch|bulb|candle|match|fire|smoke|ash|dust|mud|sand|gravel|grass|weed|seed|root|branch|leaf|flower|bloom|thorn|nest|feather|horse|cow|pig|sheep|goat|hen|duck|goose|cat|dog|mouse|crow|gull|heron|deer|fox|hound|mule","place:any:z":"the cloakroom|the shade of the East Steps|the Statuary Corridor|the caucus room|the press gallery|the members' dining room|the subway car|the back stairwell|the rotunda|the reading room|the Speaker's lobby|the committee room|the members' garage|the chapel|the barber's chair downstairs|the coat-check room|the third-floor anteroom|the long-table room"};
  const TPL_RAW = ["greet|*|p|{O} good to see you, {YOU}. The {=weather/coffee/quorum/elevator} held up today, which is more than I can say for the {DOC}.", "greet|*|p|{YOU}. I was hoping I would run into you before {T}.", "greet|*|z|{YOU}. {R:cap}, I have a minute. Not two.", "greet|*|z|Afternoon. If this is about the {DOC}, walk with me.", "greet|*|n|{YOU}. I am {F} and the {DOC} is {A-}. Make it quick.", "greet|*|n|Oh. It is you. I have had a {A-} sort of day.", "opinion|bills|p|I read the {DOC} twice. It is {A+} work, and I do not say that about anything with a {PART} in it.", "opinion|bills|n|{O} the {DOC} is {A-}. Somebody wrote it {=in a hurry/at midnight/for a donor/on a napkin} and hoped nobody would read past the {PART}.", "opinion|bills|n|Strike the {PART} and I will look at it again. As it stands it is {A-}.", "opinion|bills|z|{O} the {DOC} lives or dies on the {PART}. Everything else is staffing.", "opinion|bills|z|{WHO:cap} wants to {=move/table/recommit/whip/pass} it {T}. I want to read it first. We will see who wins.", "opinion|immigration|p|My district has a {=cannery/dairy/harbour/orchard/mill} that runs on newcomers. They start early and pay on time. I am not going to {=deport/turn away/punish} them.", "opinion|immigration|p|{O} a {A+} {=processing center/hearing office/registry date} would clear the backlog in a year. Nobody wants to fund it, which tells you everything.", "opinion|immigration|n|{O} the {=quota/waiting line/visa lottery/backlog} is {A-}. People wait four years for a {=work permit/green card/hearing} and we call that order.", "opinion|immigration|n|{WHO:cap} wants to {=close/seal/double} the whole {=border/quota/program}. I would like them to visit a {=detention center/border county/processing center} first.", "opinion|immigration|z|The {=border/visa/quota} fight is a labour question dressed up as a values question. Count the {=harvest visas/caseloads/empty jobs} and then talk to me.", "opinion|foreign|p|{O} the {=aid package/treaty/loan guarantee/relief convoy} is {A+}. We send a little, we keep a friend. Cheaper than the alternative.", "opinion|foreign|n|We are sending {=an aid package/an arms sale/a credit line} abroad while my county cannot get a {=bridge/levee/state road} fixed. Explain that at a {=church hall/diner/county fair}.", "opinion|foreign|n|{O} the {=aid tranche/embargo/arms sale} is {A-}. The realms will read it as weakness and the district will read it as theft.", "opinion|foreign|z|The realms are watching the {=aid vote/tariff/treaty}. So is the {=farm bureau/harbour masters' guild/union hall}. They want different things.", "opinion|statefed|p|{O} let the states {=decide/experiment/carry it}. The governor knows the {=county roads/schools/rivers} better than this building does.", "opinion|statefed|n|Another unfunded mandate. We tell the {=counties/statehouses/school boards} what to do and send them the bill. They will sue us, and they will be right.", "opinion|statefed|n|{O} if the governor wants to {=defy/ignore/nullify} the {=federal standard/court order/mandate}, let him explain it to a {=federal marshal/circuit court/county clerk}.", "opinion|statefed|z|It comes down to the {=commerce clause/reserved powers/matching fund}. Either the state pays or the federal office pays. Not both.", "opinion|money|p|The war chest is in good shape. I spent it on {=a field office/a phone bank/two mailers/an ad buy} and {=yard signs/a district office/a pollster}. People noticed.", "opinion|money|n|My war chest is {=thin/a rumour/spoken for}. Every {=ad buy/mailer/dinner} costs twice what it did and the donors want a {=favour/meeting/vote} back.", "opinion|money|z|{O} money does not vote. It just makes sure the {=mailer/yard sign/ballot guide} is printed.", "opinion|district|p|Home is {=holding up/better than the papers say/all right}. The {DIST} reopened and the {DIST} is full on Fridays.", "opinion|district|n|Home is {=struggling/quiet/sore}. The {DIST} closed and the {DIST} has nobody under sixty.", "opinion|district|z|In {ME} the {DIST} and the {DIST} are the same three families. You learn to count to three.", "opinion|house|p|{O} the floor was {A+} today. Nobody shouted, two people read the bill.", "opinion|house|n|The floor was {A-} today. The whip counted wrong and the Speaker pretended not to notice.", "opinion|house|z|{O} this House runs on {=favours/grudges/coffee/seniority} and {=paperwork/patience/memory}. The rest is weather.", "gossip|*|*|{O} {X} and the whip were in {P} for an hour. Nobody came out smiling.", "gossip|*|*|You hear about {X}? A {=late dinner/second phone/new tailor/quiet donor}, and a vote nobody can explain.", "gossip|*|*|{X} is telling people {X2} owes them a {=favour/vote/dinner/apology}. {X2} is telling people nothing, which is worse.", "gossip|*|*|Somebody saw {X} in {P} {=last night/this morning/at lunch}, talking to a {=lobbyist/columnist/governor's aide/donor}. Draw your own conclusions.", "gossip|*|*|{O} {X} has a {A-} {=chief of staff/press secretary/brother-in-law} and a {A+} voting record. Guess which one the press found.", "gossip|*|*|The cloakroom says {X} will {=flip on/sink/cosponsor/sit out} the {DOC}. The cloakroom has been wrong before, but not often.", "ask|bills|*|Where are you on the {DOC}? Not the speech. The vote.", "ask|bills|*|If I back your {DOC}, will you back mine? Simple question.", "ask|*|*|What does {ME} think of you these days? Honestly.", "ask|*|*|Have you eaten? You look like a {=Monday/roll call/third reading/recount}.", "agree|*|p|{O} fine. I am with you on this one. Do not make me regret it {T}.", "agree|*|p|Yes. Put me down. Tell {WHO} I said so.", "agree|*|z|I can live with that. My {=staff/wife/husband/conscience} can live with it. We will see about my district.", "refuse|*|n|{O} no. Not this week, not with this {DOC}.", "refuse|*|n|I cannot. {WHO:cap} would have my head on a plate.", "refuse|*|z|Ask me again {T}. Today the answer is no, and it is a {A0} no.", "warn|*|n|{O} watch {X}. They are counting you as a yes and they will be {F} when you are not.", "warn|*|n|Be careful with the {DOC}. It looks {A+} until you read the {PART}.", "warn|*|z|Word to the wise: the {DOC} moves {T}. Have your {=count/amendment/speech/excuse} ready.", "faith|faith|p|I went to {=Mass/service/vespers/the early service} on Sunday. {CRC} through and through, the {A+} kind. I felt {F} after.", "faith|faith|p|The {=parish/chapel/church hall} at home is full again. People came back. Nobody can say why.", "faith|faith|n|Our {=parish/congregation/chapel} is half empty. The bell still rings. Fewer people hear it.", "faith|faith|z|I am {CR}. My grandmother was {CR}. That is not an argument; it is a fact about Sundays.", "faith|faith|z|God is the Most High. Christ is King. The rest of us are on a short term.", "muse|anomaly|*|The {=clock/door/stair/lamp} in {P} was {A} this morning. I counted. Then I stopped counting.", "muse|anomaly|*|Do you ever walk into {P} and feel the {=corridor/room/hour} was waiting for you? I do not ask anyone else.", "muse|anomaly|*|I had a dream about a {=ledger/bill/plaque/page} with my name on it. I knew every word. I wrote none of them.", "muse|anomaly|*|There is a {A} {=door/stair/key/ledger} in this building that nobody has ever been asked to sign for.", "muse|anomaly|*|Some days I think somebody else is walking these halls the way I do. I do not look for them.", "small|weather|*|{O} {=rain/frost/heat/fog} in {ME} and {=sun/sleet/wind/drizzle} here. I packed for the wrong one.", "small|weather|*|The {=fog/rain/cold front/wind} came in {=early/hard/sideways} this morning. The tourists on the East Steps did not care.", "small|family|p|My {FAM} had a {FEV} on Saturday. I made it for the end. {F:cap}, honestly.", "small|family|n|Missed my {FAM}'s {FEV}. Again. The whip does not do birthdays.", "small|family|z|My {FAM} asks what I do here. I tell them I count. They think it is a joke.", "react|*|p|{O} that is {A+} of you. I will remember it {T}.", "react|*|p|Well. I did not expect that. {A+:cap}.", "react|*|n|{O} that was {A-}. I will remember that too.", "react|*|n|Hm. I see. {=Frankly/Honestly/Plainly}, that is not how we do it at home.", "react|*|z|Noted. I am writing it in the {=ledger/notebook/diary}, the one I actually read.", "react|*|z|Hm. I will want to see that in writing before I say a word.", "react|*|z|Could be. I have heard it said both ways this week.", "react|*|z|That is one reading of it. Ask me again after lunch.", "react|*|z|I will take that back to my office and sit with it.", "react|*|z|Maybe. The count will tell us more than either of us can.", "react|*|z|Fair point, though I am not sure it moves anybody.", "react|*|z|I will not argue with you. I will not agree yet, either.", "react|*|z|Interesting. My staff will have a view by morning.", "react|*|z|That is news to me. Who told you?", "react|*|z|Well. It is not nothing.", "opinion|bills|p|{O} the {DOC} is {A+}. Not perfect. {A+:cap} is enough {T}.", "opinion|bills|z|The {PART} is where they hid it. It always is. Read the {PART} and you have read the {DOC}.", "opinion|bills|n|Whoever wrote the {PART} has never met a {=farmer/nurse/county clerk/ferry captain}. I would like to introduce them.", "small|*|z|I keep a {Na} in my desk drawer for days like this. Do not ask.", "small|*|z|Some nights I count the {Nas} on the walk home. It settles me better than the vote count.", "small|*|p|Somebody left a {Na} on my chair this morning. Kindest thing that has happened all week.", "react|*|p|{=Good/Well done/Fair enough}. My {FAM} would say you were raised right.", "react|*|n|I will {=remember/write down/repeat} that, {YOU}. {=Word for word/Exactly as you said it/With the date}.", "muse|anomaly|*|I said a sentence on the floor today I do not remember choosing. It was a good sentence. That is the part that worries me.", "muse|anomaly|*|Whatever I am, I am under God. That part I do not wonder about. The corridor I wonder about.", "gossip|*|*|{X} {=voted early/left by the back stairs/skipped the caucus/sat with the other side} {=again/twice this week/on purpose}. The whip pretended not to see.", "opinion|house|p|{O} the Clerk read the {DOC} without a mistake. Small mercies. I will take a small mercy.", "warn|*|n|{O} if you {=cross/embarrass/ignore} {X} on the {DOC}, they will remember it at the {=markup/roll call/next caucus}.", "agree|*|p|{O} you have my vote. Spend it {=carefully/wisely/like it cost something}.", "faith|faith|p|{O} the {=choir/organist/old priest/deacon} at home {=outdid themselves/sang the long setting/rang the bells for an hour} on Sunday. I went back to work {F}.", "faith|faith|p|We {=lit a candle/said a rosary/kept a vigil/read the psalm} for my {FAM} last {=week/Sunday/month}. {CRC} people do not forget, and neither does God.", "faith|faith|p|I {=pray/kneel/sit a minute} in {P} some mornings before the {DOC} comes up. It is the quietest room I know, and the Most High is in it.", "faith|faith|n|{O} my {=bishop/pastor/minister/elder} wrote to me about the {DOC}. Four pages. I have read the first one {=twice/three times/once, slowly}.", "faith|faith|n|The {=collection plate/choir loft/Sunday school/parish council} back home is {A-} this year. People are tired. I am tired.", "faith|faith|z|{O} I keep the {=Lord's Day/Sabbath/early Mass/evening service} where I can. The {DOC} can wait one morning a week.", "faith|faith|z|{CRC} or not, every man in this building answers to the same God. Christ is King. We are all temporary.", "faith|faith|z|My {FAM} asked me if politicians pray. I said the honest ones pray {=before/after/during} the roll call.", "faith|faith|*|There is a {=chapel/prayer room/quiet pew} off {P}. {=Nobody/Few people/Almost nobody} uses it {T}. That is a pity.", "muse|anomaly|*|{O} the {=echo/light/draft/clock} in {P} is {A} today. It sounds like a {=second set of footsteps/vote being counted/door closing twice}.", "muse|anomaly|*|I found a {Na} in my {=coat/drawer/briefcase} that I never put there. It was {A}. I kept it.", "muse|anomaly|*|The {=portraits/plaques/clocks/windows} in {P} look {A} after dark. I do not stay late anymore. {=Mostly/Usually/Not often}.", "muse|anomaly|*|{O} somebody signed the {=visitor log/ledger/roll} in {P} with a name nobody has. The ink was {=still wet/very old/the wrong colour}.", "muse|anomaly|*|Every {=Thursday/third Friday/recess/full moon} the {=lift/stair/fountain/bell} in {P} does something {A}. I have stopped mentioning it.", "react|*|n|{O} you will {=regret/remember/answer for} that {T}. Not from me. From {ME}.", "react|*|n|{=Right/Fine/Well}. {A-:cap}, but I have seen worse in {P}. Not much worse.", "react|*|n|I {=heard/saw/noticed} that. So did {X}. {X} keeps a list too.", "react|*|n|That is the kind of thing that gets {=written down/repeated/remembered} in {P}, {YOU}. {A-:cap}.", "react|*|n|{O} I am {F}. I will be {F} {T} too. Leave it there.", "react|*|p|{O} I owe you one {T}. Remind me if I forget, which I will not.", "react|*|p|{A+:cap}. {ME} will hear about it from me, the good way.", "react|*|p|That {=helped/landed/mattered}. {X} will not say it, so I will.", "opinion|statefed|p|The governor of {ME} called me {T} about the {=mandate/standard/grant}. For once we agree. Write that down.", "opinion|statefed|n|{O} every {=mandate/preemption/rule} we pass lands on a {=county clerk/school board/sheriff} who never voted for it. {A-:cap}.", "opinion|statefed|z|{O} the states were here first. The federal office was the states' idea. People forget the order of things.", "opinion|statefed|z|The {=state house/governor's office/attorney general} in {ME} has a {A} lawyer on this already. We will be in court {T}.", "opinion|immigration|z|{O} the people on the {=waiting list/visa line/hearing docket} in {ME} have names. I keep a {=list/file/folder} of them.", "opinion|immigration|n|{WHO:cap} has never {=stood in a visa line/read a hearing docket/met a seasonal crew}. It shows in the {PART}.", "opinion|foreign|z|{O} the {=envoy/ambassador/trade delegation} from the realms was in {P} {T}. {A:cap} visit. Very polite. Very long.", "opinion|foreign|p|A {A+} {=treaty/aid line/trade deal} is the cheapest friend you will ever buy. Ask {ME}'s {=harbour/farms/mills}."];
  const BANK = {};
  for(const k in LEX) BANK[k] = LEX[k].split("|");
  const TPL = TPL_RAW.map(r => { const a = r.split("|"); return {i:a[0], t:a[1], s:a[2], x:a.slice(3).join("|")}; });
  /* order-2 chains per intent, over template tokens (slots stay slots) */
  const CH = {};
  TPL.forEach(t => {
    const toks = ["^", "^"].concat(t.x.split(" ")).concat(["$"]);
    const c = CH[t.i] || (CH[t.i] = {});
    for(let i = 2; i < toks.length; i++){
      const key = toks[i-2] + " " + toks[i-1];
      (c[key] || (c[key] = [])).push(toks[i]);
    }
  });
  const SLOT = {
    DOC:"bill|amendment|rider|substitute|conference report|manager's amendment|committee print|chairman's mark|base text|appropriation|authorization|motion".split("|"),
    PART:"section|clause|sunset clause|definitions section|savings clause|effective date|offset|carve-out|reporting requirement|waiver|enacting clause|fiscal note|severability clause".split("|"),
    FAM:"wife|husband|daughter|son|mother|father|sister|brother|grandmother|grandfather|aunt|uncle|niece|nephew|godson|goddaughter".split("|"),
    FEV:"birthday|recital|ballgame|school play|christening|graduation|anniversary|first communion|county fair ribbon".split("|")
  };
  const CULT_OPEN = {dutch:"dutch", yankee:"yankee", midlands:"midlands", prairie:"prairie", delta:"delta", highplains:"highplains", mountain:"mountain", pacific:"pacific"};
  const lexCount = Object.keys(BANK).reduce((s, k) => s + BANK[k].length, 0);
  function rnd(){ return Math.random(); }
  function pickFrom(arr){ return arr[(rnd() * arr.length) | 0]; }
  function idio(m){
    if(!m) return {p:{}, reg:"plain"};
    if(!m.idio || !m.idio.p){
      const tr = m.traits || {};
      const reg = (m.creed === "latin" || m.creed === "consul") && chance(0.35) ? "latin" : ((tr.vanity || 50) > 64 || (tr.discretion || 50) > 72 ? "formal" : "plain");
      m.idio = {p:{}, reg, n:0, last:[]};
    }
    return m.idio;
  }
  function choose(m, list){
    if(!list || !list.length) return "";
    const I = idio(m);
    /* idiolect: a speaker's favourites come back more, with a slow drift */
    let tot = 0; const w = new Array(list.length);
    for(let i = 0; i < list.length; i++){ w[i] = 1 + (I.p[list[i]] || 0); tot += w[i]; }
    let r = rnd() * tot, k = 0;
    for(; k < list.length; k++){ r -= w[k]; if(r <= 0) break; }
    const word = list[Math.min(k, list.length - 1)];
    I.p[word] = Math.min(6, (I.p[word] || 0) + 0.6);
    const keys = Object.keys(I.p);
    if(keys.length > 48){ keys.sort((a, b) => I.p[a] - I.p[b]); for(let i = 0; i < keys.length - 40; i++) delete I.p[keys[i]]; }
    return word;
  }
  function bank(pos, topic, sent){
    const s = sent > 0 ? "p" : sent < 0 ? "n" : "z";
    return BANK[pos + ":" + topic + ":" + s] || BANK[pos + ":" + topic + ":z"] || BANK[pos + ":any:" + s] || BANK[pos + ":any:z"] || [];
  }
  function plural(w){
    if(/ /.test(w)){ const i = w.lastIndexOf(" "); return w.slice(0, i + 1) + plural(w.slice(i + 1)); }
    if(/^[A-Z]/.test(w)) return w;
    if(/(s|x|z|ch|sh)$/.test(w)) return w + "es";
    if(/[^aeiou]y$/.test(w)) return w.slice(0, -1) + "ies";
    return w + "s";
  }
  function third(v){
    const i = v.indexOf(" "), b = i < 0 ? v : v.slice(0, i), rest = i < 0 ? "" : v.slice(i);
    if(/(s|x|z|ch|sh|o)$/.test(b)) return b + "es" + rest;
    if(/[^aeiou]y$/.test(b)) return b.slice(0, -1) + "ies" + rest;
    return b + "s" + rest;
  }
  function ing(v){
    const i = v.indexOf(" "), b = i < 0 ? v : v.slice(0, i), rest = i < 0 ? "" : v.slice(i);
    let o;
    if(/ie$/.test(b)) o = b.slice(0, -2) + "ying";
    else if(/[^e]e$/.test(b)) o = b.slice(0, -1) + "ing";
    else o = b + "ing";
    return o + rest;
  }
  const cap = s => s ? s.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.slice(1) : s;
  /* canon guards: run on every composed line */
  const BAD = [
    /taylor[^.]{0,40}\b(god|lord|almighty|divine|deity|messiah|saviou?r|worship)/i,
    /\b(god|lord|almighty|divine|deity|messiah)[^.]{0,40}taylor/i,
    /\b(like|as great as|greater than|the next|another|a new)\s+(the first consul|taylor)/i,
    /\bdominic\b|\bzachary\b/i,
    /\bhymn\b|7\s*\/\s*7|seven\s*[-\/ ]\s*seven/i,
    /\bconsul\b[^.]{0,30}\bis god\b/i
  ];
  function guard(s){
    if(!s) return null;
    for(const r of BAD) if(r.test(s)) return null;
    return s;
  }
  function topicFor(m, ctx){
    if(ctx && ctx.topic) return ctx.topic;
    try{
      const s = m.sent; const t = s && s.topic;
      if(t === "faith" || t === "creed") return "faith";
      if(t === "money") return "money";
      if(t === "bill" || t === "vote") return "bills";
    }catch(e){}
    const b = G.bill;
    if(b && !b.done && chance(0.5)){
      const k = b.kind || "";
      if(/immig/.test(k)) return "immigration";
      if(/foreign|aid/.test(k)) return "foreign";
      if(/state/.test(k)) return "statefed";
      return "bills";
    }
    return pickFrom(["bills", "district", "house", "money", "immigration", "foreign", "statefed"]);
  }
  function fill(x, m, ctx, topic, sent){
    const st = (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === m.state);
    const cult = st && st.cult;
    const I = idio(m);
    const others = (G.members || []).filter(o => o && o !== m && !o.gone && o.kind === "member" && !o.machine);
    const X = others.length ? pickFrom(others) : null;
    const X2 = others.length > 1 ? pickFrom(others.filter(o => o !== X)) : X;
    const you = G.you ? surname(G.you.name) : "friend";
    const cr = (typeof creedOf === "function") ? creedOf(m.creed) : null;
    return x.replace(/\{(=[^}:]+|[A-Za-z0-9+\-]+)(:cap)?\}/g, (all, k, c) => {
      let w = "";
      if(k.charAt(0) === "="){ w = choose(m, k.slice(1).split("/")); return c ? cap(w) : w; }
      if(k === "O"){
        const regList = BANK["open:" + I.reg + ":z"] || BANK["open:plain:z"];
        const dia = cult && CULT_OPEN[cult] && chance(0.4) ? BANK["open:" + CULT_OPEN[cult] + ":z"] : null;
        w = choose(m, dia || regList);
        if(chance(0.25)) w = "";
      }
      else if(k === "C") w = choose(m, BANK["close:" + (topic === "faith" ? "faith" : I.reg) + ":z"] || BANK["close:plain:z"]);
      else if(k === "N") w = choose(m, bank("n", topic, 0).concat(chance(0.2) ? bank("n", "any", 0).slice(0, 60) : []));
      else if(k === "Ns") w = plural(choose(m, bank("n", topic, 0)));
      else if(k === "Na") w = choose(m, bank("n", "any", 0));
      else if(k === "Nas") w = plural(choose(m, bank("n", "any", 0)));
      else if(k === "DOC") w = choose(m, SLOT.DOC);
      else if(k === "PART") w = choose(m, SLOT.PART);
      else if(k === "DIST") w = choose(m, bank("n", "district", 0));
      else if(k === "FAM") w = choose(m, SLOT.FAM);
      else if(k === "FEV") w = choose(m, SLOT.FEV);
      else if(k === "A+") w = choose(m, bank("a", "any", 1));
      else if(k === "A-") w = choose(m, bank("a", "any", -1));
      else if(k === "A0") w = choose(m, bank("a", "any", 0));
      else if(k === "A") w = choose(m, bank("a", "anomaly", 0));
      else if(k === "V") w = choose(m, bank("v", topic, 0).length ? bank("v", topic, 0) : bank("v", "any", 0));
      else if(k === "Vs") w = third(choose(m, bank("v", topic, 0).length ? bank("v", topic, 0) : bank("v", "any", 0)));
      else if(k === "Vany") w = choose(m, bank("v", "any", 0));
      else if(k === "R") w = choose(m, bank("r", "any", 0));
      else if(k === "WHO") w = choose(m, BANK["who:any:z"]);
      else if(k === "T") w = choose(m, BANK["time:any:z"]);
      else if(k === "F") w = choose(m, bank("feel", "any", sent));
      else if(k === "P") w = choose(m, BANK["place:any:z"]);
      else if(k === "ME") w = m.state || "the district";
      else if(k === "YOU") w = you;
      else if(k === "X") w = X ? surname(X.name) : "somebody";
      else if(k === "X2") w = X2 ? surname(X2.name) : "somebody else";
      else if(k === "CR") w = cr ? cr.adj : "Latin";
      else if(k === "CRC") w = cr ? cr.adj : "Latin";
      else if(k === "BILL") w = (G.bill && G.bill.title) || "the bill";
      return c ? cap(w) : w;
    });
  }
  function tidy(s){
    s = s.replace(/\s+/g, " ").replace(/\s+([.,?!:])/g, "$1").replace(/^\s*[,.]\s*/, "").trim();
    s = s.replace(/\ba ([aeiouAEIOU])/g, "an $1").replace(/\bA ([aeiouAEIOU])/g, "An $1");
    s = s.replace(/\b(\w+) \1\b/gi, "$1");
    s = s.replace(/([.?!]) ([a-z])/g, (a, p, l) => p + " " + l.toUpperCase());
    return cap(s);
  }
  function markov(intent){
    const c = CH[intent]; if(!c) return null;
    let a = "^", b = "^"; const out = [];
    for(let i = 0; i < 30; i++){
      const nx = c[a + " " + b]; if(!nx) break;
      const t = pickFrom(nx); if(t === "$") break;
      out.push(t); a = b; b = t;
    }
    if(out.length < 6 || out.length > 26) return null;
    const s = out.join(" ");
    if(!/[.?!]$/.test(s)) return null;
    if(TPL.some(t => t.x === s)) return null;   /* only novel recombinations */
    return s;
  }
  /* main entry: one line for member m.  ctx = {intent, topic, sent, about} */
  function say(m, ctx){
    if(!m) return "";
    ctx = ctx || {};
    let feel = {warm:0, heat:0, speak:0, attend:0};
    try{ if(typeof netFeel === "function") feel = netFeel(m, {intent:ctx.intent || "inform", heat:0, topics:[ctx.topic || "bill"]}); }catch(e){}
    const warm = (m.rel ? m.rel.warmth : 0) / 100 + (feel.warm || 0) * 0.5;
    let sent = ctx.sent !== undefined ? ctx.sent : (warm > 0.18 ? 1 : warm < -0.18 ? -1 : 0);
    let intent = ctx.intent;
    if(!intent){
      const r = rnd();
      intent = r < 0.30 ? "opinion" : r < 0.48 ? "gossip" : r < 0.60 ? "small" : r < 0.70 ? "ask" : r < 0.78 ? "warn" : "opinion";
      try{ if(m.lv && m.lv.notice > 0.55 && chance(0.18)) intent = "muse"; }catch(e){}
      try{ if(m.faith && m.faith.dev > 70 && chance(0.12)) intent = "faith"; }catch(e){}
    }
    let topic = intent === "faith" ? "faith" : intent === "muse" ? "anomaly" : intent === "small" ? pickFrom(["weather", "family"]) : topicFor(m, ctx);
    const I = idio(m);
    for(let tries = 0; tries < 6; tries++){
      let x = null;
      if(chance(0.22)) x = markov(intent);
      if(!x){
        const s1 = sent > 0 ? "p" : sent < 0 ? "n" : "z";
        let pool = TPL.filter(t => t.i === intent && (t.t === topic || t.t === "*") && (t.s === s1 || t.s === "*"));
        if(!pool.length) pool = TPL.filter(t => t.i === intent && (t.t === topic || t.t === "*"));
        if(!pool.length) pool = TPL.filter(t => t.i === "opinion" && t.t === "house");
        x = pickFrom(pool).x;
      }
      let s = tidy(fill(x, m, ctx, topic, sent));
      /* heat: hot speakers clip their sentences; talkative ones add a tail */
      if((feel.speak || 0) > 0.35 && chance(0.35)) s += " " + tidy(fill("{C}", m, ctx, topic, sent));
      s = guard(s);
      if(!s) continue;
      if(I.last.indexOf(s) >= 0) continue;
      I.last.unshift(s); if(I.last.length > 5) I.last.pop();
      I.n = (I.n || 0) + 1;
      return s;
    }
    return "";
  }
  return {say, lexCount, tplCount:TPL.length, guard, name:"D'Infinite Taylor Consular Neural Organism"};
})();

/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   20261012a · TALK THAT DOES NOT REPEAT ITSELF
   Every line is chosen from several drafts against a memory of what
   the room has already heard: exact lines, word pairs, and each
   speaker's own recent words. People keep their own habits (their
   fillers, their pet words), vary how long they talk, and pick up a
   word from the line before theirs. The canon guard runs last.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
const TK = {g:new Map(), bi:new Map(), sp:new Map(), len:new Map(), prev:null, n:0, on:true};
const TK_STOP = new Set("the a an and or but of to in on at for with is it that this be are was were i you we they he she not no so as by from if do did have has had will would can could just what about there their them our my your me us his her its than then very".split(" "));
const TK_WEAK = /(ly|ing|ed|ness)$|^(actually|really|before|business|anyone|something|nothing|everyone|because|another|whether|though|should|would|could|always|either|people|member|little|nothing|enough|almost|already|without|around|someone|anything|between|through|honest|plainly|probably|whatever|wouldn|couldn|doesn|tomorrow|yesterday|today)$/;
const TK_FILL = ["Look,", "Well,", "Honestly,", "Listen,", "Mind you,", "Frankly,", "See,", "Now,", "I'll say this:", "Between us,", "Truth is,", "Fair enough, but", "Right,", "Here's the thing:", "For what it's worth,", "Granted,"];
const TK_SYN = {
  "think":["reckon","figure","suspect","believe"], "very":["awfully","really","plenty","right"],
  "important":["serious","weighty","no small thing"], "problem":["trouble","snag","headache"],
  "bill":["measure","bill","proposal"], "vote":["vote","tally","count"], "people":["folks","people","voters"],
  "good":["decent","sound","solid"], "bad":["rotten","poor","ugly"], "maybe":["perhaps","maybe","could be"],
  "really":["truly","honestly","really"], "big":["large","sizable","big"], "quickly":["fast","quick","in a hurry"]
};
const TK_REF = ["{W}? ", "You mentioned {w}. ", "About {w}: ", "Since you bring up {w}, ", "As for {w}, ", "Back to {w}. "];
function tkHash(s){ let h = 2166136261; s = String(s); for(let i = 0; i < s.length; i++){ h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); } return h >>> 0; }
function tkWords(s){ return String(s).toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z' ]+/g, " ").split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean); }
function tkScore(m, s){
  const w = tkWords(s); let sc = (TK.g.get(s) || 0) * 50;
  let bs = 0; for(let i = 1; i < w.length; i++) bs += TK.bi.get(w[i-1] + " " + w[i]) || 0;
  sc += bs / Math.max(1, w.length - 1) * 4;
  const mine = TK.sp.get(m.id); if(mine){ let o = 0; w.forEach(x => { if(!TK_STOP.has(x) && mine.has(x)) o++; }); sc += o * 0.9; }
  const ll = TK.len.get(m.id); if(ll !== undefined){ const d = Math.abs(w.length - ll); sc -= Math.min(d, 14) * 0.15; }
  return sc;
}
function tkRemember(m, s){
  const w = tkWords(s);
  TK.g.set(s, (TK.g.get(s) || 0) + 1);
  for(let i = 1; i < w.length; i++){ const k = w[i-1] + " " + w[i]; TK.bi.set(k, (TK.bi.get(k) || 0) + 1); }
  let mine = TK.sp.get(m.id); if(!mine){ mine = new Map(); TK.sp.set(m.id, mine); }
  w.forEach(x => { if(!TK_STOP.has(x)) mine.set(x, (mine.get(x) || 0) + 1); });
  if(mine.size > 260){ const ks = [...mine.keys()].slice(0, 80); ks.forEach(k => mine.delete(k)); }
  TK.len.set(m.id, w.length);
  TK.prev = {who:m.id, s, t:G.t};
  if(++TK.n % 400 === 0){ /* forget slowly so the room can come back to a phrase days later */
    for(const [k, v] of TK.bi) if(v <= 1) TK.bi.delete(k); else TK.bi.set(k, v - 1);
    if(TK.g.size > 6000) TK.g.clear();
  }
}
function tkVoice(m, s, ctx){
  const h = tkHash((m.id || 0) + "|" + (m.name || ""));
  let out = s;
  /* synonyms: each person has their own word for things, used consistently */
  out = out.replace(/\b(think|very|important|problem|vote|people|good|bad|maybe|really|big|quickly)\b/g, (x) => {
    const L = TK_SYN[x]; if(!L || ((h >> (x.length % 8)) & 3) === 0) return x;
    return L[(h + x.length) % L.length];
  });
  /* length: someone who just spoke long answers short, and the reverse */
  const ll = TK.len.get(m.id) || 0;
  const sentences = out.match(/[^.!?]+[.!?]+/g);
  if(sentences && sentences.length > 1 && ll > 18 && chance(0.55)) out = sentences[0].trim();
  /* pick up the line before, when it was someone else's */
  const pv = TK.prev;
  if(pv && pv.who !== m.id && ((ctx.intent === "react" || ctx.intent === "agree") ? chance(0.6) : chance(0.18))){
    /* only pick up a noun: the word right after an article or possessive */
    const cand = []; const reN = /\b(?:the|a|an|this|that|your|my|our|their|his|her)\s+([A-Za-z]{5,12})\b/g; let mm;
    while((mm = reN.exec(pv.s))){ const x = mm[1]; if(!TK_STOP.has(x.toLowerCase()) && !TK_WEAK.test(x.toLowerCase())) cand.push(x); }
    if(cand.length){
      const w = cand[(h + TK.n) % cand.length];
      const f = TK_REF[(h + TK.n) % TK_REF.length];
      const proper = /^[A-Z]/.test(w);
      const lead = f.replace("{w}", proper ? w : "the " + w).replace("{W}", proper ? w : "The " + w);
      const end = lead.trim().slice(-1);
      let body = out;
      /* a bare "Noted." after a lead reads as a clipped telegram: fold it in */
      if(/^(noted|fair|right|sure|agreed|maybe)\.?\s/i.test(body) && end !== "?") body = body.replace(/^\w+\.?\s*/, "");
      out = lead + (end === "." || end === "?" ? body.charAt(0).toUpperCase() : body.charAt(0).toLowerCase()) + body.slice(1);
    }
  } else if(chance(0.30 + ((h & 7) / 30))){
    /* a person's own fillers: three habits each */
    const f = TK_FILL[(h + ((TK.n + h) % 3) * 5) % TK_FILL.length];
    if(out.indexOf(f) !== 0) out = f + " " + out.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + out.slice(1);
  }
  out = out.replace(/\bi\b/g, "I").replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim();
  return out;
}
(function(){
  if(typeof DTCNO === "undefined" || DTCNO.say0) return;
  DTCNO.say0 = DTCNO.say;
  DTCNO.say = function(m, ctx){
    if(!m) return "";
    ctx = ctx || {};
    if(!TK.on) return DTCNO.say0(m, ctx);
    let best = "", bs = 1e9;
    for(let k = 0; k < 4; k++){
      const s = DTCNO.say0(m, ctx); if(!s) continue;
      const sc = tkScore(m, s) + Math.random() * 0.3;
      if(sc < bs){ bs = sc; best = s; }
      if(sc < 0.5) break;
    }
    if(!best) return "";
    let out = best;
    try{ const v = DTCNO.guard(tkVoice(m, best, ctx)); if(v) out = v; }catch(e){}
    tkRemember(m, out);
    return out;
  };
})();

function dtcnoOk(){ return typeof DTCNO !== "undefined" && Math.hypot(cam.vx || 0, cam.vz || 0) <= 0.12; }
function dtcnoPair(a, b){
  if(!dtcnoOk() || !chance(0.55)) return null;
  try{
    const la = DTCNO.say(a, {});
    if(!la) return null;
    const w = (b.rel ? b.rel.warmth : 0);
    const lb = DTCNO.say(b, {intent:chance(0.5) ? "react" : (w > 10 ? "agree" : "react"), sent: w > 20 ? 1 : w < -20 ? -1 : 0});
    return [la, lb || "Mm."];
  }catch(e){ return null; }
}
function dtcnoReact(m){
  /* after one of your choices: a line that answers its tone */
  if(!m || !dtcnoOk() || !TALK.open || TALK.m !== m || !chance(0.5)) return;
  try{
    const note = (el("tkNote") && el("tkNote").innerHTML) || "";
    const sent = /<u>/.test(note) && !/<b>/.test(note) ? -1 : /<b>/.test(note) ? 1 : 0;
    const line = DTCNO.say(m, {intent:"react", sent});
    if(!line) return;
    const say = el("tkSay");
    if(say && say.textContent.length < 260){ say.textContent = say.textContent + " " + line; try{ speakAt(m, line); }catch(e){} }
  }catch(e){}
}
/* ── 20261011h · bills with different fights, a war chest that works, achievements ── */
/* 1 · new kinds of bill: immigration, foreign aid, the states against the Union */
function billFlavor(b){
  if(!b || !b.domain) return b;
  const d = b.domain;
  const T = {
    visa:["Harvest Visa Act","Seasonal Labour Visa Act","Employer-Bonded Visa Act"],
    border:["Border Guard Act","Federal Border Security Act","Crossings and Detention Act"],
    natur:["Naturalization Reform Act","Five-Year Citizenship Act","Oath and Civics Act"]};
  if(d === "visa" || d === "border" || d === "natur"){
    b.kind = "immig";
    b.title = pick(T[d]);
    b.restrict = b.pos.lib < 0;
    b.helps = b.restrict ? "border counties and the wage floor, by its sponsors' account" : "the harbour wards, the orchards and every mill short of hands";
    b.pays = b.restrict ? "the newcomer wards, and every farm that hires at harvest" : "nobody up front; the fight is about who arrives";
    b.why = (b.why || "") + " The newcomer wards are watching the clerk's count.";
  } else if(d === "aid" || d === "arms"){
    b.kind = "foreign";
    /* 20261027b: nobody files aid or arms for a power the Union is at war with, or barely speaking to */
    try{ const rs0 = realmEnsure(), rel = G.realmRel || {}, foe = G.conflict && G.conflict.war ? G.conflict.k : null; const rs = rs0.filter(x => x.k !== foe && (rel[x.k] || 0) > -30); const r = pick(rs.length ? rs : rs0); b.realm = r.k; b.realmT = r.t; b.realmWant = r.want; }catch(e){ b.realmT = "an ally abroad"; }
    const rn = (b.realmT || "the Allies").replace(/^the /, "");
    b.title = d === "aid" ? pick(["Aid to " + rn + " Act", rn + " Grain and Credit Act", "Foreign Assistance (" + rn + ") Act"])
                          : pick(["Arms to " + rn + " Act", rn + " Arms Sale Act", "Friendly Realms Arms Act"]);
    b.helps = (b.realmT || "an ally") + ", and the ports that load the ships";
    b.pays = "the treasury, which every district believes is theirs";
    b.why = "Cabled from " + (b.realmT || "abroad") + ": they want " + (b.realmWant || "help") + ". The envoy has been in the corridor all week.";
  } else if(d === "mandate" || d === "preempt"){
    b.kind = "statefed";
    const hot = (G.states || []).slice().sort((x, y) => (y.unrest || 0) - (x.unrest || 0))[0];
    b.target = (hot && hot.n) || b.state;
    b.title = d === "mandate" ? pick(["School Standards Mandate Act", "Federal Standards Act", "Uniform Schools Act"])
                              : pick(["Federal Preemption Act", "One Rule Act", "Interstate Uniformity Act"]);
    b.helps = d === "preempt" ? "one rule for the whole Union, and the firms that work across state lines" : "whoever the standard protects, if the states can pay for it";
    b.pays = d === "preempt" ? "the statehouses, which lose the pen" : "the states, out of their own budgets: an unfunded mandate";
    b.why = "The governor of " + b.target + " has already said, on the record, that the state will not comply.";
  }
  return b;
}
function echoEnsure(){ if(!G.echoes) G.echoes = []; return G.echoes; }
function echoLater(days, k, text, data){ echoEnsure().push({day:(G.day || 1) + days, k, t:text, data:data || {}}); }
function billConsequences(b, passed, yourVote){
  if(!b || !b.kind) return;
  const you = G.you, ays = yourVote > 0;
  G.billKinds = G.billKinds || {}; G.billKinds[b.kind] = (G.billKinds[b.kind] || 0) + 1;
  try{ if(G.billKinds.immig && G.billKinds.foreign && G.billKinds.statefed) achieve("variety"); }catch(e){}
  if(b.kind === "immig"){
    const newcomerHome = you.origin === "newcomer" || you.origin === "harbour";
    const hurtHome = passed && b.restrict && newcomerHome;
    (G.states || []).forEach(s => { if(s.cult === "pacific" || s.cult === "dutch") s.unrest = clamp((s.unrest || 0) + (passed && b.restrict ? 5 : passed ? -3 : 1), 0, 100); });
    echoLater(rint(2, 4), "immig", passed
      ? (b.restrict ? "The harvest crews did not come back to the orchards this week. " + b.title + " is being blamed at every co-op meeting."
                    : "Night-school naturalization classes are full past the doors. The first cohort under " + b.title + " takes the oath in the spring.")
      : "With " + b.title + " dead, the processing centers say the line is now four years long, and getting longer.",
      {dA: (ays === newcomerHome ? (newcomerHome ? -1 : 1) : 0) + (hurtHome && ays ? -4 : 0) + (!ays && newcomerHome && b.restrict ? 3 : 0)});
  } else if(b.kind === "foreign"){
    G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {};
    const k = b.realm || "reach";
    G.realmRel[k] = clamp((G.realmRel[k] || 0) + (passed ? 12 : -10), -100, 100);
    if(G.money) G.money.index = Math.round((G.money.index - (passed ? 1 : 0)) * 10) / 10;
    echoLater(rint(2, 5), "foreign", passed
      ? cap(b.realmT || "The ally") + " cabled thanks through the envoy and sent a grain shipment at cost. The district papers ran it under a photograph of a pothole."
      : cap(b.realmT || "The ally") + " recalled its attaché for consultations. Nobody here can say what that means. Everybody there can.",
      {dA: passed && ays ? -2 : (!passed && !ays ? 1 : 0), realm:k});
  } else if(b.kind === "statefed"){
    const st = b.target || b.state;
    const S = (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === st);
    if(S) S.unrest = clamp((S.unrest || 0) + (passed ? 9 : -4), 0, 100);
    const mine = you.state === st;
    if(passed){
      G.cases = G.cases || [];
      G.cases.push({t:st + " v. the Union (" + b.title + ")", state:st, day:G.day, voted:ays ? [you.name] : []});
      if(G.cases.length > 12) G.cases.splice(0, G.cases.length - 12);
      echoLater(2, "statefed", "The attorney general of " + st + " has filed suit against " + b.title + ". The governor says the state will not spend a guilder on it until a court says so.", {dA: mine ? (ays ? -5 : 3) : 0});
      echoLater(rint(5, 8), "statefed", chance(0.5)
        ? "The circuit court upheld " + b.title + ". " + st + " has asked the supreme bench to hear it. Federal marshals are in the state capitol for the first time in a decade."
        : "The circuit court struck down the funding section of " + b.title + " as an unfunded mandate. The rest stands. Both sides called it a win.", {dA:0});
    } else {
      echoLater(rint(2, 3), "statefed", "In " + st + ", the governor held a press conference on the capitol steps to thank the members who voted no. He read their names. " + (mine && !ays ? "Yours was one of them." : ""), {dA: mine ? (!ays ? 4 : -2) : 0});
    }
  }
}
function echoNight(news){
  const E = echoEnsure();
  for(let i = E.length - 1; i >= 0; i--){
    const e = E[i];
    if((G.day || 1) < e.day) continue;
    E.splice(i, 1);
    news.push(e.t);
    if(e.data && e.data.dA && G.you){
      let d = e.data.dA;
      if(d < 0 && G.you.legal && e.k === "statefed"){ d = Math.round(d / 2); G.you.legal = false; news.push("Your legal fund took the first of the calls. The damage was smaller than it might have been."); }
      G.you.approval = clamp(G.you.approval + d, 0, 100);
    }
  }
  /* the war chest's standing works: district office, staff */
  if(G.you){
    if(G.you.dOffice) G.you.approval = clamp(G.you.approval + 0.5, 0, 100);
    if(G.you.staff) G.you.influence = clamp((G.you.influence || 0) + 0.5 * Math.min(3, G.you.staff), 0, 100);
  }
}
/* 2 · the war chest */
const CHEST = [
  {k:"ads", t:"Run ads at home", c:30, d:"Radio and the county papers. Approval now, and a little in the race."},
  {k:"office", t:"Open a district office", c:45, d:"A storefront on Main with your name on it. A little approval every day for the rest of the term.", once:true},
  {k:"staff", t:"Hire a legislative aide", c:25, d:"More reach every day: a little influence each morning (up to three aides)."},
  {k:"field", t:"Fund field operations", c:35, d:"Doors knocked, lists cleaned, rides to the polls. Counts on election day."},
  {k:"ally", t:"Back an ally's campaign", c:20, d:"A cheque to a colleague's race. They will remember it, and it helps them hold their seat."},
  {k:"legal", t:"Retain counsel", c:25, d:"A legal fund. The next suit or mandate fight that lands on you costs half."},
  {k:"poll", t:"Commission a poll", c:15, d:"Read six members you could not read, and hear what home thinks of you."},
  {k:"press", t:"Buy time on the East Steps press", c:20, d:"A slot with the cameras. Standing and approval."}
];
function chestCard(){
  const you = G.you;
  G.running = false;
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">The war chest · ' + money(you.funds) + '</div><h1>Spend it, or it is just a number</h1>' +
    '<p class="dream">Field ' + (you.field || 0) + ' · aides ' + (you.staff || 0) + (you.dOffice ? ' · district office open' : '') + (you.legal ? ' · counsel retained' : '') + '</p>' +
    CHEST.map(c => {
      const off = you.funds < c.c || (c.once && you.dOffice) || (c.k === "staff" && (you.staff || 0) >= 3) || (c.k === "legal" && you.legal);
      return '<div class="whip__row"><span class="whip__n">' + c.t + ' <i>' + money(c.c) + '</i></span><span class="whip__w">' + c.d + '</span>' +
        '<span class="whip__b"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost whip__go" data-chest="' + c.k + '"' + (off ? ' disabled' : '') + '>Spend</button></span></div>';
    }).join("") +
    '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="chestClose">Close the ledger</button></div>';
  veil.hidden = false;
  el("chestClose").addEventListener("click", () => walkNow());
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-chest]").forEach(bt => bt.addEventListener("click", () => { chestSpend(bt.getAttribute("data-chest")); }));
}
function chestSpend(k){
  const you = G.you, c = CHEST.find(x => x.k === k);
  if(you.office === "bench" && !you.out && k !== "legal"){ note("Judges do not campaign. The chest stays shut while you sit on the bench.", true); return; }
  if(!c || you.funds < c.c) return;
  if(k === "ally"){ chestAllyCard(); return; }
  you.funds -= c.c;
  you.spent = (you.spent || 0) + c.c;
  let msg = "";
  if(k === "ads"){ you.approval = clamp(you.approval + 4, 0, 100); you.field = (you.field || 0) + 2; msg = "The ads run all week. Your mother calls to say you looked tired."; }
  else if(k === "office"){ you.dOffice = true; msg = "A storefront on Main, two desks and a coffee pot. People come in to complain, which is the point."; }
  else if(k === "staff"){ you.staff = (you.staff || 0) + 1; msg = "You hire an aide who reads everything twice. Your desk gets smaller."; }
  else if(k === "field"){ you.field = (you.field || 0) + 6; msg = "Volunteers, lists, a rented van. None of it shows until election day."; }
  else if(k === "legal"){ you.legal = true; msg = "Counsel retained. They bill by the quarter hour and they are worth it."; }
  else if(k === "poll"){
    const unread = (G.members || []).filter(m => m.kind === "member" && !m.gone && (m.known || 0) < 1).slice(0, 6);
    unread.forEach(m => m.known = Math.max(m.known || 0, 1));
    msg = "The pollster reads six of them for you" + (unread.length ? " (" + listify(unread.map(m => surname(m.name))) + ")" : "") + ". Home rates you at " + Math.round(you.approval) + ", and the trend is " + (you.approval > 50 ? "kind." : "not.");
  }
  else if(k === "press"){ you.standing = clamp((you.standing || 0) + 3, 0, 100); you.approval = clamp(you.approval + 2, 0, 100); you.influence = clamp((you.influence || 0) + 2, 0, 100); msg = "Ten minutes with the cameras on the East Steps. You said one thing and they ran it twice."; }
  note(msg, true);
  try{ achieve("spend"); if(k === "office") achieve("office"); if((you.spent || 0) >= 150) achieve("bigspender"); }catch(e){}
  chestCard();
}
function chestAllyCard(){
  const you = G.you;
  const list = (G.members || []).filter(m => m.kind === "member" && !m.gone && !m.machine && m.party === you.party).sort((a, b) => (b.rel.warmth || 0) - (a.rel.warmth || 0)).slice(0, 8);
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">Back an ally</div><h1>Whose race?</h1>' +
    list.map(m => '<div class="whip__row"><span class="whip__n">' + m.name + '</span><span class="whip__w">margin ' + (m.margin || 0) + (m.backed ? ' · you backed them' : '') + '</span>' +
      '<span class="whip__b"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost whip__go" data-back="' + m.id + '">' + money(20) + '</button></span></div>').join("") +
    '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="allyBack">Back</button></div>';
  el("allyBack").addEventListener("click", () => chestCard());
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-back]").forEach(bt => bt.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const m = byId(+bt.getAttribute("data-back")); if(!m || you.funds < 20) return;
    you.funds -= 20; you.spent = (you.spent || 0) + 20;
    m.backed = (m.backed || 0) + 5;
    ripple(m, 9, "They put money into my race without being asked. I will not forget it.", 9, true);
    note("You backed " + m.name + "'s race. It will show at the polls, and in the cloakroom.", true);
    try{ achieve("spend"); achieve("patron"); }catch(e){}
    chestCard();
  }));
}
/* 3 · achievements */
const ACH = [
  {k:"whip", t:"Whip", d:"Worked a colleague the whip count had against you."},
  {k:"rival", t:"Who Blinked", d:"Outlasted a rival to the end of the feud."},
  {k:"truce", t:"The Diner Booth", d:"Turned a rival into something like a friend."},
  {k:"cosponsor", t:"Signed On", d:"Got a colleague's name on your bill."},
  {k:"ownbill", t:"Author", d:"Filed a bill of your own."},
  {k:"spend", t:"The Chest Opens", d:"Spent from the war chest."},
  {k:"office", t:"Storefront", d:"Opened a district office."},
  {k:"patron", t:"Patron", d:"Backed an ally's race."},
  {k:"bigspender", t:"Ledger Heavy", d:"Spent 150k from the war chest in one career."},
  {k:"variety", t:"Three Fights", d:"Saw an immigration bill, a foreign aid bill and a states-versus-Union bill to the roll."},
  {k:"reelect", t:"Held", d:"Won re-election."},
  {k:"steps", t:"Still Here", d:"Lost the seat and kept going from the East Steps."},
  {k:"higher", t:"Another Room", d:"Won an office beyond the House."},
  {k:"night", t:"Somebody Was Here", d:"Found what the night left in your office.", hidden:true},
  {k:"anomaly", t:"Unexplained", d:"Found something the building will not explain.", hidden:true},
  {k:"anomaly3", t:"Notebook", d:"Found three things the building will not explain.", hidden:true},
  {k:"received", t:"Received", d:"Changed where you kneel, the slow way.", hidden:true},
  {k:"home", t:"Came Home", d:"Made a confession and returned to the Latin Rite.", hidden:true},
  {k:"smash", t:"Iconoclast", d:"Smashed a Consular idol.", hidden:true},
  {k:"listen", t:"Listener", d:"Let ten colleagues talk without interrupting.", hidden:true},
  {k:"days30", t:"A Month of Sittings", d:"Served thirty days."}
];
function achieve(k){
  G.ach = G.ach || {};
  if(G.ach[k]) return false;
  const a = ACH.find(x => x.k === k); if(!a) return false;
  G.ach[k] = G.day || 1;
  if(k === "anomaly"){ try{ if((G.life && G.life.found || 0) >= 3) achieve("anomaly3"); }catch(e){} }
  try{
    let t = el("achToast");
    if(!t){ t = document.createElement("div"); t.id = "achToast"; t.className = "ach-toast"; document.body.appendChild(t); }
    t.innerHTML = '<i>Achievement</i><b>' + a.t + '</b><span>' + a.d + '</span>';
    t.classList.add("is-on");
    clearTimeout(achieve._t); achieve._t = setTimeout(() => t.classList.remove("is-on"), 4200);
  }catch(e){}
  try{ feed("Achievement: " + a.t + ".", "big"); }catch(e){}
  return true;
}
function achCard(){
  G.running = false;
  const got = G.ach || {};
  const n = ACH.filter(a => got[a.k]).length;
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">Achievements · ' + n + ' of ' + ACH.length + '</div><h1>What the record will say</h1>' +
    ACH.map(a => {
      const has = !!got[a.k];
      const show = has || !a.hidden;
      return '<div class="whip__row' + (has ? '' : ' ach--locked') + '"><span class="whip__n">' + (show ? a.t : '???') + (has ? ' <i>day ' + got[a.k] + '</i>' : '') + '</span>' +
        '<span class="whip__w">' + (show ? a.d : 'Hidden until you find it.') + '</span><span class="whip__b"></span></div>';
    }).join("") +
    '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="achClose">Close</button></div>';
  veil.hidden = false;
  el("achClose").addEventListener("click", () => walkNow());
}
function achDaily(){
  try{ if((G.day || 1) >= 30) achieve("days30"); }catch(e){}
}

/* ── 20261011i · the ladder: distinct roles, term limits in law, NPC careers ── */
function lawEnsure(){
  if(!G.law) G.law = {limits:{house:0, senate:2, gov:2, pres:2, bench:0}};
  if(G.noLimits) G.law.limits.pres = 0;
  return G.law;
}
function officeTermsOf(k){ const y = G.you; if(k === "house") return y.terms || 0; y.officeTerms = y.officeTerms || {}; return y.officeTerms[k] || 0; }
function termLimited(k){
  const lim = lawEnsure().limits[k] || 0;
  if(!lim) return false;
  /* the limit binds those who hold the office and want it again */
  return officeTermsOf(k) >= lim;
}
function careerWon(seeking){
  const y = G.you;
  y.officeTerms = y.officeTerms || {};
  y.officeTerms[seeking] = (y.officeTerms[seeking] || 0) + 1;
  if(seeking === "house") y.office = "house";
  y.role = null; y.staffOf = null; y.envoyTo = null;
}
/* NPCs walk the ladder too: a member with a record may leave for the Senate or a governorship */
function npcLadder(news){
  G.ladder = G.ladder || [];
  let n = 0;
  const cands = G.members.filter(m => m.kind === "member" && !m.gone && !m.machine && !(typeof isChaplain === "function" && isChaplain(m))
    && (m.terms || 0) >= 2 && (m.influence || 0) > 40);
  cands.forEach(m => {
    if(n >= 2 || !chance(0.14)) return;
    n++;
    const to = chance(0.5) ? "senate" : "gov";
    const won = chance(0.5 + (m.influence - 40) / 120);
    if(won && (m.traits.ambition || 50) > 62 && (m.traits.loyalty || 50) < 58 && chance(0.12 + ((m.traits.ambition || 50) - 62) / 160)){
      try{ dualStart(m, to, news); }catch(e){}
      return;
    }
    G.members = G.members.filter(x => x !== m);
    G.seatsBy[m.party] = Math.max(0, (G.seatsBy[m.party] || 1) - 1);
    const where = to === "gov" ? "the governor's chair in " + m.state : "the Senate";
    G.ladder.unshift({name:m.name, party:m.party, state:m.state, to, won, term:G.term, creed:m.creed});
    if(G.ladder.length > onumLim(40,"hist")) G.ladder.length = onumLim(40,"hist");
    try{ accolade(m, (won ? "Left the House for " : "Gave up the seat to run for ") + where + "."); }catch(e){}
    const line = won ? m.name + " gave up the seat and won " + where + ". The House loses a vote and gains a phone call."
                     : m.name + " gave up the seat to run for " + where + " and lost. Last seen on the East Steps, shaking hands.";
    if(news) news.push(line); else note(line, true);
  });
}
function senateColleague(){
  const s = (G.ladder || []).filter(x => x.won && x.to === "senate");
  return s.length ? "Senator " + pick(s).name : "Senator " + newName(pick(STATES));
}
/* the powers that come with the chair you hold */
function roleKey(){
  const y = G.you;
  if(y.out) return y.staffOf ? "staff" : y.envoyTo ? "envoy" : "out";
  const o = y.office || "house";
  if(o !== "house") return o;
  if(y.post === "speaker" || y.post === "leader" || y.post === "minority" || y.post === "whip") return "leader";
  if(y.post === "ways" || y.post === "judic" || y.post === "armed") return "chair";
  return "house";
}
const ROLE_T = {house:"Representative", leader:"Party leadership", chair:"Committee chair", senate:"Senator", gov:"Governor",
  pres:"Executive", bench:"Justice", envoy:"Envoy abroad", staff:"Staff to a member", out:"Out of office"};
function rolePowers(){
  const y = G.you, b = G.bill, live = b && !b.done, k = roleKey(), P = [];
  const once = (key) => { y.used = y.used || {}; return y.used[key] === G.day; };
  const mark = (key) => { y.used = y.used || {}; y.used[key] = G.day; };
  if(k === "leader"){
    const mineQ = (G.billQueue || []).findIndex(x => x && x.mine);
    P.push({t:"Set the calendar: bring your bill to the front", off:mineQ < 1, d:"Your filed bill jumps the queue.", run(){
      const q = G.billQueue; const [mb] = q.splice(mineQ, 1); q.unshift(mb); y.standing = clamp(y.standing - 1, 0, 100);
      return "The calendar is yours to write. " + mb.title + " is next."; }});
    P.push({t:"Discipline a member who broke the line", off:once("disc"), d:"Loyalty up, warmth down.", run(){
      mark("disc");
      const m = pick(G.members.filter(x => x.party === y.party && x.kind === "member" && !x.machine && !x.gone)) ; if(!m) return "Nobody to discipline.";
      m.traits.loyalty = clamp(m.traits.loyalty + 8, 0, 100); ripple(m, -8, "Leadership took my committee slot for a week. I will vote the line. I will remember.", -6, true);
      return "You took " + m.name + "'s committee slot for a week. They will vote the line."; }});
  }
  if(k === "chair"){
    P.push({t:"Hold the bill in committee", off:!live || b.held || once("hold"), d:"The roll call slips two days. The sponsor will not thank you.", run(){
      mark("hold"); b.held = true; b.voteDay += 2; y.standing = clamp(y.standing - 2, 0, 100);
      const sp = b.sponsorId != null ? byId(b.sponsorId) : null; if(sp) ripple(sp, -8, "They sat on my bill in committee.", -6, true);
      return b.title + " sits in your committee for two more days."; }});
    P.push({t:"Mark it up toward your own lines", off:!live || b.marked2, d:"The text moves toward you.", run(){
      b.marked2 = true; for(const a in b.pos) b.pos[a] = Math.round(b.pos[a] + (y.pos[a] - b.pos[a]) * 0.18);
      b.line = describeBill(b); return "You rewrite two clauses in markup. The bill is a little more yours."; }});
  }
  if(k === "senate"){
    P.push({t:"Hold a confirmation hearing", off:once("conf"), d:"A nominee for the bench. Confirm, or make a fight of it.", run(){ mark("conf"); confirmCard(); return null; }});
    P.push({t:"Ratify a treaty", off:once("treaty"), d:"A treaty with a realm abroad: read the terms, hear both sides. Two thirds of the Senate, and you.", run(){ mark("treaty"); treatyCard(); return null; }});
    P.push({t:"Filibuster the bill", off:!live || b.filibustered, d:"Talk until it dies or they give way. It costs you influence; home will judge.", run(){
      b.filibustered = true; b.voteDay += 3; y.influence = clamp(y.influence - 6, 0, 100);
      const fit = districtFit(b); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + (fit < 0 ? 4 : -4), 0, 100);
      return "You held the floor for eleven hours. " + b.title + " slips three days. " + (fit < 0 ? "Home liked it." : "Home did not."); }});
  }
  if(k === "bench"){
    const C = (G.cases || []).filter(c => !c.done);
    C.slice(0, 3).forEach(c => {
      const recuse = c.state === y.state || (c.voted && c.voted.indexOf(y.name) >= 0);
      if(recuse) P.push({t:"Recuse yourself: " + c.t, d:"Your own state or your own vote. The rule is plain.", run(){ c.done = true; c.recused = true; feed("Justice " + surname(y.name) + " recused from " + c.t + ".", "good"); return "You recused. The bench decides without you."; }});
      else {
        if(c.dual != null){
          P.push({t:"Rule for the House: " + c.t, d:"One person, one elected office.", run(){ return benchRule(c, true); }});
          P.push({t:"Rule for the member: " + c.t, d:"The Charter is silent; both seats stand.", run(){ return benchRule(c, false); }});
        } else {
        P.push({t:"Rule for the Union: " + c.t, d:"Uphold the federal act.", run(){ return benchRule(c, true); }});
        P.push({t:"Rule for the state: " + c.t, d:"Strike the mandate.", run(){ return benchRule(c, false); }});
        }
      }
    });
    if(!C.length) P.push({t:"No case is ripe", off:true, d:"State-versus-Union suits land here after the House passes a mandate or preemption.", run(){ return ""; }});
  }
  if(k === "gov"){
    const S = (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === y.state);
    P.push({t:"Veto the statehouse bill", off:!(S && S.bill), d:S && S.bill ? S.bill.title : "Nothing on your desk from the statehouse.", run(){
      const t = S.bill.title; reactState(S, S.bill, false); S.bill = null; S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + 2, 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + rint(-3, 4), 0, 100);
      feed("Governor " + surname(y.name) + " vetoed the " + t + ".", "bad"); return "Vetoed. The statehouse will try again next session."; }});
    P.push({t:"Appoint a state judge", off:once("appt"), d:"Three named candidates, each with their own views and backers.", run(){ appointCard("judge"); return null; }});
    P.push({t:"Appoint an agency head", off:once("appt2"), d:"Roads, schools, the constabulary or health: a named person who will advise you from their own view.", run(){
      const k = ["roads", "schools", "police", "health"][Math.floor((G.day || 0) % 4)]; appointCard(k); return null; }});
    P.push({t:"Defy the federal mandate", off:!(G.billKinds && G.billKinds.statefed) || y.defied === G.term, d:"Refuse the money and the rule. Home cheers; the Union sends lawyers.", run(){
      y.defied = G.term; if(S) S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + 6, 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 6, 0, 100); y.standing = clamp(y.standing - 4, 0, 100);
      G.cases = G.cases || []; G.cases.push({t:"the Union v. " + y.state, state:y.state, day:G.day, voted:[]});
      return "You stood on the capitol steps and said no. The Union's attorney filed by supper."; }});
    P.push({t:"Lead a trade mission abroad", off:once("trade") || y.funds < 20, d:"Foreign money spent at home. Costs 20k from the chest.", run(){
      mark("trade"); y.funds -= 20; const r = pick(realmEnsure()); G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}; G.realmRel[r.k] = clamp((G.realmRel[r.k] || 0) + 6, -100, 100);
      if(S) S.ind = clamp(S.ind + 2, 0, 100); return "Four days in " + r.capital + ". You came back with a cannery contract."; }});
  }
  if(k === "pres"){
    const last = (G.lastActs || []).find(a => !a.signed && !a.vetoed);
    P.push({t:last ? "Veto: " + last.title : "No act awaits your signature", off:!last, d:"Send it back to the House.", run(){
      last.vetoed = true; y.standing = clamp(y.standing - 3, 0, 100); y.influence = clamp(y.influence + 3, 0, 100);
      reactAct(last.title, last.pos, false); feed(execTitle() + " " + surname(y.name) + " vetoed the " + last.title + ".", "bad"); return "Vetoed. The House can override with two thirds, if it can find them."; }});
    if(last) P.push({t:"Sign: " + last.title, d:"Make it law with your name on it.", run(){ last.signed = true; reactAct(last.title, last.pos, true); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 2, 0, 100); return "Signed, with eleven pens."; }});
    P.push({t:"Appoint a cabinet secretary", off:once("cab"), d:"Three named candidates; the Senate will have its say.", run(){ appointCard("cab"); return null; }});
    P.push({t:"Send foreign aid on your own authority", off:once("aid"), d:"Money abroad, a realm warmer, a district colder.", run(){
      mark("aid"); const r = pick(realmEnsure()); const M = realmMotive(r.k); G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}; G.realmRel[r.k] = clamp((G.realmRel[r.k] || 0) + 12, -100, 100);
      y.approval = clamp(y.approval - 2, 0, 100); if(G.money) G.money.index = Math.round((G.money.index - 0.5) * 10) / 10;
      feed("The executive sent grain and credit to " + r.t + ".", "good"); return r.t + " takes the grain. They had asked for " + M.ask + ". " + M.because + (/grain|iron|credit|aid|river|food/.test(M.ask) ? " This is close to that." : " Grain is not what they named, and " + M.pow + " will say so."); }});
  }
  if(k === "out"){
    const allies = G.members.filter(m => m.party === y.party && m.kind === "member" && !m.machine && !m.gone && (m.rel.warmth || 0) > 10);
    P.push({t:"Join a member's staff", off:!allies.length, d:"Work for someone who kept their seat. It keeps your name in the building.", run(){
      const m = allies.sort((a, b) => b.rel.warmth - a.rel.warmth)[0]; y.staffOf = m.id; y.role = "staff";
      return "You are now on " + m.name + "'s staff. Your old badge still opens the cloakroom door."; }});
    P.push({t:"Accept an envoy's posting abroad", off:(y.standing || 0) < 35 || !(G.exec && !G.exec.you), d:"The executive needs a voice in a foreign capital.", run(){
      const r = pick(realmEnsure()); y.envoyTo = r.k; y.role = "envoy";
      return "You are posted to " + r.capital + ". The cables home will carry your name."; }});
  }
  if(k === "staff"){
    const m = byId(y.staffOf);
    P.push({t:"Draft a bill for your member", off:!m || once("draft"), d:"Their name on it, your work in it.", run(){
      mark("draft"); m.influence = clamp(m.influence + 3, 0, 100); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 2, 0, 100);
      return "You wrote it in a night. " + m.name + " filed it in the morning and thanked you in the cloakroom."; }});
    P.push({t:"Leave the staff", d:"Back to the East Steps.", run(){ y.staffOf = null; y.role = null; return "You hand in the badge."; }});
  }
  if(k === "envoy"){
    const r = realmEnsure().find(x => x.k === y.envoyTo);
    P.push({t:"Cable home", off:once("cable"), d:"Tell the Union what " + (r ? r.t : "they") + " want.", run(){
      mark("cable"); G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}; G.realmRel[y.envoyTo] = clamp((G.realmRel[y.envoyTo] || 0) + 6, -100, 100); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100);
      return "Cabled: they want " + (r ? r.want : "time") + "."; }});
    P.push({t:"Come home", d:"Resign the posting.", run(){ y.envoyTo = null; y.role = null; return "You come home to the East Steps."; }});
  }
  return P;
}
/* ── the bench: clerks who read the case, justices who argue it, an opinion you write, and petitions that choose what the Court hears ── */
const BENCH_CLERKS = {senior:"Senior law clerk", clerk:"Law clerk", junior:"Junior law clerk"};
function benchClerks(){
  const y = G.you; G.benchStaff = G.benchStaff || {}; const S = {n:y.state};
  Object.keys(BENCH_CLERKS).forEach(k => { if(!G.benchStaff[k]) G.benchStaff[k] = mkOfficial("clerk:" + k + ":" + y.name, S, BENCH_CLERKS[k]); });
  return G.benchStaff;
}
/* which way a justice leans on a case: federalism for state-v-Union suits, one-person-one-office for dual-seat suits */
function justiceLean(j, c){
  const r = rng(seedOf("jl:" + j.name + ":" + c.t)), p = j.pos || {};
  const v = c.dual != null ? (p.lib || 0) * 0.5 - (p.def || 0) * 0.2 : (p.def || 0) * 0.5 + (p.econ || 0) * 0.4 - (p.lib || 0) * 0.2 + (p.wel || 0) * -0.1;
  return v + (r() - 0.5) * 30;
}
function justiceWhy(j, c, forSide, idx){
  const p = j.pos || {}, ax = AXES.slice().sort((a, b) => Math.abs(p[b.k] || 0) - Math.abs(p[a.k] || 0))[0], X = DK_AXIS[ax.k], P = (p[ax.k] || 0) > 0 ? X.hi : X.lo;
  const r = rng(seedOf("jw:" + j.name + ":" + c.t));
  const bank = c.dual != null ? (forSide ? ["The Charter says one person, one office, and I will not read in an exception because it is convenient.", "A seat held in two places is held fully in neither.", "Offices are trusts. A person cannot hold two trusts that may one day pull against each other.", "The framers feared a man in two rooms at once. I take them at their word.", "If we allow it today for someone we like, we allow it tomorrow for someone we do not."]
      : ["The Charter is silent, and a court should not write what the framers left out.", "The voters chose this person twice; I would not undo that on an inference.", "A prohibition has to be written down by someone with the power to write it. We are not that someone.", "I want to see the harm before I vacate a seat. I have not been shown it.", "Silence in the Charter is the legislature's invitation, not ours."])
    : (forSide ? ["The act is the law of the Union and the states may not pick which laws bind them.", "A republic of fifty rulebooks is not a republic. The mandate stands.", "The supremacy clause is not a suggestion, and the state's quarrel is with Congress, not with us.", "If every state may opt out of what it dislikes, the Union is a debating society.", "I see a valid exercise of a power the Charter plainly gives. The policy is for the voters to revisit."]
      : ["The Charter gives the Union enumerated powers, and this is not on the list.", "The states are not the Union's departments. This mandate reaches past what the Charter allows.", "A power that is not named is reserved, and I do not find this one named.", "The state is being told to spend its own money on the Union's idea. That is a commandeering the framers refused.", "Federalism is not a courtesy. It is the reason the states agreed to be a Union at all."]);
  const i0 = Math.floor(r() * bank.length), k = (idx == null ? i0 : (seedOf("jb:" + c.t) + idx) % bank.length);
  return bank[k] + " I come to it as a person who leans " + P.w.toLowerCase() + ", and I will not pretend that has nothing to do with it.";
}
function benchCase(){ return (G.cases || []).find(x => x && !x.done) || null; }
function benchConf2(){
  const y = G.you, c = benchCase(); if(!c){ govCardOpen("Conference", "Nothing is ripe", "No case is ready for conference today. You talk about the long view and the coffee.", "", "bconf"); return null; }
  const clerks = benchClerks(), J = (G.court || []).filter(j => j && !j.you), forS = (j) => justiceLean(j, c) > 0, lobbied = G.confLobby = {};
  const lab = c.dual != null ? ["for the House", "for the member"] : ["for the Union", "for the state"];
  const tally = () => { let u = 0, s2 = 0; J.forEach(j => { const l = lobbied[j.name]; const v = l != null ? l : (forS(j) ? 1 : 0); if(v === 1) u++; else s2++; }); return {u, s2}; };
  const render = () => {
    const t = tally();
    el("cfCount").textContent = "The count so far, without you: " + lab[0] + " " + t.u + ", " + lab[1] + " " + t.s2 + ". Five justices sit; you are the fifth, and three carry it.";
    J.forEach((j, i) => { const l = lobbied[j.name]; const side = l != null ? l === 1 : forS(j); el("jc_" + i).textContent = "“" + justiceWhy(j, c, side, i) + "” — leans " + (side ? lab[0] : lab[1]) + (l != null ? " (you have spoken to them)" : ""); });
  };
  const body = '<div class="muted" style="margin:6px 0">' + pcEsc(c.dual != null ? "Can one person hold two elected offices?" : "A state against the Union over a federal act.") + ' Filed day ' + c.day + (c.state ? ' · ' + pcEsc(c.state) : '') + '.</div>' +
    '<div id="cfCount" class="eyebrow" style="margin:8px 0"></div>' +
    J.map((j, i) => '<div style="margin:8px 0;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)"><b>' + pcEsc(j.name) + '</b> <span class="muted">· Justice · ' + pcEsc(viewWords(j.pos || {})) + ' · named by ' + pcEsc(j.by || "a previous executive") + '</span><div id="jc_' + i + '" style="font-size:13px;margin:4px 0"></div>' +
      '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-lobby="' + i + ':1">Press them ' + lab[0] + ' (3 influence)</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-lobby="' + i + ':0">Press them ' + lab[1] + ' (3 influence)</button></div></div>').join("") +
    '<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:10px">Your clerks</div>' +
    Object.keys(BENCH_CLERKS).map(k => '<div style="margin:6px 0;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)">' + officialHTML(clerks[k]) + '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-clk="' + k + '">Ask what they make of it</button></div><div class="dream" id="ck_' + k + '"></div></div>').join("") +
    '<p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Nothing is decided in conference; it only tells you where the votes are. The opinion is written afterwards.</p>';
  govCardOpen("Conference · " + c.t, "The justices, in their own words", "Each of them has argued it already in their own heads. Their lines are not yours.", body, "bconf");
  render();
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-lobby]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [i, side] = b.getAttribute("data-lobby").split(":"), j = J[+i]; if(lobbied[j.name] != null) return; if(y.influence < 3){ el("gcSay").textContent = "You are short of influence."; return; }
    y.influence -= 3; spend(15, 2); const natural = forS(j) ? 1 : 0, want = +side, odds = (natural === want ? 0.9 : 0.25 + (Math.abs(justiceLean(j, c)) < 12 ? 0.3 : 0));
    lobbied[j.name] = chance(odds) ? want : natural; el("gcSay").textContent = lobbied[j.name] === want ? j.name + " will think about it, and gives you more than they meant to." : j.name + " listens politely and does not move."; render(); }));
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-clk]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const k = b.getAttribute("data-clk"), o = clerks[k], v = justiceLean({pos:o.pos, name:o.name}, c) > 0;
    el("ck_" + k).textContent = "“I read it " + (v ? lab[0] : lab[1]) + ", Justice. " + justiceWhy({pos:o.pos, name:o.name}, c, v) + "”"; }));
  return null;
}
function benchOpinion(){
  const y = G.you, c = benchCase(); if(!c){ govCardOpen("Opinions", "No case is ripe", "There is nothing to decide today. State-versus-Union suits land here once the House passes a mandate.", "", "bopin"); return null; }
  const J = (G.court || []).filter(j => j && !j.you), conf = G.confLobby || {};
  const lab = c.dual != null ? ["for the House", "for the member"] : ["for the Union", "for the state"];
  const recuse = c.state === y.state || (c.voted && c.voted.indexOf(y.name) >= 0);
  if(recuse){ govCardOpen("Opinions · " + c.t, "You must recuse", "Your own state, or a vote you already cast on it. The rule is plain.", '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="rcGo">Recuse</button></div>', null); el("rcGo").addEventListener("click", () => { c.done = true; c.recused = true; el("gcSay").textContent = "You recused. The bench decides without you."; try{ kMark("bopin"); }catch(e){} }); return null; }
  const form = [["narrow", "Narrow opinion", "Decide it on this record only. More justices will join; less changes."], ["broad", "Broad opinion", "Settle the principle for every state. Fewer will join; much changes."]];
  const body = '<p class="muted">Filed day ' + c.day + (c.state ? ' · ' + pcEsc(c.state) : '') + '. Choose your side, then how far you write.</p>' +
    form.map(f => '<div style="margin:8px 0;padding:6px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)"><b>' + pcEsc(f[1]) + '</b> <span class="muted">' + pcEsc(f[2]) + '</span><div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn" data-op="' + f[0] + ':1">Write ' + lab[0] + '</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-op="' + f[0] + ':0">Write ' + lab[1] + '</button></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("Opinions · " + c.t, "Write the opinion", "You are the fifth vote. Your opinion is the Court's voice if three join you; if not, it is a dissent.", body, null);
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-op]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { if(c.done) return; const [fm, side] = b.getAttribute("data-op").split(":"), forU = side === "1";
    let joins = 1; J.forEach(j => { const l = conf[j.name], nat = l != null ? l : (justiceLean(j, c) > 0 ? 1 : 0); let vote = nat === (forU ? 1 : 0); if(vote && fm === "broad" && Math.abs(justiceLean(j, c)) < 14 && chance(0.5)) vote = false; if(vote) joins++; });
    const win = joins >= 3, ax = AXES.slice().sort((a, d) => Math.abs((y.pos || {})[d.k] || 0) - Math.abs((y.pos || {})[a.k] || 0))[0], X = DK_AXIS[ax.k], P = ((y.pos || {})[ax.k] || 0) > 0 ? X.hi : X.lo;
    const text = "Justice " + surname(y.name) + ", " + (win ? "for the Court" : "dissenting") + ": “" + (c.dual != null ? (forU ? "The Charter's plain meaning is one person, one office." : "The Charter is silent on a second seat, and silence is not a prohibition.") : (forU ? "The act is a valid exercise of the Union's powers, and the state's objection is to the policy, not the power." : "The Charter does not enumerate this power, and what is not enumerated is reserved to the states.")) + " " + (fm === "narrow" ? "We decide this record and no more." : "We settle the principle for every state, so that no one needs to litigate it again.") + " I write as one who leans " + P.w.toLowerCase() + ", and I invite the reader to weigh that.”";
    spend(60, 6);
    if(win){ const msg = benchRule(c, forU); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + (fm === "broad" ? 3 : 1), 0, 100); if(fm === "broad"){ try{ setPrecedent("wrote the opinion for the Court in " + c.t, "that the Union's reach " + (forU ? "extends to what the states would rather not do" : "stops short of what the Charter does not name")); }catch(e){} const S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === c.state); if(S) S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + (forU ? 2 : -2), 0, 100); }
      el("gcSay").textContent = text + "\n\nJoined by " + (joins - 1) + " of the other four. " + msg; feed("The Court rules in " + c.t + ", " + joins + " to " + (5 - joins) + ".", "good"); }
    else { const msg = benchRule(c, !forU); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); el("gcSay").textContent = text + "\n\nOnly " + (joins - 1) + " of the other four joined you; the Court goes the other way, " + (5 - joins) + " to " + joins + ". Your dissent is printed beside it. " + msg; feed("The Court rules in " + c.t + ", " + (5 - joins) + " to " + joins + ", over your dissent.", "bad"); }
    el("gcSay").style.whiteSpace = "pre-line"; G.confLobby = {}; try{ kMark("bopin"); }catch(e){} card.querySelectorAll("[data-op]").forEach(z => z.disabled = true); }));
  return null;
}
function benchCert(){
  const y = G.you, clerks = benchClerks(), S0 = (G.states || []), done = {};
  const pool = [["the grain tariff act", "a state's refusal to collect it", 0], ["the pension mandate", "a state's refusal to fund it", 1], ["a school standards act", "a state's objection that education is its own", 2], ["the militia levy", "a state's claim that its own militia is not the Union's to call", 3], ["the river survey act", "a state's claim to its own waters", 4]];
  const picks = pool.slice().sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5).slice(0, 3).map(p => { const st = pick(S0).n; return {t:st + " v. the Union (" + p[0] + ")", state:st, what:p[0], gist:p[1], petitioner:newName(st)}; });
  const body = picks.map((p, i) => { const cl = clerks[["senior", "clerk", "junior"][i]], v = (cl.pos.def || 0) > 5 || (cl.pos.econ || 0) > 12;
    return '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)"><b>' + pcEsc(p.t) + '</b> <span class="muted">petition by ' + pcEsc(p.petitioner) + ', ' + pcEsc(p.state) + '</span><p style="margin:4px 0;font-size:13px">The state objects to ' + pcEsc(p.what) + ': ' + pcEsc(p.gist) + '.</p>' +
      '<div class="muted" style="font-size:12px">' + pcEsc(cl.name) + ' (' + pcEsc(viewWords(cl.pos)) + '): “' + pcEsc(v ? "I would take it. The question is real and the lower courts disagree." : "I would deny it. The record is thin and the question will come back in better shape.") + '”</div>' +
      '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" data-ce="' + i + ':1">Grant review</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-ce="' + i + ':0">Deny</button></div><div class="dream" id="ce_' + i + '"></div></div>'; }).join("");
  govCardOpen("Petitions for review", "What the Court will hear", "The Court chooses its own docket. Four justices must agree; you have the vote of one. Granting a petition puts a real case on the bench.", body, "bcert");
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-ce]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [i, g] = b.getAttribute("data-ce").split(":"), p = picks[+i]; if(done[i]) return; done[i] = 1; spend(15, 2);
    if(g === "1"){ const ok = chance(0.6); if(ok){ G.cases = G.cases || []; G.cases.push({t:p.t, state:p.state, day:G.day, voted:[]}); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); el("ce_" + i).textContent = "Review is granted. " + p.t + " is on the docket and will be argued."; feed("The Court granted review in " + p.t + ".", "good"); } else el("ce_" + i).textContent = "You vote to grant, but the other justices do not join you. It is denied."; }
    else { el("ce_" + i).textContent = "Denied. " + p.petitioner + " will be told by letter, and the lower ruling stands."; }
    card.querySelectorAll('[data-ce^="' + i + ':"]').forEach(z => z.disabled = true); }));
  return null;
}
function benchRule(c, forUnion){
  reactEmit("ruling", {t:c.t, forUnion, state:c.state, dual:c.dual != null});
  if(c.dual != null){
    c.done = true; c.ruled = forUnion ? "union" : "member";
    const m = byId(c.dual);
    feed("The bench ruled for " + (forUnion ? "the House" : (m ? m.name : "the member")) + " in " + c.t + ".", "good");
    G.you.standing = clamp(G.you.standing + 1, 0, 100);
    try{ dualTick(null); }catch(e){}
    return forUnion ? "One person, one elected office. The seat is vacated." : "The Charter is silent, so both seats stand. The House will want an amendment.";
  }
  c.done = true; c.ruled = forUnion ? "union" : "state";
  const S = (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === c.state);
  if(S) S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + (forUnion ? 7 : -5), 0, 100);
  feed("The bench ruled for " + (forUnion ? "the Union" : c.state) + " in " + c.t + ".", forUnion ? "bad" : "good");
  G.you.standing = clamp(G.you.standing + 1, 0, 100);
  return forUnion ? "The act stands. " + c.state + " will comply, slowly." : "The mandate falls. " + c.state + " keeps its money and its schools.";
}
/* ── the Senator's working day: a staff that speaks, a nominee who answers, a treaty with terms, callers with cases ── */
const SEN_ROLES = {chief:"Chief of staff", legdir:"Legislative director", state:"State director"};
function senStaff(){
  const y = G.you; G.senStaff = G.senStaff || {}; const S = {n:y.state};
  Object.keys(SEN_ROLES).forEach(k => { if(!G.senStaff[k]) G.senStaff[k] = mkOfficial("sen:" + k + ":" + y.name, S, SEN_ROLES[k]); });
  return G.senStaff;
}
function senBrief(){
  const y = G.you, st = senStaff(), S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === y.state) || {unrest:30, lean:0, n:y.state}, b = G.bill && !G.bill.done ? G.bill : null;
  const done = {};
  const lean = b ? dkStateLean(S, {pos:b.pos}) : 0;
  const rel = (G.realmRel || {}), realm = WORLD_POWERS.slice().sort((a, c) => (rel[a.k] || 0) - (rel[c.k] || 0))[0];
  const towns = (function(){ try{ return (townsOf(y.state) || []).map(t => t.name); }catch(e){ return []; } })(), town = towns.length ? towns[(G.day || 0) % towns.length] : "the county seat";
  const say = {
    chief:"Morning, Senator. " + (b ? "The " + b.title + " is on the calendar. " + y.state + " leans " + (lean > 12 ? "toward it" : lean < -12 ? "against it" : "both ways on it") + ", so " + (lean > 12 ? "voting aye is the easy vote and I would take it." : lean < -12 ? "an aye will have to be explained at home, and I would want the explanation ready first." : "you can afford to listen to the floor first.") : "Nothing is on the calendar, which gives us a day to do the work nobody sees.") + " Your standing is " + Math.round(y.standing) + (y.standing < 45 ? "; I would build it before you spend it." : "; spend a little of it."),
    legdir:"On the Senate's business: a confirmation hearing in committee, and a treaty with " + (realm ? realm.t : "a neighbour") + " that is " + realmRelLabel(rel[realm ? realm.k : ""] || 0) + " towards us. " + ((st.legdir.pos.def || 0) > 20 ? "I would read the treaty hard: we give away more than we are told." : (st.legdir.pos.def || 0) < -20 ? "I would want that treaty ratified. A paper peace is cheaper than a garrison." : "I have read both and I will tell you what is in them when you ask.") + " The two-thirds rule means one absent senator can sink it.",
    state:"From home: " + (S.unrest > 55 ? "unrest is high, and " + town + " is the worst of it; they want to hear from you by name." : S.unrest > 35 ? town + " is restless but not angry." : "it is quiet; " + town + " asked whether you had forgotten them.") + " " + ((st.state.pos.wel || 0) > 20 ? "Two callers are waiting about pensions and relief, and I would take those first." : (st.state.pos.econ || 0) > 20 ? "The chamber of commerce wants an hour; I would give them one." : "I would take the callers in the order they rang.")
  };
  const acts = {
    chief:[{t:"Plan to vote with " + y.state, d:"Approval if it holds", run(){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 1, 0, 100); return "The chief of staff writes the explanation for home before the vote."; }}, {t:"Hold your vote until the floor speaks", d:"Nothing spent", run(){ return "You keep the vote open."; }}],
    legdir:[{t:"Have the treaty read to you tonight", d:"+1 standing in committee", run(){ y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); return "A summary and the full text are on your desk by evening."; }}, {t:"Ask for the opposition's reading too", d:"A fairer hearing", run(){ y.influence = clamp(y.influence + 1, 0, 100); return "The director sends for the other side's memorandum."; }}],
    state:[{t:"Take the callers first", d:"Approval at home", run(){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 2, 0, 100); return "You tell the state director to book the afternoon for home."; }}, {t:"Send word that you'll write", d:"Small, safe", run(){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 1, 0, 100); return "A letter goes out under your name by evening."; }}]
  };
  const body = Object.keys(SEN_ROLES).map(k => '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)">' + officialHTML(st[k]) + '<p style="margin:6px 0">“' + pcEsc(say[k]) + '”</p>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap">' + acts[k].map((x, j) => '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-sa="' + k + ':' + j + '" title="' + pcEsc(x.d) + '">' + pcEsc(x.t) + '</button>').join("") + '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-sw="' + k + '">Ask why</button></div><div class="dream" id="sa_' + k + '"></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("Staff meeting · " + (y.state || ""), "Your staff, in their own words", "Three people who work for you, each with a view of their own.", body, "sbrief");
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-sw]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const k = b.getAttribute("data-sw"), o = st[k], cr = creedOf(o.creed), og = originOf(o.origin);
    el("sa_" + k).textContent = "“I am " + o.bg + ", of " + cr.t + ", and my people carry the grievance " + og.grievance + ". It colours how I read the room, Senator, so weigh me knowing it.”"; }));
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-sa]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [k, j] = b.getAttribute("data-sa").split(":"); if(done[k]) return; done[k] = 1; spend(10, 1); el("sa_" + k).textContent = acts[k][+j].run(); }));
  return null;
}
/* ── the President's day: a cabinet with views, acts with consequences, capitals with a voice ── */
const PRES_ROLES = {treasury:"Secretary of the Treasury", state:"Secretary of State", war:"Secretary of War", justice:"Attorney General"};
function presStaff(){
  const y = G.you; G.presStaff = G.presStaff || {}; const S = {n:y.state};
  Object.keys(PRES_ROLES).forEach(k => { if(!G.presStaff[k]) G.presStaff[k] = mkOfficial("pres:" + k + ":" + y.name, S, PRES_ROLES[k]); });
  return G.presStaff;
}
function presAdvice(o, role, act){
  const p = o.pos, pos = act.pos || {econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0};
  const axis = {treasury:"econ", state:"def", war:"def", justice:"lib"}[role];
  const v = pos[axis] || 0, mine = p[axis] || 0, agree = v * mine > 0 || (Math.abs(v) < 8 && Math.abs(mine) < 14), X = DK_AXIS[axis];
  const topic = {treasury:"the Treasury's books", state:"how the neighbours will read it", war:"the frontier and the fleet", justice:"how the courts will take it"}[role];
  if(Math.abs(v) < 8) return "On " + topic + " it barely matters, Mr President. " + (mine > 20 ? "My own bent is toward " + (X.hi.w).toLowerCase() + ", so I would not lose sleep over it either way." : "I would sign it and spend the effort elsewhere.");
  return (agree ? "I would sign it. On " + topic + " it moves the country " + dkStr(v) + " toward " + (v > 0 ? X.hi.w : X.lo.w).toLowerCase() + ", which is where I would take it myself." : "I would hold it back. On " + topic + " it moves the country " + dkStr(v) + " toward " + (v > 0 ? X.hi.w : X.lo.w).toLowerCase() + ", and I read that the other way.") + " You should know that is my own view and not the whole cabinet's.";
}
function presActs(){
  const y = G.you, st = presStaff(), acts = (G.lastActs || []).filter(a => !a.signed && !a.vetoed).slice(0, 3);
  if(!acts.length){ govCardOpen("Acts awaiting signature", "Nothing on the desk", "The House and Senate have sent nothing over today.", "", "pacts"); return null; }
  const mem = (G.members || []).filter(m => m && !m.gone && m.kind === "member" && m.pos);
  const body = acts.map((a, i) => { const bill = {pos:a.pos || {econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0}, title:a.title, id:"act:" + a.title};
    let aye = 0; mem.forEach(m => { try{ if(alignment(m, bill) > 0) aye++; }catch(e){} }); const frac = mem.length ? aye / mem.length : 0.5, ovr = frac > 0.68 ? "probable" : frac > 0.55 ? "possible" : "unlikely";
    const lines = ["treasury", "state", "war", "justice"].map(k => '<div style="margin:6px 0"><b>' + pcEsc(st[k].name) + '</b> <span class="muted">· ' + pcEsc(PRES_ROLES[k]) + ' · ' + pcEsc(viewWords(st[k].pos)) + '</span><div style="font-size:13px">“' + pcEsc(presAdvice(st[k], k, a)) + '”</div></div>').join("");
    return '<div style="margin:12px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)"><b>' + pcEsc(a.title) + '</b> <span class="muted">passed day ' + a.day + '</span>' +
      '<details open style="margin:4px 0"><summary class="muted">What it does</summary>' + dkShiftsHTML({pos:bill.pos, title:a.title}) + '</details>' +
      '<details style="margin:4px 0"><summary class="muted">What your cabinet says</summary>' + lines + '</details>' +
      '<p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">If you veto it, a two-thirds override is ' + ovr + ' (about ' + Math.round(frac * 100) + '% of the chamber reads it favourably).</p>' +
      '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-pt="' + i + '"' + (a.cabinetVote ? ' disabled' : '') + '>Put it to the cabinet (aye or nay)</button><button type="button" class="btn" data-ps="' + i + ':s">Sign it</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-ps="' + i + ':v">Veto it</button></div><div class="dream" id="pt_' + i + '">' + (a.cabinetVote ? pcEsc(a.cabinetVote.line || "") : "") + '</div><div class="dream" id="ps_' + i + '"></div></div>'; }).join("");
  govCardOpen("Acts awaiting signature", "On the President's desk", "Each act, what it does axis by axis, and what four members of your cabinet make of it, in their own words.", body, "pacts");
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-pt]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const i = +b.getAttribute("data-pt"), a = acts[i]; if(!a || a.cabinetVote) return; spend(10, 1);
    const q = {pos:a.pos || {econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0}, title:a.title, id:"act:" + a.title}, roll = {aye:[], no:[]};
    Object.keys(PRES_ROLES).forEach(r => { const o = st[r]; let v = 0; try{ v = alignment(o, q); }catch(e){} (v >= 0 ? roll.aye : roll.no).push(o.name); });
    const line = "The cabinet on the " + a.title + ": aye " + roll.aye.length + " (" + (roll.aye.join(", ") || "none") + "), nay " + roll.no.length + " (" + (roll.no.join(", ") || "none") + "). " + (roll.aye.length > roll.no.length ? "The table would sign it." : roll.aye.length < roll.no.length ? "The table would veto it." : "The table is split; it is yours.");
    a.cabinetVote = {d:G.day, aye:roll.aye.length, no:roll.no.length, roll, line}; el("pt_" + i).textContent = line; b.disabled = true; try{ feed(line, ""); }catch(e){} }));
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-ps]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [i, k] = b.getAttribute("data-ps").split(":"), a = acts[+i]; if(a.signed || a.vetoed) return; spend(15, 2);
    let r; if(k === "s"){ a.signed = true; y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 2, 0, 100); reactAct(a.title, a.pos, true); feed(execTitle() + " " + surname(y.name) + " signed the " + a.title + ".", "good"); r = "Signed, with eleven pens."; }
    else { a.vetoed = true; y.standing = clamp(y.standing - 3, 0, 100); y.influence = clamp(y.influence + 3, 0, 100); reactAct(a.title, a.pos, false); feed(execTitle() + " " + surname(y.name) + " vetoed the " + a.title + ".", "bad"); r = "Vetoed. The House can override with two thirds."; }
    el("ps_" + i).textContent = r; card.querySelectorAll('[data-ps^="' + i + ':"]').forEach(z => z.disabled = true); }));
  return null;
}
function realmTouch(k, o){
  o = o || {};
  G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {};
  const was = G.realmRel[k] || 0;
  G.realmRel[k] = clamp(was + (o.rel || 0), -100, 100);
  let w = null; try{ w = worldEnsure(); }catch(e){ w = G.world; }
  if(w){
    if(o.heat) w.heat = clamp((w.heat || 0) + o.heat, 0, 100);
    if(o.bread) w.bread = clamp((w.bread || 1) + o.bread, 0.7, 2.6);
    if(o.foe) w.foe = o.foe;
  }
  if(o.rivalRel && typeof REALM_RIVAL !== "undefined" && REALM_RIVAL[k]){
    const rv = REALM_RIVAL[k];
    G.realmRel[rv] = clamp((G.realmRel[rv] || 0) + o.rivalRel, -100, 100);
  }
  const y = G.you;
  if(y){
    if(o.appr) y.approval = clamp((y.approval || 0) + o.appr, 0, 100);
    if(o.stand) y.standing = clamp((y.standing || 0) + o.stand, 0, 100);
    if(o.infl) y.influence = clamp((y.influence || 0) + o.infl, 0, 100);
    if(o.funds) y.funds = Math.max(0, (y.funds || 0) + o.funds);
    if(o.ind && y.state){ const S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === y.state); if(S) S.ind = clamp((S.ind || 50) + o.ind, 0, 100); }
    if(o.unrest){ const hot = (G.states || []).slice().sort((a, c) => (c.unrest || 0) - (a.unrest || 0))[0]; if(hot) hot.unrest = clamp((hot.unrest || 30) + o.unrest, 0, 100); }
  }
  const P = WORLD_POWERS.find(x => x.k === k);
  const line = o.line || "";
  G.realmWire = G.realmWire || {};
  G.realmWire[k] = {d:G.day || 1, verb:o.verb || "spoke", t:line};
  try{ if(P) loreAdd(P.t, "Day " + (G.day || 1) + ": " + line); }catch(e){}
  try{ const W = wmStore(); W.log.push({d:G.day, k:k, type:"call", how:o.verb || "spoke"}); if(W.log.length > 40) W.log.shift(); W.sel = k; }catch(e){}
  try{ if(P) feed("Abroad — " + P.t + ". " + line); }catch(e){}
  try{ reactEmit("foreign", {k:k, verb:o.verb || "spoke"}); }catch(e){}
  return {was:was, now:G.realmRel[k], line:line};
}
function foreignAtlas(sel){
  const rel = G.realmRel || {}, wire = G.realmWire || {};
  let w = G.world || {}; try{ w = worldEnsure(); }catch(e){}
  const home = (G.country && G.country.name) || "the Republic";
  const short = String(home).replace(/^(The\s+)?(Free\s+|Consular\s+|People's\s+)?(Republic|Commonwealth|Union|Kingdom)\s+of\s+/i, "").replace(/\s+(VII|[IVX]+|\d+)$/, "").slice(0, 22) || "the Republic";
  const P = {rep:[380,118], pale:[380,36], reach:[632,84], horn:[598,190], isles:[200,198], rift:[96,154], marches:[102,68]};
  const W = 760, H = 240;
  let svg = '<svg viewBox="0 0 ' + W + ' ' + H + '" role="img" aria-label="The foreign capitals" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:280px;border-radius:10px;display:block;background:#071018">';
  svg += '<defs><radialGradient id="faSea" cx="48%" cy="44%" r="72%"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#1c4c64"/><stop offset="58%" stop-color="#0e2836"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#070e14"/></radialGradient><filter id="faSoft" x="-20%" y="-20%" width="140%" height="140%"><feDropShadow dx="0" dy="1" stdDeviation="1.4" flood-color="#000" flood-opacity=".5"/></filter></defs>';
  svg += '<rect width="' + W + '" height="' + H + '" fill="url(#faSea)"/>';
  svg += '<g stroke="#245066" stroke-width=".55" opacity=".4">' + [90,180,270,360,450,540,630].map(x => '<line x1="' + x + '" y1="0" x2="' + x + '" y2="' + H + '"/>').join("") + [48,96,144,192].map(y => '<line x1="0" y1="' + y + '" x2="' + W + '" y2="' + y + '"/>').join("") + '</g>';
  svg += '<text x="18" y="22" fill="#8eb4c6" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.5">THE CAPITALS</text>';
  WORLD_POWERS.forEach(p => {
    const b = P[p.k]; if(!b) return;
    const v = rel[p.k] || 0, foe = w && w.foe === p.k;
    svg += '<line x1="' + P.rep[0] + '" y1="' + P.rep[1] + '" x2="' + b[0] + '" y2="' + b[1] + '" stroke="' + realmHue(v) + '" stroke-width="' + (foe ? 3.4 : 1.5) + '" stroke-linecap="round" opacity=".88"' + (foe ? ' stroke-dasharray="6 4"' : '') + '/>';
  });
  svg += '<ellipse cx="' + P.rep[0] + '" cy="' + P.rep[1] + '" rx="58" ry="34" fill="#1a4032" stroke="#e4d4a4" stroke-width="2" filter="url(#faSoft)"/>';
  svg += '<text x="' + P.rep[0] + '" y="' + (P.rep[1] - 2) + '" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f6efe0" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700">' + pcEsc(short) + '</text>';
  svg += '<text x="' + P.rep[0] + '" y="' + (P.rep[1] + 14) + '" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d9c89a" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="10">the capital</text>';
  WORLD_POWERS.forEach(p => {
    const b = P[p.k]; if(!b) return;
    const v = rel[p.k] || 0, foe = w && w.foe === p.k, on = sel === p.k || sel === p.t, wr = wire[p.k];
    const name = String(p.t || "").replace(/^the /, "");
    svg += '<g data-qplace="' + pcEsc(p.t) + '" style="cursor:pointer">';
    svg += '<ellipse cx="' + b[0] + '" cy="' + b[1] + '" rx="' + (on ? 50 : 44) + '" ry="28" fill="' + realmFill(v) + '" stroke="' + (on ? "#ffe7a6" : realmHue(v)) + '" stroke-width="' + (foe ? 2.8 : on ? 2.4 : 1.6) + '" filter="url(#faSoft)"/>';
    svg += '<text x="' + b[0] + '" y="' + (b[1] - 5) + '" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f7f2e8" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="12" font-weight="700">' + pcEsc(name) + (foe ? " !" : "") + '</text>';
    svg += '<text x="' + b[0] + '" y="' + (b[1] + 9) + '" text-anchor="middle" fill="' + realmHue(v) + '" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="10">' + realmRelLabel(v) + " " + (v > 0 ? "+" : "") + Math.round(v) + '</text>';
    if(wr && wr.verb) svg += '<text x="' + b[0] + '" y="' + (b[1] + 21) + '" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ead9a8" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="9">' + pcEsc(String(wr.verb).slice(0, 22)) + '</text>';
    svg += '</g>';
  });
  svg += '<text x="16" y="' + (H - 8) + '" fill="#89a6b6" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="10">Colour is how they stand with you. A dashed line is this term\'s quarrel. The word under a capital is the last decision you made there.</text></svg>';
  return svg;
}
function realmFill(v){
  v = +v || 0;
  if(v >= 60) return "#163d2c";
  if(v >= 25) return "#1e3a26";
  if(v > -25) return "#3a3824";
  if(v > -60) return "#4a3018";
  return "#4a201c";
}
function realmHue(v){
  v = +v || 0;
  if(v >= 60) return "#1f7a4d";
  if(v >= 25) return "#4e8f3a";
  if(v > -25) return "#c6a15a";
  if(v > -60) return "#d4843a";
  return "#c84b3a";
}
function presForeign(){
  const y = G.you, rs = realmEnsure(), rel = G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}, st = presStaff();
  const foeK = G.world && G.world.foe;
  const order = rs.slice().sort((a, c) => (rel[a.k] || 0) - (rel[c.k] || 0));
  const sos = st.state;
  const optsFor = (r) => {
    const M = realmMotive(r.k);
    const rv = (typeof REALM_RIVAL !== "undefined") ? REALM_RIVAL[r.k] : null;
    const rvName = rv ? ((WORLD_POWERS.find(x => x.k === rv) || {}).t || rv) : "their rival";
    return [
      {id:"meet", t:"Meet the ask", tip:"Give them " + M.ask + " in full. They warm a great deal. Bread is dearer at home, the war chest is lighter, and " + rvName + " reads it as you choosing a side."},
      {id:"credit", t:"Credit, not the thing", tip:"A loan, not " + M.ask + ". They take the money and still say the ask was unmet."},
      {id:"schedule", t:"Sign their offer", tip:"They put " + M.give + " in writing, dated. Your state's industry moves. A cold capital may refuse, and say so."},
      {id:"bargain", t:"Quiet bargain", tip:"You meet " + M.ask + " only if they sign " + M.give + " and cool the border. Their hardliners may leak that you tried to buy them."},
      {id:"back", t:"Pull the garrison back", tip:"You give ground before they finish asking. Heat falls. Standing falls. " + rvName + " says you blinked."},
      {id:"line", t:"Name the red line", tip:"You say their line back and you move up: " + M.red + ". Heat rises. If they are the quarrel of the term, it gets hotter."},
      {id:"ports", t:"Close the ports", tip:"An embargo. Relations break. Bread and heat rise. " + rvName + " is pleased. A restless state feels the price."},
      {id:"rival", t:"Take it to " + String(rvName).replace(/^the /, ""), tip:"You do not answer them. You brief " + rvName + " instead. They will hear where the call went."},
      {id:"none", t:"Say nothing yet", tip:"The call ends. They take " + M.ask + " to whoever else will hear it. Sometimes that is " + rvName + ", the same day."}
    ];
  };
  const block = (r, i) => {
    const M = realmMotive(r.k), g = REALM_GOV[r.k] || {}, head = realmFolk(r.k).find(f => f.id === "head"), rl = rel[r.k] || 0;
    const hawk = (sos.pos.def || 0) > 20, dove = (sos.pos.def || 0) < -20;
    const note = hawk ? ("Do not pay them for a reason that is theirs to carry. " + M.because)
      : dove ? ("The reason is theirs and it is real. " + M.because + " A paper is cheaper than keeping a garrison to answer the same sentence.")
      : ("Separate the reason from the price. " + M.because + " Meet the ask only if what they give is dated.");
    const wr = (G.realmWire || {})[r.k];
    return '<details ' + (i < 2 || r.k === foeK ? "open " : "") + 'style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid ' + realmHue(rl) + '"><summary><b>' + pcEsc(head ? head.name : (g.head || "The government")) + '</b> <span class="muted">· ' + pcEsc(g.head || "Head of government") + ' of ' + pcEsc(r.t) + ' · ' + realmRelLabel(rl) + ' (' + Math.round(rl) + ')' + (foeK === r.k ? " · the quarrel" : "") + '</span></summary>' +
      '<p style="margin:6px 0">“' + pcEsc(M.line) + '”</p>' +
      '<p class="muted" style="font-size:12px"><b>Why, in their own government.</b> ' + pcEsc(M.because) + ' ' + pcEsc(M.today) + '</p>' +
      (wr ? '<p class="muted" style="font-size:12px"><b>Last word from you, day ' + wr.d + '.</b> ' + pcEsc(wr.verb) + (wr.t ? " — " + pcEsc(String(wr.t).slice(0, 180)) : "") + '</p>' : '') +
      '<p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">' + pcEsc(sos.name) + ', Secretary of State (' + pcEsc(viewWords(sos.pos)) + '): “' + pcEsc(note) + '”</p>' +
      '<div class="card__actions" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4px">' + optsFor(r).map(o => '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-pf="' + i + ':' + o.id + '" title="' + pcEsc(o.tip) + '" style="white-space:normal;text-align:left;min-height:36px">' + pcEsc(o.t) + '</button>').join("") + '</div>' +
      '<div class="dream" id="pf_' + i + '"></div></details>';
  };
  const body = '<div id="pfMap">' + foreignAtlas(foeK) + '</div><p class="muted" style="font-size:12px;margin:6px 0 2px">Six capitals. Hover a choice to read the cost. The map changes when you decide, and so do the heat, the bread, and the capital you did not call.</p>' + order.map(block).join("");
  govCardOpen("Calls with foreign capitals", "The wire is open", "Each head of government, in their own words. A decision is not a mood. It moves the relation, the price of bread, and the map.", body, "aid");
  const paintMap = (k) => { const m = el("pfMap"); if(m) m.innerHTML = foreignAtlas(k); try{ if(document.body.classList.contains("ui-open")) refreshUnion(); }catch(e){} };
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-pf]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const raw = b.getAttribute("data-pf").split(":"), i = +raw[0], knd = raw.slice(1).join(":"), r = order[i];
    const box = b.parentNode; if(!r || box.getAttribute("data-done")) return; box.setAttribute("data-done", "1");
    spend(20, 3);
    const M = realmMotive(r.k);
    const rv = (typeof REALM_RIVAL !== "undefined") ? REALM_RIVAL[r.k] : null;
    const rvName = rv ? ((WORLD_POWERS.find(x => x.k === rv) || {}).t || rv) : "their rival";
    let o;
    if(knd === "meet") o = {verb:"ask met", rel:18, heat:-4, bread:0.05, funds:-25, rivalRel:-6, appr:-1, stand:1, line:r.t + " can tell " + M.pow + " that the Union met " + M.ask + ". Bread is dearer at home for it, and " + rvName + " reads the choice."};
    else if(knd === "credit") o = {verb:"credit only", rel:6, funds:-18, bread:0.01, line:r.t + " takes the credit. " + M.pow + " will say the ask was still " + M.ask + ", and that money was not it."};
    else if(knd === "schedule"){
      const cold = (rel[r.k] || 0) < -20 && Math.random() < 0.45;
      o = cold ? {verb:"schedule refused", rel:-5, stand:1, line:r.t + " will not sign " + M.give + " while you will not meet " + M.ask + ". They say so, and the wire prints it."}
        : {verb:"schedule signed", rel:11, ind:2, heat:-1, line:"A dated schedule for " + M.give + " is signed with " + r.t + ". It is the writing. It does not, by itself, give them " + M.ask + ". Your own state's workshops feel the paper."};
    } else if(knd === "bargain"){
      const ok = Math.random() < clamp(0.42 + ((rel[r.k] || 0) / 220) + ((y.standing || 50) / 500), 0.18, 0.82);
      o = ok ? {verb:"bargain held", rel:14, heat:-6, ind:1, funds:-12, line:"They sign " + M.give + " and pull a patrol back. You meet " + M.ask + ". Both sides can sell it at home."}
        : {verb:"bargain leaked", rel:-7, heat:3, stand:-1, line:"Their hardliners leak that you tried to buy " + M.ask + " for " + M.give + ". The bargain is dead, and " + r.t + " is colder for having been asked."};
    } else if(knd === "back") o = {verb:"garrison back", rel:9, heat:-8, stand:-2, appr:-1, rivalRel:-5, line:"You pull the garrison back before they finish the sentence. Heat falls. " + rvName + " says you blinked. Standing at home notices."};
    else if(knd === "line") o = {verb:"line named", rel:-12, heat:(G.world && G.world.foe === r.k) ? 12 : 8, stand:3, appr:-1, rivalRel:4, line:"You name their line back to them — " + M.red + " — and you move up. " + M.pow + " hear that the Union chose the line and not the deal."};
    else if(knd === "ports") o = {verb:"ports closed", rel:-22, heat:12, bread:0.08, ind:-2, unrest:4, stand:2, rivalRel:10, line:"The ports to " + r.t + " are closed. Bread moves. Heat moves. " + rvName + " is pleased, and a restless state feels the price."};
    else if(knd === "rival") o = {verb:"carried across", rel:-9, heat:3, rivalRel:9, infl:1, line:"You do not answer " + M.ask + ". You brief " + rvName + ". They are delighted. " + r.t + " learns where the call went."};
    else {
      const spill = Math.random() < 0.35;
      o = {verb:"no answer", rel:-3, heat:spill ? 2 : 0, rivalRel:spill ? 3 : 0, line:"You do not answer " + M.ask + ". " + M.pow + " are told the Union heard the reason and did not move." + (spill ? " By evening the same ask is in " + rvName + "." : " They will take it to whoever else will.")};
    }
    const done = realmTouch(r.k, o);
    const slot = el("pf_" + i); if(slot) slot.textContent = done.line + " Relations " + Math.round(done.was) + " → " + Math.round(done.now) + ".";
    box.querySelectorAll("button").forEach(z => z.disabled = true);
    paintMap(r.k);
  }));
  return null;
}
function presBrief(){
  const y = G.you, st = presStaff(), rel = G.realmRel || {}, foe = WORLD_POWERS.find(p => G.world && p.k === G.world.foe), hot = (G.states || []).slice().sort((a, c) => (c.unrest || 0) - (a.unrest || 0))[0], done = {};
  const say = {
    treasury:"The Union's books are " + ((G.money && G.money.index < 0.5) ? "thin; I would not announce anything new." : "sound for now.") + (hot ? " " + hot.n + " is the worst for unrest, at " + Math.round(hot.unrest) + ", and it will ask for money." : "") + " " + ((st.treasury.pos.econ || 0) > 20 ? "I would answer it with a tax holiday, not a grant." : (st.treasury.pos.econ || 0) < -20 ? "I would answer it with a public works grant, and I would take the heat." : "I would wait for the auditors."),
    state:foe ? cap(foe.t) + " is the rival this term; the temperature is " + Math.round((G.world && G.world.heat) || 0) + ". " + ((st.state.pos.def || 0) > 20 ? "I would meet strength with strength, and say so quietly." : "I would open a channel before anyone opens a fire.") : "No rival is hot this week, which is the time to mend fences.",
    war:"The fleet and the garrisons are at their usual state, which is to say short. " + ((st.war.pos.def || 0) > 20 ? "I want the second base on the strait, and I will argue for it." : (st.war.pos.def || 0) < -20 ? "I would rather not ask for more ships; I would rather ask what they are for." : "I will tell you what they cost when you decide what you want from them."),
    justice:"Two states have a mandate in the courts. " + ((st.justice.pos.lib || 0) > 20 ? "I will defend the people's liberties against the executive, and that includes yours." : (st.justice.pos.lib || 0) < -20 ? "I would not let a technicality slow the Union's work." : "I will give you the law as it is, and you can decide how hard to lean on it.")
  };
  const acts = {
    treasury:[{t:"Answer unrest with a grant", d:"Unrest down, treasury thinner", run(){ if(hot) hot.unrest = clamp(hot.unrest - 3, 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 1, 0, 100); return "A grant is drawn up for " + (hot ? hot.n : "the worst-hit state") + "."; }}, {t:"Wait for the auditors", d:"Nothing spent", run(){ return "You wait."; }}],
    state:[{t:"Open a quiet channel", d:"Realm warmer", run(){ if(foe){ G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}; G.realmRel[foe.k] = clamp((G.realmRel[foe.k] || 0) + 4, -100, 100); } return "A channel is opened through the Secretary's office."; }}, {t:"Meet strength with strength", d:"Standing up, tension up", run(){ y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); if(G.world) G.world.heat = clamp((G.world.heat || 0) + 3, 0, 100); return "The Secretary is told to say it plainly."; }}],
    war:[{t:"Ask what the fleet is for", d:"A fairer review", run(){ y.influence = clamp(y.influence + 1, 0, 100); return "The Secretary of War is told to write you the answer."; }}, {t:"Fund the strait base", d:"Hawk, costly", run(){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval - 1, 0, 100); if(G.world) G.world.heat = clamp((G.world.heat || 0) + 2, 0, 100); return "The base is put on the budget."; }}],
    justice:[{t:"Defend the mandate", d:"Standing", run(){ y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); return "The Attorney General files in your name."; }}, {t:"Hold off for now", d:"Nothing", run(){ return "The filing waits."; }}]
  };
  const body = Object.keys(PRES_ROLES).map(k => '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)">' + officialHTML(st[k]) + '<p style="margin:6px 0">“' + pcEsc(say[k]) + '”</p><div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap">' + acts[k].map((x, j) => '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-pb2="' + k + ':' + j + '" title="' + pcEsc(x.d) + '">' + pcEsc(x.t) + '</button>').join("") + '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-pw="' + k + '">Ask why</button></div><div class="dream" id="pb2_' + k + '"></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("The morning briefing", "The cabinet, in their own words", "Four secretaries, four different lines.", body, null);
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-pw]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const k = b.getAttribute("data-pw"), o = st[k], cr = creedOf(o.creed), og = originOf(o.origin); el("pb2_" + k).textContent = "“I am " + o.bg + ", of " + cr.t + ", and my people carry the grievance " + og.grievance + ". Weigh me knowing it, Mr President.”"; }));
  /* 20261117o JUPITER: the briefing is a sitting of the cabinet. Each choice is put to the table first: the four secretaries vote
     aye or nay in their own interest, the roll is named, and then the President decides, with or against the table. */
  const lean = {treasury:[{econ:-20, wel:20}, {econ:20, wel:-5}], state:[{def:-20, lib:5}, {def:25}], war:[{def:-15, econ:5}, {def:25, econ:-5}], justice:[{lib:20}, {lib:-12}]};
  const tableVote = (k, j) => { const pos = Object.assign({econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0}, lean[k][j]), q = {pos, title:acts[k][j].t, id:"brief:" + k + ":" + j + ":" + G.day}, roll = {aye:[], no:[]};
    Object.keys(PRES_ROLES).forEach(r => { const o = st[r]; let a = 0; try{ a = alignment(o, q); }catch(e){} if(r === k && j === 0) a += 12; (a >= 0 ? roll.aye : roll.no).push(o.name); });
    return roll; };
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-pb2]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [k, j] = b.getAttribute("data-pb2").split(":"); if(done[k]) return; done[k] = 1; spend(10, 1);
    const roll = tableVote(k, +j), carried = roll.aye.length > roll.no.length, tie = roll.aye.length === roll.no.length;
    let out = "Put to the table: " + acts[k][+j].t + ". Aye: " + (roll.aye.join(", ") || "none") + ". Nay: " + (roll.no.join(", ") || "none") + ". " + (tie ? "Tied, " + roll.aye.length + " to " + roll.no.length + "; the President decides." : (carried ? "Carried " : "Lost ") + roll.aye.length + " to " + roll.no.length + ".") + " ";
    out += acts[k][+j].run();
    if(!carried && !tie){ out += " You go against your own table; it is minuted, and the secretaries who were outvoted remember it."; try{ G.you.standing = clamp(G.you.standing - 1, 0, 100); }catch(e){} }
    try{ (G.briefVotes = G.briefVotes || []).push({d:G.day, k, j:+j, t:acts[k][+j].t, aye:roll.aye.length, no:roll.no.length, carried}); if(G.briefVotes.length > onumLim(60, "hist")) G.briefVotes.shift(); }catch(e){}
    try{ feed("Cabinet briefing: " + acts[k][+j].t + " \u2014 " + roll.aye.length + " aye, " + roll.no.length + " nay.", carried || tie ? "good" : "bad"); }catch(e){}
    el("pb2_" + k).textContent = out; card.querySelectorAll('[data-pb2^="' + k + ':"]').forEach(z => z.disabled = true); }));
  return null;
}
function confirmCard(){
  const y = G.you, nom = mkOfficial("nom:" + G.day + ":" + y.name, {n:pick(STATES)}, "Nominee to the federal bench");
  const fit = alignment(y, {pos:nom.pos}), asked = {};
  let grill = 0;
  const ax = AXES.slice().sort((a, c) => Math.abs(nom.pos[c.k]) - Math.abs(nom.pos[a.k]))[0], v = nom.pos[ax.k] || 0, X = DK_AXIS[ax.k], side = v > 0 ? X.hi : X.lo;
  const witness = (G.members || []).filter(m => m && !m.gone && m.kind === "member" && m.pos).sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5).slice(0, 2);
  const wFor = witness[0], wAg = witness[1];
  const q = {
    record:{t:"Ask about their record", say:"“I was " + nom.bg + " before this. On " + ax.n.toLowerCase() + " I have always leaned " + side.w.toLowerCase() + ": I would read the law as a state that " + side.does + ". I will not apologise for it and I will not pretend I have no view.”", d:fit > 0 ? 2 : -1},
    precedent:{t:"Ask how they treat precedent", say:"“Precedent binds me until I can show why it should not. I am " + (nom.temper > 60 ? "stubborn, and I will say so." : "careful, and I will say so.") + " I have overruled my own earlier opinion twice, and I wrote both reasons down.”", d:nom.temper > 60 ? -1 : 2},
    backers:{t:"Ask who recommended them", say:"“" + (wFor ? wFor.name + " (" + wFor.party + ") put my name forward, and I have been honest with " + (wAg ? wAg.name : "the minority") + " that I will not be anyone's vote.”" : "“Nobody you would know, Senator.”"), d:1}
  };
  const body = '<div style="margin:8px 0">' + officialHTML(nom, "By your own answers, they read the law " + (fit > 8 ? "much as you do" : fit < -8 ? "the other way from you" : "somewhere near you") + ".") + '</div>' +
    '<p class="muted" style="font-size:13px"><b>Who backs them:</b> ' + pcEsc(wFor ? wFor.name + " (" + wFor.party + "), who has known them for years" : "a short list of former colleagues") + '. <b>Who objects:</b> ' + pcEsc(wAg ? wAg.name + " (" + wAg.party + "), who thinks they will legislate from the bench" : "nobody in particular") + '. ' + pcEsc(senateColleague()) + ' wants a quick vote.</p>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap">' + Object.keys(q).map(k => '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-cq="' + k + '">' + pcEsc(q[k].t) + '</button>').join("") + '</div><div id="cqSay" class="dream" style="white-space:pre-line"></div>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn" id="cfYes">Confirm</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" id="cfNo">Reject</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" id="cfFight">Make a fight of it</button></div>';
  govCardOpen("Senate Judiciary · confirmation", nom.name, "Nominated to the bench. They will answer anything you ask them, in their own way.", body, null);
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-cq]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const k = b.getAttribute("data-cq"); if(asked[k]) return; asked[k] = 1; spend(10, 1); grill += q[k].d; el("cqSay").textContent += (el("cqSay").textContent ? "\n" : "") + nom.name + ": " + q[k].say; }));
  let fin = false;
  const done = (how) => { if(fin) return; fin = true;
    const odds = clamp(0.5 + fit / 200 + grill * 0.06, 0.1, 0.92);
    let msg = "";
    if(how === "yes"){ G.court = G.court || []; if(G.court.length) G.court[rint(0, G.court.length - 1)] = {name:nom.name, by:"the Senate", pos:nom.pos}; y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); msg = nom.name + " is confirmed to the bench."; }
    else if(how === "no"){ y.standing = clamp(y.standing + (fit < 0 ? 2 : -2), 0, 100); msg = "The committee rejects " + nom.name + ". " + senateColleague() + " is not pleased."; }
    else { const won = chance(1 - odds); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + (won ? 4 : -3), 0, 100); if(!won){ G.court = G.court || []; if(G.court.length) G.court[rint(0, G.court.length - 1)] = {name:nom.name, by:"the Senate", pos:nom.pos}; } msg = won ? nom.name + "'s nomination is withdrawn after a week of hearings." : nom.name + " is confirmed over your objection."; }
    reactEmit("confirm", {name:nom.name, confirmed:/is confirmed/.test(msg)}); el("cqSay").textContent += "\n" + msg; feed(msg, "good"); card.querySelectorAll("#cfYes,#cfNo,#cfFight,[data-cq]").forEach(x => x.disabled = true); };
  el("cfYes").addEventListener("click", () => done("yes")); el("cfNo").addEventListener("click", () => done("no")); el("cfFight").addEventListener("click", () => done("fight"));
  return null;
}
function treatyCard(){
  const y = G.you, rs = realmEnsure(), rel = G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {};
  const r = rs[(G.day || 0) % rs.length], D = DLG[r.k] || {ask:r.want, give:"goodwill", red:"being asked for too much"}, g = REALM_GOV[r.k] || {}, folk = realmFolk(r.k), head = folk.find(f => f.id === "head"), env = folk[0];
  const sens = (G.members || []).filter(m => m && !m.gone && m.kind === "member" && m.pos), sen = sens.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5).slice(0, 2);
  const opp = sen.find(m => (m.pos.def || 0) > 10) || sen[0], sup = sen.find(m => m !== opp) || sen[1];
  const sec = (a, b) => '<p style="margin:6px 0"><b>' + a + '</b> ' + b + '</p>';
  const body = '<p class="muted">' + pcEsc(cap(r.t)) + ' is ' + realmRelLabel(rel[r.k] || 0) + ' towards the Union (' + Math.round(rel[r.k] || 0) + '). ' + pcEsc(g.d || "") + '</p>' +
    sec("Article I — what they ask.", pcEsc(cap(D.ask)) + ".") + sec("Article II — what they give.", pcEsc(cap(D.give)) + ".") +
    sec("Article III — the line they will not cross.", "The Union will not do, and " + pcEsc(r.t) + " will not be asked for, " + pcEsc(D.red) + ".") +
    sec("Article IV — duration.", "Six years, renewable, with an exit clause on ninety days' notice.") +
    sec("Who backs it.", pcEsc(sup ? sup.name + " (" + sup.party + "), who thinks " + D.give + " is worth the price" : "the trade committee") + ".") +
    sec("Who objects.", pcEsc(opp ? opp.name + " (" + opp.party + "), who thinks the Union gives " + D.ask + " and gets a promise" : "the hawks") + ". " + pcEsc(g.powers ? cap(g.powers[0][0]) + " will be watching how the Senate votes." : "") ) +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-tr="env">Hear ' + pcEsc(env.name) + '</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-tr="opp">Hear the objection</button></div><div id="trSay" class="dream" style="white-space:pre-line"></div>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn" data-trv="yes">Ratify</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-trv="res">Ratify with a reservation</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-trv="hold">Hold it in committee</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-trv="no">Reject</button></div>';
  govCardOpen("Treaties and foreign business", "A treaty with " + r.t, "Advice and consent: two thirds of the Senate, and you in the room.", body, null);
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-tr]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const k = b.getAttribute("data-tr");
    el("trSay").textContent += (el("trSay").textContent ? "\n" : "") + (k === "env" ? env.name + " (" + env.title + "): “" + realmVoice(r.k, {}, "what do you want") + " We will not accept " + D.red + ", and I say so before the vote rather than after it.”" : (opp ? opp.name + ": “" + "We would be giving " + D.ask + " to a government that is " + realmRelLabel(rel[r.k] || 0) + " to us, and taking its word for " + D.give + ". I will vote no unless the text says what happens if it does not keep it.”" : "No objection was heard.")); }));
  let fin = false;
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-trv]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { if(fin) return; fin = true; const k = b.getAttribute("data-trv"); spend(30, 3);
    const base = 0.5 + (y.standing - 50) / 200 + (rel[r.k] || 0) / 300; let msg = "";
    if(k === "yes" || k === "res"){ const ok = chance(clamp(base + (k === "res" ? 0.15 : 0), 0.1, 0.95)); rel[r.k] = clamp((rel[r.k] || 0) + (ok ? (k === "res" ? 8 : 15) : -6), -100, 100); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + (ok ? 3 : -2), 0, 100);
      msg = ok ? "The Senate ratifies the treaty with " + r.t + (k === "res" ? ", with your reservation on " + D.red : "") + ". " + senateColleague() + " shakes your hand in the cloakroom." : "The treaty with " + r.t + " falls short of two thirds."; }
    else if(k === "hold"){ rel[r.k] = clamp((rel[r.k] || 0) - 2, -100, 100); msg = "You hold it in committee. " + r.t + " will say you are stalling."; }
    else { rel[r.k] = clamp((rel[r.k] || 0) - 8, -100, 100); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); msg = "You vote it down. " + (env ? env.name : "Their envoy") + " asks for a meeting."; }
    reactEmit("treaty", {k:r.k, verb:k, ok:/ratifies/.test(msg)}); el("trSay").textContent += "\n" + msg; feed(msg, "good"); card.querySelectorAll("[data-trv],[data-tr]").forEach(x => x.disabled = true); }));
  return null;
}
function senCalls(){
  const y = G.you, S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === y.state), done = {};
  const wants = [["dairy farmer", "the co-op road washed out in spring and is still out"], ["widow", "a pension letter that came back unopened"], ["county clerk", "ballots for the special election that never came"], ["mayor", "the water main the state required, which the town cannot pay for"]];
  const calls = wants.slice().sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5).slice(0, 3).map(w => { const name = newName(y.state); return {name, role:w[0], c:caseFile(w[0], w[1], S, name)}; }).filter(x => x.c);
  const body = calls.map((x, i) => '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)"><b>' + pcEsc(x.name) + '</b> <span class="muted">· ' + pcEsc(x.role) + ' · ' + pcEsc(y.state) + '</span><p style="margin:6px 0">“' + pcEsc(x.c.open.join(" ")) + '”</p>' +
    '<div class="muted" style="font-size:12px">It would cost ' + pcEsc(x.c.costText) + '. They would settle for ' + pcEsc(x.c.settle) + '</div>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-cl="' + i + ':1">Raise it in committee (4 influence)</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-cl="' + i + ':2">Promise a letter to the agency</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-cl="' + i + ':3">Say it is for the state</button></div><div class="dream" id="cl_' + i + '"></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("Calls from " + y.state, "People who voted for you", "Three callers, each with something the Senate might do and something it cannot.", body, "scalls");
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-cl]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [i, k] = b.getAttribute("data-cl").split(":"); if(done[i]) return; done[i] = 1; spend(15, 2);
    let r = ""; const x = calls[+i];
    if(k === "1"){ if(y.influence < 4){ r = "You are short of influence; you promise to write instead."; y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 1, 0, 100); } else { y.influence -= 4; y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 3, 0, 100); y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); r = x.name + ": “Then someone is finally listening.” You will raise " + x.c.short + " in committee."; feed("You raised " + x.c.short + " in committee.", "good"); } }
    else if(k === "2"){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 1, 0, 100); r = x.name + ": “A letter is a start. Put a date on it.”"; }
    else { y.approval = clamp(y.approval - 1, 0, 100); r = x.name + ": “Then who do I ring? I have rung everyone.”"; }
    el("cl_" + i).textContent = r; card.querySelectorAll('[data-cl^="' + i + ':"]').forEach(z => z.disabled = true); }));
  return null;
}
function confirmCard_old(){
  const nom = {name:newName(pick(STATES)), pos:{econ:rint(-60, 60), lib:rint(-60, 60), def:0, wel:0}};
  const fit = alignment(G.you, {pos:nom.pos});
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">Senate Judiciary · confirmation</div><h1>' + nom.name + '</h1>' +
    '<p>Nominated to the bench. ' + (fit > 0 ? "Reads the law much as you do." : "Reads the law the other way from you.") + ' ' + senateColleague() + ' wants a quick vote.</p>' +
    '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="cfYes">Confirm</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" id="cfNo">Make a fight of it</button></div>';
  veil.hidden = false;
  const done = (yes) => {
    const won = yes || chance(0.45);
    if(yes){ G.court = G.court || []; if(G.court.length) G.court[rint(0, G.court.length - 1)] = {name:nom.name, by:"the Senate", pos:nom.pos}; }
    G.you.standing = clamp(G.you.standing + (yes ? 1 : won ? 4 : -3), 0, 100);
    feed(yes ? nom.name + " confirmed to the bench." : (won ? nom.name + "'s nomination was withdrawn after a week of hearings." : nom.name + " confirmed over your objection."), "good");
    walkNow();
  };
  el("cfYes").addEventListener("click", () => done(true));
  el("cfNo").addEventListener("click", () => done(false));
}
function officeCard(){
  G.running = false;
  const y = G.you, k = roleKey(), L = lawEnsure();
  const P = rolePowers();
  const lim = Object.keys(L.limits).map(o => (OFFICES[o] ? OFFICES[o].short : o) + " " + (L.limits[o] ? L.limits[o] + (L.limits[o] === 1 ? " term" : " terms") : "no limit")).join(" · ");
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">Your office · ' + ROLE_T[k] + '</div><h1>' + officeTitle() + '</h1>' +
    '<p class="dream">Term limits in law: ' + lim + '. They change only by amendment.</p>' +
    '<p class="np__matter">' + pcEsc(officeAspect()) + '</p>' +
    P.map((p, i) => '<div class="whip__row"><span class="whip__n">' + p.t + '</span><span class="whip__w">' + (p.d || "") + '</span>' +
      '<span class="whip__b"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost whip__go" data-pow="' + i + '"' + (p.off ? ' disabled' : '') + '>Do it</button></span></div>').join("") +
    (P.length ? '' : '<p>A Representative votes, talks and files. The bigger rooms have bigger levers.</p>') +
    '<div id="powSay" class="dream"></div>' +
    '<div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="powClose">Close</button></div>';
  veil.hidden = false;
  el("powClose").addEventListener("click", () => walkNow());
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-pow]").forEach(bt => bt.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const p = P[+bt.getAttribute("data-pow")]; if(!p || p.off) return;
    spend(20, 4);
    const r = p.run();
    if(r === null) return;
    officeCard();
    const s = el("powSay"); if(s) s.textContent = r || "";
  }));
}

/* today's aims, on the screen where the player is looking, not only in the pause menu */
function paintAims(){
  try{ const box = el("aimsHud"), nx = el("aimsNext"), all = el("aimsAll"); if(!box || !nx) return;
    if(!G.running || !G.you || !veil.hidden){ box.hidden = true; return; }
    if(box._closed === G.day){ box.hidden = true; return; }
    const Gs = goalsEnsure(); if(!Gs || !Gs.list || !Gs.list.length){ box.hidden = true; return; }
    const done = Gs.list.filter(g => g.done).length, next = Gs.list.find(g => !g.done), sig = done + "|" + (next ? next.t + (next.have || 0) : "all") + "|" + Gs.day;
    if(box._sig !== sig){ box._sig = sig; nx.textContent = next ? done + "/" + Gs.list.length + " \u00b7 " + next.t + (next.k === "talk" ? " (" + next.have + "/" + next.need + ")" : "") : "All done today \u2713"; if(all) setHTML(all, goalsHTML()); }
    box.hidden = false; }catch(e){}
}
function paintVoteDock(){
  const d = document.getElementById("voteDock");
  if(d) d.remove();
  const tk = document.getElementById("talk");
  if(tk && !tk._stick){
    tk._stick = true;
    tk.addEventListener("pointerdown", () => { tk._down = true; });
    tk.addEventListener("pointerup", () => { tk._down = false; });
    tk.addEventListener("pointercancel", () => { tk._down = false; });
    tk.addEventListener("pointerleave", () => { tk._down = false; });
  }
  try{ stampScreenClose(); }catch(e){}
}
function stampScreenClose(){
  function stamp(node, fn){
    if(!node || node.hidden || node.querySelector(":scope > .onum-x")) return;
    const b = document.createElement("button");
    b.type = "button";
    b.className = "onum-x";
    b.textContent = "Close";
    b.addEventListener("pointerdown", ev => { try{ ev.stopPropagation(); }catch(x){} });
    b.addEventListener("click", ev => { try{ ev.preventDefault(); ev.stopPropagation(); }catch(x){} fn(); });
    node.insertBefore(b, node.firstChild);
  }
  const pr = el("prompt");
  if(pr && !pr.hidden) stamp(pr, () => {
    promptKey = ""; glassClearHold(); promptActs = [];
    pr.classList.remove("is-live", "is-catch"); pr.hidden = true; pr.innerHTML = "";
  });
  const aims = el("aimsHud");
  if(aims && !aims.hidden) stamp(aims, () => { aims.hidden = true; aims._closed = (G && G.day) || 1; });
  const tip = el("tipCard");
  if(tip && !tip.hidden) stamp(tip, () => { tip.hidden = true; try{ closeTip(); }catch(e){} });
  const toast = document.getElementById("apToast");
  if(toast) stamp(toast, () => { try{ toast.remove(); if(typeof AP !== "undefined" && AP.toast === toast) AP.toast = null; }catch(e){} });
  const cardEl = el("card");
  if(cardEl && veil && !veil.hidden && !cardEl.querySelector(".onum-x") && !/okNight|okElect|sitOut|chClose|lpClose|data-off=|data-post=/.test(cardEl.innerHTML)){
    stamp(cardEl, () => { try{ walkNow(); }catch(e){ veil.hidden = true; G.running = true; } });
  }
}
function paintJob(){
  try{ paintVoteDock(); }catch(e){}
  try{ paintAims(); }catch(e){}
  try{ lifeMorningCheck(); lifeMailCheck(); }catch(e){}
  try{ lTick(); }catch(e){}
  try{ texUpgradeIdle(); }catch(e){}
  const box = el("job"), txt = el("jobText");
  if(!box || !txt) return;
  let line = activeJob();
  try{ const mh = mHintLine(); if(mh) line = mh; }catch(e){}
  try{ line = mPadWords(line); }catch(e){}
  try{
    const od = objectiveDoor();
    if(line && od && !/Sleep\.|Speak\.$/.test(line)){
      line += "  ▸ " + (od.dr.to === od.goal ? ROOMS[od.goal].t : ROOMS[od.dr.to].t + ", then " + ROOMS[od.goal].t);
    }
  }catch(e){}
  if(txt._line === line && box.hidden === !!( !G.running || !line )) return;
  txt._line = line;
  txt.textContent = line;
  box.hidden = !G.running || !line;
  const st = el("scene") && el("scene").parentNode;
  if(st && st.classList){
    if(G.you && G.you.energy < 28) st.classList.add("is-spent");
    else st.classList.remove("is-spent");
  }
}
function paintCompass(){
  const wrap = el("compass");
  const box = el("compassTicks");
  if(!box) return;
  if(wrap) wrap.style.display = (G.running && !TALK.open) ? "" : "none";
  if(!G.running) return;
  const list = hereNow();
  const bits = [];
  const yaw = cam.yaw || 0;
  const half = 50;
  for(let i=0;i<list.length;i++){
    const m = list[i];
    const bear = Math.atan2(m.x - cam.x, m.z - cam.z);
    const rel = wrapPi(bear - yaw);
    if(Math.abs(rel) > 1.25) continue;
    const pct = 50 + (rel / 1.25) * half;
    let cls = "compass__tick";
    if(m.wantsWord) cls += " is-quest";
    else if(TALK.m === m) cls += " is-talk";
    bits.push('<i class="' + cls + '" style="left:' + pct.toFixed(1) + '%" title="' + (m.name || "") + '"></i>');
  }
  /* 20261011b: the door that leads toward the job — pinned to the rail edge when behind you */
  try{
    const od = objectiveDoor();
    if(od){
      const dp = doorAt(G.room, od.dr);
      const relD = wrapPi(Math.atan2(dp.x - cam.x, dp.z - cam.z) - yaw);
      const edge = Math.abs(relD) > 1.25;
      const pctD = edge ? (relD > 0 ? 1 : 99) : 50 + (relD / 1.25) * half;
      bits.push('<i class="compass__tick is-goal' + (edge ? ' is-edge' : '') + '" style="left:' + pctD.toFixed(1) + '%" title="' + ROOMS[od.dr.to].t + '"></i>');
    }
  }catch(e){}
  const html = bits.join("");
  if(box._html === html) return;
  box._html = html;
  box.innerHTML = html;
}
function refreshBar(){
  const you = G.you; if(!you) return;
  say(el("hName"), you.name);
  setHTML(el("hSub"), chipFor(you) +
    "<span>" + (you.out ? officeTitle() : inHouse() ? (you.post ? postTitle(you.post) : "Member of the House") : officeTitle()) + "</span><span>·</span>" +
    (you.out ? "<span>standing again</span>" : inHouse() ? "<span>" + committeeOf(you.committee).t + "</span>" : "<span>" + officeSeat() + "</span>") +
    (inHouse() || you.out ? "<span>·</span><span>" + you.state + " " + you.dist + "</span>" : ""));
  try{ officeTabLabel(); }catch(e){}
  say(el("hDate"), dateString() + " · " + dayLabel());
  say(el("hClock"), hhmm());
  say(el("hCong"), ordinal(G.congress));
  el("hCong").setAttribute("data-tipk", "country");
  el("hCong").setAttribute("data-tipv", "now");
  el("hCong").classList.add("tipword");
  say(el("hSess"), "Sitting day " + G.sittingDay + "/" + G.termLength);
  setHTML(el("hStats"),
    statHTML("Approval", Math.round(you.approval), 100, "var(--good)") +
    statHTML("Influence", Math.round(you.influence), 100, "var(--fed)") +
    statHTML("Standing", Math.round(you.standing), 100, "var(--com)") +
    statHTML("Energy", Math.round(you.energy), 100, you.energy<34?"var(--bad)":"var(--warn)") +
    statHTML("War chest", Math.round(you.funds), 300, "var(--ind)", money(you.funds)) +
    '<div class="stat"><i>Mood</i><b>' + (G.mood>0?"+":"") + Math.round(G.mood) +
      '</b><span class="stat__track"><span class="stat__fill" style="width:'+((G.mood+60)/120*100)+'%;background:var(--ink-3)"></span></span></div>');
  try{ goalsTick(); }catch(e){}
  try{ paintJob(); paintCompass(); }catch(e){}
}
/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   20261011k · THE HIGHER ROOMS
   The Senate, the Court, the Executive wing and the State House are
   real rooms now: walls, floors, furniture, people who work there,
   and a desk that is yours only if the chair is yours.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
const K_ROOM_OF = {senate:"senate", bench:"court", pres:"exec", gov:"govoffice"};
const K_HERE_LINE = {
  senate:"The Senate sits. Your desk is on the aisle. E.",
  court:"The Court is in session. The bench is yours. E.",
  exec:"The wing is waiting on you. The desk. E.",
  govoffice:"The State House is open. Your desk. E."
};
function kChamberRoom(){ try{ return K_ROOM_OF[roleKey()] || null; }catch(e){ return null; } }
function kChamberDone(){ const y = G.you; return !!(y && y.used && y.used.chamber === G.day); }
function kMarkChamber(){ const y = G.you; y.used = y.used || {}; y.used.chamber = G.day; }
function kChamberDue(){
  if(!G.you || G.you.out) return null;
  const r = kChamberRoom(); if(!r || !ROOMS[r]) return null;
  const m = G.minute || 0;
  if(m < 9*60 || m >= 18*60 || kChamberDone()) return null;
  try{ if(dayType() === "recess" && r !== "govoffice") return null; }catch(e){}
  return r;
}
function kHolds(room){ return kChamberRoom() === room; }
function kOnceToday(key){ const y = G.you; y.used = y.used || {}; return y.used[key] === G.day; }
function kMark(key){ const y = G.you; y.used = y.used || {}; y.used[key] = G.day; }

/* ── the people who work in them ─────────────────────────── */
const K_STAFF = {
  senate:   [["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senclerk","Secretary of the Senate","the Senate journal"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"],["senator","Senator","the Senate calendar"]],
  court:    [["justice","Justice","the docket"],["courtclerk","Clerk of the Court","the docket"],["marshal","Marshal of the Court","order in the room"]],
  exec:     [["chief","Chief of Staff","the Executive's day"],["aide","Executive aide","the morning briefing"]],
  govoffice:[["gsec","Governor's secretary","the Governor's calendar"],["gcounsel","Counsel to the Governor","the state's lawsuits"]]
};
function kEnsurePeople(){
  if(!G.civ) G.civ = [];
  let added = false;
  Object.keys(K_STAFF).forEach(room => {
    K_STAFF[room].forEach((spec, i) => {
      const slot = room + ":" + i;
      const have = G.civ.find(c => c && c.kslot === slot);
      if(have){
        /* whoever won the Senate sits in it: the desk follows the election */
        if(spec[0] === "senator"){
          const won = (G.ladder || []).filter(x => x && x.won && x.to === "senate");
          if(i < 2 && won[i] && have.name !== won[i].name){ have.name = won[i].name; have.met = false; }
        }
        return;
      }
      try{
        const c = makeCivilian();
        c.kslot = slot; c.krole = spec[0]; c.role = spec[1]; c.cause = spec[2];
        c.chamber = room; c.room = room; c.caseOpen = false;
        if(spec[0] === "senator"){
          const won = (G.ladder || []).filter(x => x && x.won && x.to === "senate");
          if(i < 2 && won[i]) c.name = won[i].name;
          if(i >= 3){ const ss = (G.states || []).filter(x => x.n !== (G.you && G.you.state)), st = ss[(i * 7 + 3) % Math.max(1, ss.length)]; if(st){ c.state = st.n; try{ c.name = wallSafeMint(() => newName(st.n)); }catch(e){} } c.party = ["FED", "COM"][i % 2]; }
        }
        if(spec[0] === "justice" && G.court && G.court[0]) c.name = G.court[0].name;
        if(room === "govoffice" && G.you && G.you.state){ try{ c.state = G.you.state; }catch(e){} }
        try{ placeInRoom(c); }catch(e){}
        G.civ.push(c); added = true;
      }catch(e){}
    });
  });
  if(added){ _allCache = null; }
}
/* ── person by person: each of the people who work in these rooms is somebody. A name, a manner, a story, a want, a way of putting things, something particular they can do for you, and a day of their own ── */
const K_ARCH = {
  senclerk:[["the stickler","quotes the rule number before the rule"], ["the fixer","knows three ways round every rule"], ["the old hand","remembers what used to happen"]],
  courtclerk:[["the sceptic","thinks every petition is overstated"], ["the champion of the small filer","reads the handwritten ones first"], ["the keeper of the calendar","lives and dies by deadlines"]],
  marshal:[["the bulwark","treats order as a courtesy and enforces it like one"], ["the gossip","knows who was in the building and why"], ["the veteran","served, and has views on everyone who did not"]],
  chief:[["the gatekeeper","decides who gets fifteen minutes"], ["the fixer","settles it before it reaches the desk"], ["the loyalist","speaks for the Executive and means it"]],
  aide:[["the early riser","has read everything twice by seven"], ["the diplomat","phrases every bad thing well"], ["the cynic","has seen this file before"]],
  gsec:[["the keeper of the waiting bench","knows every petitioner's mother"], ["the efficient one","runs the list by the minute"], ["the soft touch","lets the long ones run over"]],
  gcounsel:[["the cautious lawyer","tells you what can go wrong first"], ["the litigator","would rather be sued than wait"], ["the constitutionalist","reads the Charter aloud when nervous"]],
  senator:[["the committee man","trades in markups"], ["the speaker","lives for the floor"], ["the quiet vote","says little and counts everything"]],
  justice:[["the textualist","starts with the words"], ["the pragmatist","asks what happens next"], ["the dissenter","enjoys being the only one"]]
};
const K_STORY = {
  senclerk:["came up as a page at fourteen and never left", "was the clerk who read the roll the night the vote tied", "has outlasted nine majority leaders and keeps the notes"],
  courtclerk:["filed the first petition of a famous case by hand", "once lost a filing in a flood and has never lost one since", "grew up in a house with a law library and no car"],
  marshal:["served in the border guard before this", "was a bailiff in a county court for twenty years", "lost an election once and says it was the best thing that happened"],
  chief:["ran three campaigns before this, and won two", "was a county clerk who got noticed", "has been in the building longer than the Executive has"],
  aide:["wrote the speeches nobody remembers", "reads the cables before the Secretary does", "joined out of university and is still surprised"],
  gsec:["has kept the Governor's door through three administrations", "was a schoolteacher before this", "knows where every county road floods"],
  gcounsel:["litigated for the state before taking the job", "argued a case in front of the bench and lost by one vote", "keeps a copy of the Charter in a coat pocket"],
  senator:["came up through the statehouse", "was a judge before standing", "never planned any of this and is good at it anyway"],
  justice:["was a prosecutor, then a professor, then here", "wrote the dissent people quote", "still reads every brief themselves"]
};
const K_WANT = ["a quiet retirement and a pension that holds", "to see one rule changed before they go", "to be thanked once, in public", "a seat of their own one day", "to be left alone to do the job properly", "to be proved right about something"];
const K_WORK = {
  senclerk:"I keep the journal, the calendar and the rules. When a Senator asks 'is that in order?', I am the answer. It matters to you because a motion that is out of order loses the room before it is heard.",
  courtclerk:"I take the petitions, keep the docket and the deadlines. Who is heard, and when, passes through this desk. It matters to you because a case that is never filed is never decided, and one filed late is filed for nothing.",
  marshal:"I keep order in the Court and in the building around it: who comes in, who stays, who is asked to leave. It matters to you because nobody argues well in a room that does not feel safe.",
  chief:"I run the Executive's day: who sees the Executive, for how long, and with what in their hands. It matters to you because fifteen minutes in this wing can be worth a year of letters.",
  aide:"I read the overnight file and put it in front of the Executive in the order it should be read. It matters to you because what leads the file is what leads the day.",
  gsec:"I keep the Governor's calendar and the list of who comes in on open hours. It matters to you because nobody gets heard who is not on my list, and most people on it have waited weeks.",
  gcounsel:"I advise the Governor on what the state may do and what it may be sued for. It matters to you because a measure that wins at home and loses in the federal court is the worst of both.",
  senator:"I sit, I vote, and I count. It matters to you because the Senate is two votes per state and every one of them has a reason.",
  justice:"I read the briefs, argue it in conference and write or join an opinion. It matters to you because five of us decide what the law means for everyone else."
};
function kMeta(c){
  if(c.kmeta) return c.kmeta; const r = rng(seedOf("km:" + (c.kslot || c.id) + ":" + c.name)), A = K_ARCH[c.krole] || [["steady", "does the job"]], a = A[Math.floor(r() * A.length)], S = K_STORY[c.krole] || ["has been here a while"];
  c.kmeta = {arch:a[0], quirk:a[1], years:3 + Math.floor(r() * 27), story:S[Math.floor(r() * S.length)], want:K_WANT[Math.floor(r() * K_WANT.length)]}; c.rapport = c.rapport || 0; return c.kmeta;
}
function kVoice(c, text){ const m = kMeta(c); const pre = {"the stickler":"Section and subsection, then. ", "the fixer":"Between us: ", "the old hand":"In my time, ", "the sceptic":"Frankly, ", "the bulwark":"Plainly: ", "the gossip":"You did not hear this from me, but ", "the gatekeeper":"Short version: ", "the cynic":"I have seen this one. ", "the diplomat":"If I may put it kindly: ", "the cautious lawyer":"First, what can go wrong: ", "the litigator":"Let them sue. ", "the constitutionalist":"As the Charter has it, ", "the speaker":"Let me say this loudly: ", "the quiet vote":"(low) ", "the dissenter":"I may be the only one, but ", "the pragmatist":"What happens next is "}[m.arch] || ""; return pre + text; }
function kGossip(c){
  const b = G.bill && !G.bill.done ? G.bill : null, rn = (G.reactNews || []).slice(-3), hot = (G.states || []).slice().sort((x, z) => (z.unrest || 0) - (x.unrest || 0))[0], L = [];
  if(rn.length) L.push("The talk is: " + rn[rn.length - 1].t);
  if(b){ try{ const t = tallyBill(b, true); L.push("The " + b.title + " is " + (t.aye > t.no ? "ahead" : "behind") + ", " + t.aye + " to " + t.no + ", and the undecided are not telling anyone."); }catch(e){} }
  if(hot) L.push(hot.n + " is the state everyone is watching: unrest is " + Math.round(hot.unrest || 0) + ".");
  try{ const w = worldEnsure(); L.push("Bread is at " + (w.bread || 1).toFixed(2) + " and " + worldFoe().t + " is the name on every tongue."); }catch(e){}
  if(G.conflict) L.push("There is a measure against " + ((WORLD_POWERS.find(p => p.k === G.conflict.k) || {}).t || "a neighbour") + " under way, and people are taking sides.");
  return L[Math.floor(Math.random() * L.length)] || "Nothing worth repeating.";
}
function kChamberActs(c){
  const you = G.you, b = G.bill, live = b && !b.done, M = kMeta(c), A = [], done = c.kday === G.day, mark = () => { c.kday = G.day; };
  const intro = {t:"Ask about their work", c:"5m", run(){ spend(5, 1); c.met = true; setSay(kVoice(c, K_WORK[c.krole] || "I do my job."), fx("", "you understand what they do")); }};
  const heard = {t:"Ask what they have heard", c:"5m", run(){ spend(5, 1); setSay(kVoice(c, kGossip(c)), ""); }};
  const about = {t:"Ask about them", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); c.met = true; c.rapport = Math.min(4, (c.rapport || 0) + 1); let fam = ""; try{ fam = " " + kinSummary(c); }catch(e){} setSay("I am " + M.arch + ": someone who " + M.quirk + ". " + cap(M.story) + ". " + M.years + " years at it, now, and what I would like is " + M.want + "." + fam, fx("+ rapport", "they tell you something real")); try{ if(c.rel) ripple(c, 2, "They asked about me and listened.", 2, false); }catch(e){} }};
  A.push(intro);
  /* the thing each of them can tell you or do for you */
  if(c.krole === "senclerk"){
    A.push({t:"Ask if a move would be in order", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); c.met = true; setSay(kVoice(c, b ? "On the " + b.title + ": you may hold the floor (it slips the vote three days and costs you six influence), offer a reservation or a compromise before the vote (it moves the middle), or move to table (it needs a majority and loses you the sponsor). Cloture takes three fifths. Anything else is a speech." : "Nothing is before us, so nothing is out of order, which is the best condition the Senate is ever in."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask for the calendar", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); const acts = (G.lastActs || []).slice(0, 3).map(x => x && (x.title || x.t || x)).filter(Boolean); setSay(kVoice(c, acts.length ? "The journal has " + listify(acts) + ". The rest is confirmations and morning business." : "Morning business and a quorum call. A quiet day is a good day here."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask a favour: put your item early on the calendar", c:"15m", off:done, run(){ if((c.rapport || 0) < 1){ setSay(kVoice(c, "Ask me again when we have talked properly. I do not move the calendar for strangers."), ""); return; } spend(15, 2); mark(); you.influence = clamp(you.influence + 2, 0, 100); setSay(kVoice(c, "It is on the list before the morning business. That is all I am doing, and all I will say I did."), fx("+2 influence", "")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "marshal"){
    A.push({t:"Ask how the room feels", c:"5m", run(){ spend(5, 1); let warm = 0, sore = 0, n = 0; try{ hereNow().forEach(p => { if(!p || p === G.you || !p.traits) return; n++; const l = presentOf(p).label; if(/warm|animated|easy|delight/.test(l)) warm++; else if(/cold|closed|short|angry/.test(l)) sore++; }); }catch(e){} setSay(kVoice(c, n ? "Of the " + n + " in here, " + warm + " look easy and " + sore + " look sore; the rest are composed, which is what I would be too." : "Nobody is in but us. It is the best the room ever looks."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask who has been in the building", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); const m = pick((G.members || []).filter(x => x && !x.gone && x.kind === "member")); setSay(kVoice(c, m ? surname(m.name) + " was in before eight, alone, and left with a folder under the arm. I do not ask. I note." : "A quiet morning."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask a favour: a word with someone", c:"15m", off:done, run(){ if((c.rapport || 0) < 1){ setSay(kVoice(c, "I do not arrange meetings for people I have only just met."), ""); return; } spend(15, 2); mark(); const m = pick((G.members || []).filter(x => x && !x.gone && x.kind === "member" && !x.met)); if(m){ m.met = true; try{ if(m.rel) ripple(m, 2, "The Marshal said somebody wanted to meet me. They did.", 2, false); }catch(e){} } setSay(kVoice(c, m ? "I have told " + m.name + " you would welcome a word. They will find you." : "I could not think of anyone you have not met."), fx(m ? "you are introduced" : "", "")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "courtclerk"){
    A.push({t:"Ask about the docket", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); const open = (G.cases || []).filter(x => x && !x.done); setSay(kVoice(c, open.length ? "On the docket: " + listify(open.slice(0, 3).map(x => x.t)) + "." : "Nothing pending. Write a law somebody hates and that will change."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask which petitions are strongest", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); setSay(kVoice(c, "The ones that get four votes are the ones where two courts below have said opposite things about the same words. The ones that do not are the ones where the petitioner is angry and the record is thin. Read the first kind first."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask a favour: an early look at the petitions", c:"15m", off:done, run(){ if((c.rapport || 0) < 1){ setSay(kVoice(c, "The petitions go out when they go out. We have not spoken enough for me to do otherwise."), ""); return; } spend(15, 2); mark(); you.influence = clamp(you.influence + 1, 0, 100); setSay(kVoice(c, "Three are on top of the pile, and the second is the one I would hear. That is all I should say."), fx("+1 influence", "")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "justice"){
    A.push({t:"Ask for their view on the case before the Court", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 2); c.met = true; const cs = benchCase(); if(!cs){ setSay(kVoice(c, "Nothing is ripe. We talk about the long view and the coffee."), ""); return; } const side = justiceLean({name:c.name, pos:c.pos}, cs) > 0, lab = cs.dual != null ? ["for the House", "for the member"] : ["for the Union", "for the state"]; setSay(kVoice(c, justiceWhy({name:c.name, pos:c.pos}, cs, side) + " So I lean " + (side ? lab[0] : lab[1]) + ", for now, and I may be talked out of it."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Share a coffee", c:"15m", off:done, run(){ spend(15, 1); mark(); c.rapport = Math.min(4, (c.rapport || 0) + 1); you.standing = clamp(you.standing + 1, 0, 100); setSay(kVoice(c, "Nobody talks shop over coffee in this building, which is why it is the only place anyone says anything true."), fx("+1 standing", "")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "senator"){
    A.push({t:"Ask where they stand on the bill", c:"10m", off:!live, run(){ spend(10, 2); c.met = true; setSay(kVoice(c, huddleSay(c, false)), fx(kHolds("senate") ? "+1 influence" : "", "")); if(kHolds("senate")) you.influence = clamp(you.influence + 1, 0, 100); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask what they would trade for it", c:"15m", off:done || !live, run(){ spend(15, 3); mark(); setSay(kVoice(c, (alignment(c, b) > 0 ? "I am with you already; I would not trade for something I believe. " : "It would take a change to section four and a vote from you on mine. ") + "That is how it is done."), ""); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "chief"){
    A.push({t:"Ask where the Executive stands", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); const ex = G.exec; setSay(kVoice(c, b && ex && !ex.you ? "On the " + b.title + ", the Executive is " + (alignment(ex, b) > 0 ? "inclined to sign" : alignment(ex, b) < -18 ? "inclined to veto" : "reading it") + ". " + (ex.vetoes || 0) + " vetoes so far this term." : "Nothing before us the Executive has a view on."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask for time with the Executive", c:"30m", off:done || (G.exec && G.exec.you), run(){ if((c.rapport || 0) < 1 && G.exec && G.exec.party !== you.party){ setSay(kVoice(c, "Five minutes in the doorway, and that is generous. Come back when we know each other."), ""); } spend(30, 6); mark(); const same = G.exec && G.exec.party === you.party; you.influence = clamp(you.influence + (same ? 3 : 1), 0, 100); setSay(kVoice(c, same ? "Fifteen minutes, door closed. The Executive asked about your district by name." : "Five minutes in the doorway. Polite, short, and on the record."), fx("+" + (same ? 3 : 1) + " influence", "30 minutes")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "aide"){
    A.push({t:"Ask what the Executive is reading", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); const S = (G.states || []).slice().sort((x, z) => (z.unrest || 0) - (x.unrest || 0))[0]; setSay(kVoice(c, "The morning file leads with " + (S ? S.n + ", where the mood is sour" : "the realms") + (G.exec ? ". " + (G.exec.vetoes || 0) + " vetoes so far this term." : ".")), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask a favour: a copy of the overnight file", c:"15m", off:done, run(){ if((c.rapport || 0) < 1){ setSay(kVoice(c, "It is not mine to copy. Ask me again when I know you."), ""); return; } spend(15, 1); mark(); you.influence = clamp(you.influence + 1, 0, 100); setSay(kVoice(c, "Here. It never left this room, and you did not read it."), fx("+1 influence", "")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "gsec"){
    A.push({t:"Ask who is on today's list", c:"5m", run(){ spend(5, 1); const names = ["a dairy farmer", "a school board chair", "a mayor", "a county clerk", "a widow", "a union steward"].sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5).slice(0, 3); setSay(kVoice(c, "On today's list: " + listify(names) + ". Each has been waiting; none will be short, and one of them will cry."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask the Governor's office for help at home", c:"30m", off:done || kHolds("govoffice"), run(){ spend(30, 5); mark(); you.approval = clamp(you.approval + 2, 0, 100); setSay(kVoice(c, "A road crew, a letter and a ribbon cutting. The State House keeps its promises when they are small."), fx("+2 approval", "30 minutes")); }});
  } else if(c.krole === "gcounsel"){
    A.push({t:"Ask what the state could be sued over", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 2); const S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === (you.state)) || null, foe = worldFoe(); let risk = []; try{ if(S) GOV_ACTS.filter(a => a.fed).forEach(a => { const pl = govWarPlan(a, S, foe.k); risk.push(a.t.toLowerCase() + " (about " + Math.round((1 - pl.fed) * 100) + "% a suit)"); }); }catch(e){} setSay(kVoice(c, risk.length ? "If you act first on the " + foe.t.replace(/^the /, "") + " question, the exposed ones are: " + listify(risk) + ". The state's own business is safe." : "Nothing the state does today is likely to be sued."), ""); }});
    A.push({t:"Ask about the cases pending", c:"10m", run(){ spend(10, 1); const open = (G.cases || []).filter(x => x && !x.done && x.state === you.state); setSay(kVoice(c, open.length ? "Pending against " + you.state + ": " + listify(open.slice(0, 3).map(x => x.t)) + "." : "Nothing pending. Write a law somebody hates and that will change."), ""); }});
  }
  A.push(heard, about);
  if(/^(gcounsel|gsec|chief|senclerk|courtclerk)$/.test(c.krole || "") && kHolds(c.chamber)) A.unshift({t:"Go over the diary", c:"5m", run(){ spend(5, 0); setSay(kVoice(c, "Here is the day as it stands. Tell me what you will take and what you will not."), ""); scheduleCard(); }});
  A.push({t:"Leave them to it", c:"0m", run(){ setSay("You nod and let them get back to " + c.cause + ".", ""); }});
  return A;
}
/* ── the desks: yours if the office is yours ─────────────── */
/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   20261012a · SIT-DOWN SCENES AS PROCEDURE
   The Senate floor, the bench, the morning briefing and the State
   House open hours used to be one click. Now each is a sitting:
   the gavel, openings, rounds of questions, motions, deliberation,
   the vote or ruling, and adjournment, in that order. Lines come in
   on a beat and go to the transcript. Continue hurries a line; it
   never skips a step. What you choose at each step costs or pays in
   standing, influence, approval, the war chest, pledges on the bill
   in play and a rival's heat. Reading the file first helps.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
function sitEsc(s){ return String(s).replace(/&/g, "&"+"amp;").replace(/</g, "&"+"lt;"); }
const SIT = {on:null, timer:0, beat:1500, log:[]};
const SIT_DEF = {
  senate:{title:"The Senate sits", chair:"The Presiding Officer", min:60, en:12, kind:"vote",
    steps:["gavel","open","question","question","motion","deliberate","vote","adjourn"]},
  court:{title:"Oral argument", chair:"The Marshal", min:90, en:14, kind:"ruling",
    steps:["gavel","open","question","question","motion","deliberate","ruling","adjourn"]},
  exec:{title:"The morning briefing", chair:"The Chief of Staff", min:45, en:8, kind:"decision",
    steps:["gavel","open","question","motion","deliberate","ruling","adjourn"]},
  govoffice:{title:"Open hours at the State House", chair:"The Governor's secretary", min:60, en:10, kind:"decision",
    steps:["gavel","open","question","question","motion","deliberate","ruling","adjourn"]}
};
const SIT_STEP_T = {gavel:"Called to order", open:"Openings", question:"Questions", motion:"Motions and objections", deliberate:"Deliberation", vote:"The vote", ruling:"The ruling", adjourn:"Adjourned"};
function sitCast(room){
  let ppl = [];
  try{ ppl = hereNow().filter(m => m && m.name && m !== G.you && !m.machine); }catch(e){}
  const named = ppl.filter(m => m.kind === "member" || m.kslot || m.post);
  const pool = (named.length ? named : ppl).slice(0, 8);
  const nm = i => pool.length ? pool[i % pool.length].name : ["the Senator from the North", "counsel", "the Secretary"][i % 3];
  return {a:nm(0), b:nm(1), c:nm(2), ppl:pool};
}
function sitLines(room, step, C, ctx){
  const y = G.you, bill = G.bill && !G.bill.done ? G.bill : null, bt = bill ? bill.title : "the calendar";
  const cs = (G.cases || []).find(x => x && !x.done);
  const S = {
    senate:{
      gavel:[[ "The Presiding Officer", "The Senate will come to order. The clerk will read the journal."], ["The Clerk", "The journal of the last day stands approved without objection."]],
      open:[[C.a, "The question before us is " + bt + ". I will be brief, which in this room means twenty minutes."], [C.b, "The minority has a view, and the minority would like it on the record."]],
      question:[[C.b, pick(["Will the Senator yield for a question?", "I ask the Senator plainly: who pays for this?", "Has the Senator read section four, or only the summary?"])]],
      motion:[[C.c, pick(["I move to table.", "Point of order: the amendment is not germane.", "I ask unanimous consent to limit debate to one hour."])]],
      deliberate:[["The Presiding Officer", "Without objection, the Senate will stand in quorum call."], [C.a, "Twenty minutes in the cloakroom. Count your votes."]],
      vote:[["The Clerk", "The question is on passage. The clerk will call the roll."]],
      adjourn:[["The Presiding Officer", "The Senate stands adjourned until tomorrow at ten."]]},
    court:{
      gavel:[["The Marshal", "Oyez, oyez, oyez. All persons having business before this Court draw near and give attention."]],
      open:[["Counsel for " + (cs ? cs.state : "the petitioner"), cs ? "This Court should hold that the act reaches past what the Charter allows." : "A narrow question, Your Honor, on filing deadlines."], ["Counsel for the Union", "The act is the law, and the law is clear."]],
      question:[["Counsel for " + (cs ? cs.state : "the petitioner"), pick(["If I may finish the point, Your Honor.", "The record shows otherwise.", "With respect, that is not what the statute says."])]],
      motion:[["Counsel for the Union", pick(["Objection. Counsel is arguing facts not in the record.", "We move to strike that answer.", "We ask leave to file a supplemental brief."])]],
      deliberate:[["The Marshal", "The Court will retire to conference."]],
      ruling:[["The Clerk", "The Court has reached its decision."]],
      adjourn:[["The Marshal", "This honorable Court is now adjourned."]]},
    exec:{
      gavel:[["The Chief of Staff", "Everyone sit. We have forty minutes and the realm has a lot of problems."]],
      open:[[C.a, "The overnight file. Unrest is up in two states and the treasury wants an answer by noon."]],
      question:[[C.b, pick(["The numbers are soft. I would not lean on them.", "My office was not consulted, for the record.", "If you want it done by Friday, I need the authority today."])]],
      motion:[[C.c, pick(["I'd recommend we hold until the vote.", "I object to moving money we have not got.", "Sign it now and explain it later."])]],
      deliberate:[["The Chief of Staff", "Take a minute. Everyone else out of the room."]],
      ruling:[["The Chief of Staff", "Then it is decided."]],
      adjourn:[["The Chief of Staff", "Thank you. Go do it."]]},
    govoffice:{
      gavel:[["The Governor's secretary", "Open hours begin. Five on the list today, please keep it to ten minutes each."]],
      open:[[pick(["A dairy farmer", "A school board chair", "A mayor"]), pick(["The road to the co-op washed out in spring and it is still out.", "We are three teachers short and the state check is late.", "My town cannot pay for the water main the state required."])]],
      question:[[pick(["A widow", "A union steward", "A county clerk"]), pick(["My husband's pension letter came back unopened.", "The plant says it will close if the permit waits another month.", "The ballots for the special election never came."])]],
      motion:[[pick(["The second mayor", "A state senator"]), pick(["With respect, Governor, the first mayor's road is in my county and he never asked me.", "If you move that money, my district loses its clinic."])]],
      deliberate:[["The Governor's secretary", "Shall I clear the room, Governor?"]],
      ruling:[["The Governor's secretary", "I'll write it down as you say it."]],
      adjourn:[["The Governor's secretary", "That is the list. Open hours are closed."]]}
  };
  return ((S[room] || S.senate)[step] || []).slice();
}
/* risk/reward choices per step: [label, risk, good, bad, kind] */
function sitChoices(room, step){
  const C = {
    open:[["Open steady and on the record", 0.05, {standing:1}, {}, "safe"],
          ["Open bold, name names", 0.40, {standing:3, influence:1}, {standing:-2, heat:6}, "bold"],
          ["Cite the file chapter and verse", 0.15, {standing:2, approval:1}, {standing:-1}, "prep"]],
    question:[["Ask one fair question", 0.10, {standing:1}, {}, "safe"],
              ["Press hard until they give", 0.45, {influence:2, standing:1, heat:-4}, {standing:-2, heat:8}, "bold"],
              ["Let it pass to save time", 0.0, {}, {standing:-1}, "rush"]],
    motion:[["Rule it in order and move on", 0.10, {standing:1}, {}, "safe"],
            ["Object and make them argue it", 0.35, {influence:2}, {standing:-1, influence:-1}, "bold"],
            ["Offer a deal on the side", 0.30, {pledge:2, funds:-2}, {funds:-2, standing:-1}, "deal"]],
    deliberate:[["Take the full time to work it", 0.10, {support:3, pledge:1}, {}, "safe"],
                ["Spend from the war chest for votes", 0.25, {pledge:3, support:4, funds:-4}, {funds:-4}, "deal"],
                ["Cut it short", 0.0, {}, {standing:-2, support:-2}, "rush"]],
    vote:[["Aye — and say why", 0.10, {standing:1, approval:1, vote:1}, {}, "safe"],
          ["No — and say why", 0.10, {standing:1, vote:-1}, {}, "safe"],
          ["Present. I am in the room and I am not voting", 0.05, {vote:0}, {standing:-1}, "safe"],
          ["Speak last and swing it", 0.40, {influence:3, support:4}, {standing:-2}, "bold"]],
    ruling:[["Aye. Decide it and own it", 0.15, {standing:2, approval:1, vote:1}, {}, "safe"],
            ["No. Send it back", 0.15, {standing:1, vote:-1}, {approval:-1}, "safe"],
            ["Decide narrowly", 0.10, {standing:1}, {}, "safe"],
            ["Decide broadly and own it", 0.40, {standing:3, approval:2}, {standing:-2, approval:-2}, "bold"]]
  };
  return C[step] || null;
}
function sitApply(d, sign){
  const y = G.you, out = [];
  if(!d) return "";
  const add = (k, v, lab) => { if(!v) return; y[k] = clamp((y[k] || 0) + v, 0, 100); out.push((v > 0 ? "+" : "") + v + " " + lab); };
  add("standing", d.standing, "standing"); add("influence", d.influence, "influence"); add("approval", d.approval, "approval");
  if(d.funds){ y.funds = Math.max(0, (y.funds || 0) + d.funds); out.push((d.funds > 0 ? "+" : "") + d.funds + " war chest"); }
  if(d.vote === 1 || d.vote === -1 || d.vote === 0){
    y.vote = d.vote;
    try{ if(d.vote) taylorDayVoteDefiance(d.vote); }catch(e){}
    out.push(d.vote > 0 ? "you are aye" : d.vote < 0 ? "you are no" : "you are present");
  }
  if(d.heat){ const r = rivalLive(); if(r){ r.heat = clamp((r.heat || 0) + d.heat, 0, 100); out.push("rival heat " + (d.heat > 0 ? "+" : "") + d.heat); } }
  if(d.support && G.bill && !G.bill.done){ G.bill.sitSupport = (G.bill.sitSupport || 0) + d.support; out.push((d.support > 0 ? "+" : "") + d.support + " bill support"); }
  if(d.pledge && G.bill && !G.bill.done){
    const C = (G.members || []).filter(m => m && !m.gone && m.kind === "member" && !m.machine && !m.pledge).sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5).slice(0, d.pledge);
    C.forEach(m => { m.pledge = 1; m.pledgeDay = G.day; });
    if(C.length) out.push(C.length + " pledged");
  }
  return out.join(" · ");
}
function sitStart(room){
  const D = SIT_DEF[room]; if(!D) return;
  try{ if(TALK.open) closeTalk(); }catch(e){}
  const y = G.you;
  G.sitPrep = G.sitPrep || {};
  const prep = G.sitPrep[room] === G.day;
  SIT.on = {room, D, i:0, li:0, lines:[], cast:sitCast(room), score:0, rush:0, prep, t0:performance.now(), m0:G.minute || 0, tally:[], picked:false};
  try{ kMark({senate:"ksen", court:"kct", exec:"kex", govoffice:"kgv"}[room]); kMarkChamber(); }catch(e){}
  G.running = false;
  sitStep();
}
function sitStep(){
  const S = SIT.on; if(!S) return;
  const step = S.D.steps[S.i];
  S.lines = sitLines(S.room, step, S.cast); S.li = 0; S.picked = false; S.res = "";
  spend(Math.round(S.D.min / S.D.steps.length), Math.round(S.D.en / S.D.steps.length));
  sitDraw(); sitBeat();
}
function sitBeat(){
  const S = SIT.on; if(!S) return;
  clearTimeout(SIT.timer);
  if(S.li < S.lines.length){
    const L = S.lines[S.li++];
    try{ tlog(L[0], L[1], "sit"); }catch(e){}
    sitDraw();
    SIT.timer = setTimeout(sitBeat, SIT.beat);
  } else sitDraw();
}
function sitPick(ci){
  const S = SIT.on; if(!S || S.picked) return;
  const step = S.D.steps[S.i], ch = sitChoices(S.room, step); if(!ch || !ch[ci]) return;
  const c = ch[ci];
  let p = 1 - c[1] + (S.prep ? 0.15 : 0) + ((G.you.standing || 50) - 50) / 250 - S.rush * 0.08;
  if(c[4] === "prep" && !S.prep) p -= 0.45;
  if(c[4] === "deal" && (G.you.funds || 0) < 4) p -= 0.5;
  const ok = Math.random() < p;
  if(c[4] === "rush"){ S.rush++; }
  const r = sitApply(ok ? c[2] : c[3]);
  S.score += ok ? (c[4] === "bold" ? 2 : 1) : -1;
  S.tally.push({step, pick:c[0], ok, r});
  try{ tlog("You", c[0] + ".", "you"); }catch(e){}
  const answer = ok ? pick(["That lands.", "Heads nod down the row.", "Nobody has an answer to that.", "Fair enough."])
                    : pick(["It goes over badly.", "Someone laughs, not kindly.", "The room cools.", "That was thin, and they noticed."]);
  try{ tlog(S.cast.b || "", answer, "sit"); }catch(e){}
  S.res = answer + (r ? " (" + r + ")" : "");
  S.picked = true;
  sitDraw();
}
function sitNext(){
  const S = SIT.on; if(!S) return;
  if(S.li < S.lines.length){ sitBeat(); return; }          /* hurry the line, never the step */
  const step = S.D.steps[S.i];
  if(sitChoices(S.room, step) && !S.picked) return;
  if(step === "vote" || step === "ruling") sitOutcome();
  S.i++;
  if(S.i >= S.D.steps.length){ sitEnd(false); return; }
  sitStep();
}
function sitOutcome(){
  const S = SIT.on, y = G.you;
  const good = S.score >= 2 && S.rush === 0;
  const res = sitApply(good ? {standing:2, influence:1, approval:S.room === "govoffice" ? 3 : 0} : S.score < 0 ? {standing:-2} : {standing:1});
  if(S.room === "exec" || S.room === "govoffice"){
    try{ const st = S.room === "exec" ? (G.states || []).slice().sort((a, b) => (b.unrest || 0) - (a.unrest || 0))[0] : (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === y.state);
      if(st) st.unrest = clamp((st.unrest || 0) - (good ? 3 : 1), 0, 100); }catch(e){}
  }
  S.out = (good ? "A clean sitting." : S.score < 0 ? "A rough sitting." : "A middling sitting.") + (res ? " " + res : "");
  try{ tlog(S.D.chair, S.out, "sit"); }catch(e){}
  if(good && S.prep){ try{ achieve("sitting"); }catch(e){} }
}
function sitEnd(walked){
  const S = SIT.on; if(!S) return;
  clearTimeout(SIT.timer);
  if(walked){ sitApply({standing:-3, influence:-1}); try{ tlog("", "You walked out of the sitting.", "sit"); }catch(e){} }
  SIT.log.push({room:S.room, ms:Math.round(performance.now() - S.t0), gameMin:(G.minute || 0) - S.m0, steps:S.i, walked:!!walked, score:S.score});
  try{ note((walked ? "Walked out of " : "Sat through ") + S.D.title.toLowerCase() + "."); }catch(e){}
  SIT.on = null;
  walkNow();
}
function sitDraw(){
  const S = SIT.on; if(!S) return;
  const step = S.D.steps[S.i], ch = sitChoices(S.room, step);
  const done = S.li >= S.lines.length;
  const lines = S.lines.slice(0, S.li).map(l => '<p class="sit__l"><b>' + sitEsc(l[0]) + '</b> ' + sitEsc(l[1]) + '</p>').join("");
  const prog = S.D.steps.map((s, i) => '<span class="sit__dot' + (i < S.i ? ' is-done' : i === S.i ? ' is-now' : '') + '">' + SIT_STEP_T[s] + '</span>').join("");
  let acts = "";
  if(done && ch && !S.picked) acts = ch.map((c, i) => '<button type="button" class="btn' + (i ? ' btn--ghost' : '') + '" data-sit="' + i + '">' + c[0] + (c[4] === "rush" ? ' <small>(rushes it)</small>' : c[1] >= 0.3 ? ' <small>(risky)</small>' : '') + '</button>').join("");
  else acts = '<button type="button" class="btn" id="sitGo">' + (done ? (S.i === S.D.steps.length - 1 ? "Rise" : "Next step") : "Continue") + '</button>';
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">' + S.D.title + ' · step ' + (S.i + 1) + ' of ' + S.D.steps.length + (S.prep ? ' · you read the file' : '') + '</div>' +
    '<h1>' + SIT_STEP_T[step] + '</h1><div class="sit__prog">' + prog + '</div>' +
    '<div class="sit__lines">' + lines + '</div>' + (S.res ? '<p class="dream">' + S.res + '</p>' : '') + (S.out && step !== "adjourn" ? '' : (S.out && step === "adjourn" ? '<p class="dream">' + S.out + '</p>' : '')) +
    '<div class="card__actions">' + acts + '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" id="sitOut">Walk out</button></div>';
  veil.hidden = false;
  const g = el("sitGo"); if(g) g.addEventListener("click", sitNext);
  el("sitOut").addEventListener("click", () => sitEnd(true));
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-sit]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => sitPick(+b.getAttribute("data-sit"))));
  try{ refreshPicks(); }catch(e){}
}
function sitPrepAct(room){
  return {t:"Read the file before you sit", c:"20m", off:(G.sitPrep || {})[room] === G.day, run(){
    spend(20, 2); G.sitPrep = G.sitPrep || {}; G.sitPrep[room] = G.day;
    setSay("You read it twice and mark the pages. Tomorrow's surprises will be today's notes.", fx("prepared for the sitting", "20 minutes"));
  }};
}
(function(){
  try{ if(!ACH.some(a => a.k === "sitting")) ACH.push({k:"sitting", t:"Order of the Day", d:"Prepared for a sitting and ran it clean."}); }catch(e){}
  try{
    const st = document.createElement("style");
    st.textContent = ".sit__prog{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;margin:6px 0 10px}.sit__dot{font-size:11px;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);opacity:.6}" +
      ".sit__dot.is-done{opacity:.9;background:rgba(150,120,60,.18)}.sit__dot.is-now{opacity:1;background:rgba(150,120,60,.45);font-weight:600}" +
      ".sit__lines{max-height:38vh;overflow:auto}.sit__l{margin:4px 0}";
    document.head.appendChild(st);
  }catch(e){}
})();

function kDeskActs(room){
  const you = G.you, mine = kHolds(room), A = [];
  if(mine) A.push({t:"Use the powers of your office", c:"opens your office", run(){ kMarkChamber(); officeCard(); }});
  if(room === "senate"){
    if(mine) A.push(sitPrepAct("senate"));
    if(mine) A.push({t:"Sit the Senate: take the floor", c:"60m · step by step", off:kOnceToday("ksen"), run(){ sitStart("senate"); return null; }});
    else A.push({t:"Watch from the gallery rail", c:"20m", run(){
      spend(20, 2);
      setSay("Six desks occupied, one Senator talking, a clerk reading the journal under her breath. It is slower than the House and nobody here minds.", "");
    }});
  } else if(room === "court"){
    if(mine) A.push(sitPrepAct("court"));
    if(mine) A.push({t:"Hear oral argument", c:"90m · step by step", off:kOnceToday("kct"), run(){ sitStart("court"); return null; }});
    else A.push({t:"Sit in the public seats", c:"30m", run(){
      spend(30, 3);
      const c = (G.cases || []).find(x => x && !x.done);
      setSay(c ? "They are hearing " + c.t + ". The questions from the bench tell you more than the briefs did."
               : "A slow morning in the Court. You learn that the marshal knows every lawyer by their shoes.", "");
    }});
  } else if(room === "exec"){
    if(mine) A.push(sitPrepAct("exec"));
    if(mine) A.push({t:"Take the morning briefing", c:"45m · step by step", off:kOnceToday("kex"), run(){ sitStart("exec"); return null; }});
    else A.push({t:"Leave a letter for the Executive", c:"15m", off:kOnceToday("kexl"), run(){
      spend(15, 2); kMark("kexl");
      setSay("The aide takes it with both hands and promises it will be read. It might even be true.", "");
    }});
  } else if(room === "govoffice"){
    if(mine) A.push(sitPrepAct("govoffice"));
    if(mine) A.push({t:"Hold open hours at the State House", c:"60m · step by step", off:kOnceToday("kgv"), run(){ sitStart("govoffice"); return null; }});
    else A.push({t:"Petition the Governor for the district", c:"30m", off:kOnceToday("kgvp"), run(){
      spend(30, 4); kMark("kgvp");
      you.approval = clamp(you.approval + 1, 0, 100);
      setSay("The secretary writes it all down and reads it back to you. That is more than most offices do.", fx("+1 approval", "30 minutes"));
    }});
  }
  return A;
}
PROPS.senate = [{id:"ksdesk", label:"The Senate desks", sub:"Old mahogany, names carved inside the drawers", x:0, z:6.0, r:2.3,
  acts:() => kDeskActs("senate")}];
PROPS.court = [{id:"kbench", label:"The bench", sub:"Nine feet of oak and a long view", x:0, z:7.6, r:2.4,
  acts:() => kDeskActs("court")}];
PROPS.exec = [{id:"kxdesk", label:"The Executive's desk", sub:"Built from the timbers of a ship nobody remembers", x:0, z:8.7, r:2.3,
  acts:() => kDeskActs("exec")}];
PROPS.govoffice = [{id:"kgdesk", label:"The Governor's desk", sub:"A state map under the glass", x:0, z:7.9, r:2.3,
  acts:() => kDeskActs("govoffice")}];

/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   20261012g · ONE CHAIR AT A TIME
   An elected office you win is the job you do. A Governor is not a
   Member of the House: no House vote, no House post, no Cannon office.
   The title is the most senior elected one; appointed work (staff,
   envoy) never outranks it. Each chair keeps its own working day, as
   the real one does, and its own office is where you wake up.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
const OFFICE_RANK = ["pres", "senate", "bench", "gov", "house"];
function heldOffice(){ const y = G.you; if(!y || y.out) return null; return y.office || "house"; }
function inHouse(){ return heldOffice() === "house"; }
function abroadOffice(){ const k = heldOffice(); return !!k && k !== "house"; }
function officeShort(k){
  if(k === "pres"){ try{ return execTitle(); }catch(e){} }
  return (OFFICES[k] || OFFICES.house).short;
}
function officeSeat(){
  const y = G.you, k = heldOffice();
  if(k === "gov") return "Governor of " + y.state;
  if(k === "senate") return "Senator from " + y.state;
  if(k === "bench") return "the high bench";
  if(k === "pres") return "the Union";
  return y.state + " " + y.dist;
}
const K_HOME_OF = {pres:"exec", gov:"govoffice"};
function homeRoom(){ const k = heldOffice(); return (k && K_HOME_OF[k]) || "office"; }
function inMyWorkRoom(){ try{ return G.room === homeRoom() || G.room === kChamberRoom(); }catch(e){ return false; } }
/* what people call you to your face: the chair you hold, or the highest you held */
function youAddress(){
  const y = G.you; if(!y) return "Representative";
  const k = heldOffice() || OFFICE_RANK.find(o => o !== "house" && officeTermsOf(o) > 0) || "house";
  if(k === "house"){
    if(!y.out && y.post === "speaker") return "Speaker";
    if(!y.out && y.post && /^(ways|judic|armed)$/.test(y.post)) return "Chairman";
    return "Representative";
  }
  return officeShort(k);
}
function seniorElected(){
  const y = G.you; if(!y) return null;
  const held = heldOffice();
  if(held) return held;
  return OFFICE_RANK.find(k => k !== "house" && officeTermsOf(k) > 0) || ((y.terms || 0) > 0 ? "house" : null);
}

/* ── the working day of each chair ───────────────────────── */
function docketFor(k){
  const y = G.you;
  const S = (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === y.state);
  const D = {
    gov:[
      {h:8,  key:"gbrief", t:"Morning briefing", d:"Your secretary reads the state: roads, prisons, the treasury, the weather.", run:() => govBrief2(S)},
      {h:10, key:"kgv",    t:"Open hours at the State House", d:"Citizens, mayors and county clerks, one at a time.", sit:"govoffice"},
      {h:12, key:"gwar",   t:"The bread question", d:"A neighbour holds the grain. What the state may do itself, what it needs the Union's consent for, and who answers.", run:() => { kMark("gwar"); govWarCard(); return null; }},
      {h:13, key:"gdesk",  t:"The statehouse desk", d:S && S.bill ? "On your desk: the " + S.bill.title + ". Sign it or veto it." : "Bills sent over from the legislature.", run:() => govDesk(S)},
      {h:15, key:"gbud",   t:"Agencies and the budget", d:"One department gets the money this week.", run:() => govBudget2(S)},
      {h:17, key:"gpress", t:"Press availability", d:"The capitol reporters, on the record.", run:() => officePress("the State House steps")}
    ],
    senate:[
      {h:13, key:"swar",   t:"The situation abroad", d:"The Reach holds the bread. Authorise, restrain, hold hearings or pass sanctions: the Senate's own levers.", run:() => { kMark("swar"); legWarCard(); return null; }},
      {h:8,  key:"sbrief", t:"Staff meeting", d:"Your chief of staff, legislative director and state director, in their own words.", run:() => senBrief()},
      {h:9,  key:"conf",   t:"Committee: a confirmation hearing", d:"A nominee for the bench, under oath. Question them, then decide.", run:() => { kMark("conf"); confirmCard(); return null; }},
      {h:11, key:"ksen",   t:"The Senate sits", d:"The journal, the question, the roll.", sit:"senate"},
      {h:14, key:"treaty", t:"Treaties and foreign business", d:"A treaty with a neighbour: read the terms, hear both sides, then advise and consent.", run:() => { kMark("treaty"); treatyCard(); return null; }},
      {h:16, key:"scalls", t:"Calls from " + y.state, d:"Three constituents with real problems; what you promise is remembered.", run:() => senCalls()}
    ],
    bench:[
      {h:9,  key:"bconf",  t:"Conference with the other justices", d:"The case, argued in private: four justices in their own words, and your clerks.", run:() => benchConf2()},
      {h:10, key:"kct",    t:"Oral argument", d:"Counsel for each side, and your questions.", sit:"court"},
      {h:13, key:"bcert",  t:"Petitions for review", d:"Choose which cases the Court will hear.", run:() => benchCert()},
      {h:14, key:"bopin",  t:"Write the opinion", d:"Pick your side and how far to write; three votes make it the Court's.", run:() => benchOpinion()}
    ],
    pres:[
      {h:8,  key:"kex",    t:"The morning briefing", d:"The overnight file: states, realms, the treasury.", sit:"exec"},
      {h:9,  key:"pwar",   t:"The situation room", d:"A neighbour holds the bread. Sanctions, convoys, a blockade, war: as far as the law lets you, and with Congress if it does not.", run:() => { kMark("pwar"); warCard(); return null; }},
      {h:11, key:"pacts",  t:"Acts awaiting signature", d:"Sign or veto what the House and Senate send.", run:() => presActs()},
      {h:14, key:"cab",    t:"Cabinet", d:"Appoint, or hear the secretaries out.", power:"Appoint a cabinet secretary"},
      {h:16, key:"aid",    t:"Calls with foreign capitals", d:"Three heads of government on the line, in their own words. Aid, trade or a warning.", run:() => presForeign()},
      {h:17, key:"ppress", t:"The press room", d:"Questions from the whole Union.", run:() => officePress("the Executive's press room")}
    ]
  };
  return D[k] || [];
}
function docketToday(){ const k = heldOffice(); return k && k !== "house" ? docketFor(k) : []; }
function docketDone(){ return docketToday().filter(d => kOnceToday(d.key)).length; }
function docketNext(){
  const m = G.minute || 0;
  if(m >= 19*60) return null;
  return docketToday().find(d => !kOnceToday(d.key) && m >= d.h*60 - 60) || null;
}
const DK_ROOM = {conf:"committee", treaty:"senate", swar:"senate", sbrief:"office", scalls:"office", bconf:"court", bcert:"court", bopin:"office", pwar:"exec", cab:"exec", aid:"exec", pacts:"exec", gbrief:"govoffice", gwar:"govoffice", gdesk:"govoffice", gbud:"govoffice"};
function docketAfter(d, want){ let n = 0; const t = setInterval(() => { n++; if(G.room === want && !G.moving && G.running !== false){ clearInterval(t); try{ docketRun(d); }catch(e){} } else if(n > 16) clearInterval(t); }, 500); }
function docketRun(d, here){
  if(!d || kOnceToday(d.key)) return;
  if(!here){ const sr = d.sit ? String(d.sit).split(":")[0] : null, chamber = sr && ["senate", "court", "committee", "caucus", "floor"].indexOf(sr) >= 0 ? sr : null, want = chamber || DK_ROOM[d.key] || null;
    if(want){ if(G.room !== want){ goTo(want); try{ feed("You walk to " + (ROOMS[want] ? ROOMS[want].t : want) + " for " + d.t.toLowerCase() + "."); }catch(e){} docketAfter(d, want); return; } }
    else if(G.room !== homeRoom() && !inMyWorkRoom()){ goTo(homeRoom()); docketAfter(d, homeRoom()); return; } }
  if(d.sit){ sitStart(d.sit); return; }
  if(d.power){
    const p = rolePowers().find(x => x.t.indexOf(d.power) === 0);
    if(!p || p.off){ kMark(d.key); note("Nothing for " + d.t.toLowerCase() + " today."); refreshPanels(); return; }
    spend(20, 4);
    const r = p.run(); kMark(d.key);
    if(r) note(r, true);
    refreshPanels(); return;
  }
  const r = d.run ? d.run() : "";
  if(r === null) return;
  kMark(d.key);
  if(r) note(r, true);
  refreshPanels();
}
/* ── the governor's staff, agency heads and appointees: real people with views, not a click ── */
const GOV_ROLES = {
  chief:{t:"Chief of staff", ax:"lib"}, treasurer:{t:"State treasurer", ax:"econ"}, safety:{t:"Commissioner of public safety", ax:"lib"}, press:{t:"Press secretary", ax:"wel"}
};
const GOV_AGENCIES = {
  roads:{t:"Roads and bridges", head:"Director of public works", ax:"econ", effect:[-1, 3, 1], ask:[14, 30], why:"the bottom road, the bridge on the river road, and the culverts nobody has inspected"},
  schools:{t:"Schools", head:"Superintendent of schools", ax:"wel", effect:[-3, 1, 2], ask:[12, 26], why:"three teachers where the state cheque was late, and a roof that is not a roof"},
  police:{t:"The constabulary", head:"Chief of the state constabulary", ax:"lib", effect:[-4, 0, -1], ask:[10, 24], why:"men on the corners, a second radio net, and the overtime nobody budgeted"},
  health:{t:"Hospitals and the poor", head:"Commissioner of health", ax:"wel", effect:[-2, -1, 3], ask:[12, 28], why:"the maternity floor, the county hospitals' arrears, and the poor-relief rolls"}
};
function mkOfficial(key, S, roleTitle){
  const r = rng(seedOf("off:" + key + ":" + ((G.you && G.you.name) || "")));
  const bg = BACKGROUNDS[Math.floor(r() * BACKGROUNDS.length)], cr = CREEDS[Math.floor(r() * CREEDS.length)], og = ORIGINS[Math.floor(r() * ORIGINS.length)];
  const pos = {}; AXES.forEach(a => { pos[a.k] = clamp(Math.round((bg.pos[a.k] || 0) + (cr.pos[a.k] || 0) * 0.5 + (og.pos[a.k] || 0) * 0.5 + (r() - 0.5) * 36), -100, 100); });
  let name = ""; try{ name = wallSafeMint(() => newName(S ? S.n : null)); }catch(e){}
  if(!name) name = "A. Official";
  return {name, role:roleTitle, bg:bg.t, creed:cr.k, origin:og.k, pos, temper:Math.round(25 + r() * 60), warm:0, since:G.day};
}
function govStaff(S){
  if(!S) return {};
  S.cab = S.cab || {}; S.agency = S.agency || {};
  Object.keys(GOV_ROLES).forEach(k => { if(!S.cab[k]) S.cab[k] = mkOfficial("cab:" + k + ":" + S.n, S, GOV_ROLES[k].t); });
  Object.keys(GOV_AGENCIES).forEach(k => { if(!S.agency[k]) S.agency[k] = mkOfficial("ag:" + k + ":" + S.n, S, GOV_AGENCIES[k].head); });
  return S;
}
function viewWords(pos){
  const top = AXES.map(a => ({a, v:pos[a.k] || 0})).filter(x => Math.abs(x.v) >= 14).sort((x, y) => Math.abs(y.v) - Math.abs(x.v)).slice(0, 2);
  if(!top.length) return "has no strong line on anything, which is itself a position";
  return "leans " + top.map(x => (x.v > 0 ? x.a.hi : x.a.lo)).join(" and ") + (Math.abs(top[0].v) > 45 ? ", firmly" : "");
}
function officialHTML(o, extra){
  const cr = creedOf(o.creed);
  return '<b>' + pcEsc(o.name) + '</b> <span class="muted">· ' + pcEsc(o.role) + '</span><div class="muted" style="font-size:12px">' + pcEsc(cap(o.bg)) + ', of ' + pcEsc(cr.t) + '. ' + pcEsc(cap(viewWords(o.pos))) + '.' + (extra ? " " + extra : "") + '</div>';
}
function govCardOpen(eyebrow, title, intro, body, closeKey){
  /* drawing the same card again (after pressing something on it) keeps your place, and whatever it says in reply is scrolled into view */
  const keepTop = (!veil.hidden && card.getAttribute("data-gcT") === title) ? [veil.scrollTop, card.scrollTop] : null;
  G.running = false;
  card.innerHTML = '<div class="eyebrow">' + pcEsc(eyebrow) + '</div><h1>' + pcEsc(title) + '</h1>' + (intro ? '<p class="dream">' + pcEsc(intro) + '</p>' : '') + body +
    '<div id="gcSay" class="dream"></div><div class="card__actions"><button type="button" class="btn" id="gcClose">Close</button></div>';
  veil.hidden = false; card.setAttribute("data-gcT", title);
  if(keepTop){ veil.scrollTop = keepTop[0]; card.scrollTop = keepTop[1]; }
  try{ const gs = el("gcSay"); if(gs && window.MutationObserver) new MutationObserver(() => { try{ gs.scrollIntoView({block:"nearest"}); }catch(e){} }).observe(gs, {childList:true, characterData:true, subtree:true}); }catch(e){}
  el("gcClose").addEventListener("click", () => { if(closeKey){ try{ kMark(closeKey); }catch(e){} } walkNow(); try{ refreshPanels(); }catch(e){} });
}
function advisorLine(o, S, topic){
  const p = o.pos, tilt = a => p[a] || 0;
  const hot = (S.unrest || 0) > 55, calm = (S.unrest || 0) < 30, ind = Math.round(S.ind || 0);
  const towns = (function(){ try{ return (townsOf(S.n) || []).map(t => t.name); }catch(e){ return []; } })();
  const town = towns.length ? towns[Math.floor(seedOf("t:" + o.name + G.day) % towns.length)] : "the county seat";
  if(topic === "chief"){
    const b = S.bill, dir = b ? b.dir * (b.axis === "econ" ? 1 : 1) : 0;
    const bl = b ? "The legislature has sent over the " + b.title + ". " + (tilt(b.axis || "econ") * dir > 12 ? "I would sign it: it is where I stand, and where most of the majority stands." : tilt(b.axis || "econ") * dir < -12 ? "I would not sign it; it cuts against what I believe, and I would rather tell you than pretend." : "I can argue it either way, so I will let you hear the arguments first.") : "Nothing has come over from the legislature, which gives us a clear desk.";
    return "Morning, " + youAddress() + ". " + bl + " Your approval is at " + Math.round(G.you.approval) + ". " + (G.you.approval < 45 ? "That is low enough that I would take a public question today." : "That is comfortable, so do not spend it on anything small.");
  }
  if(topic === "treasurer"){
    const avail = govAvail(S);
    const lean = tilt("econ") > 20 ? "I would rather leave it in the private economy: bank some, cut a levy next session, and let the contractors bid." : tilt("econ") < -20 ? "I would spend it where the counties can see it, on works the state owns, and keep the contractors honest." : tilt("wel") > 20 ? "I would keep a reserve for hardship before anything else." : "I would rather not tell you what to do with it before you have heard the departments.";
    return "The state has " + curF(avail) + " unallocated this week. Industry stands at " + ind + ". " + lean;
  }
  if(topic === "safety"){
    const lean = tilt("lib") < -20 ? "I want the constables visible, and I want curfews in " + town + " considered before somebody is hurt." : tilt("lib") > 20 ? "I would stand the patrols down in " + town + " and let the mayor and the clergy keep the peace; a constable on every corner makes a crowd." : "I will watch " + town + " and tell you the moment it changes.";
    return (hot ? "Unrest is high: crowds outside two county courthouses, and " + town + " is the worst of it. " : calm ? "The counties are quiet. " : "The counties are restless, not yet angry. ") + lean;
  }
  const t = G.world && G.world.foe ? (WORLD_POWERS.find(x => x.k === G.world.foe) || {}).t : null;
  return "The Standard is running the day your way and the Courier is asking who pays. " + (t ? "The wire says " + t + " is the story abroad, and a reporter will ask you about it." : "Nothing abroad to ask about.") + " " + (tilt("wel") > 20 ? "I would answer any question about the poor first. People believe that of you." : tilt("wel") < -20 ? "I would answer any question about the budget first. The papers will not forgive vagueness." : "Whatever you decide to say, say it once, plainly.");
}
function govAvail(S){ return Math.round((18 + (S.ind || 50) * 0.28 + (seedOf("av:" + S.n + ":" + G.day) % 10)) ) * 1000; }
function govBrief2(S){
  if(!S){ return "The secretary reads the day's file. Nothing in it is on fire."; }
  govStaff(S);
  const y = G.you, did = {};
  const adv = ["chief", "treasurer", "safety", "press"].map(k => ({k, o:S.cab[k], line:advisorLine(S.cab[k], S, k)}));
  const acts = {
    chief:[{t:"Take the public question", d:"Approval, if it lands", run(){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + (chance(0.6) ? 2 : -1), 0, 100); return "You take a question on the steps and the Courier gets its answer."; }}, {t:"Keep a clear desk", d:"Nothing spent", run(){ return "You keep the day clear and the papers wait."; }}],
    treasurer:[{t:"Bank part of it", d:"Industry steady, hardship waits", run(){ S.ind = clamp(S.ind + 1, 0, 100); return "A quarter goes into the reserve."; }}, {t:"Release it to the counties", d:"Unrest down, treasury thinner", run(){ S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest - 2, 0, 100); return "The counties are told the cheques are coming."; }}],
    safety:[{t:"More patrols", d:"Order now, resentment later", run(){ S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest - 3, 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval - 1, 0, 100); return "Constables on the corners of the worst streets."; }}, {t:"Stand the patrols down", d:"Quieter streets, louder papers", run(){ S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + (chance(0.5) ? 2 : -2), 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 1, 0, 100); return "The patrols come off; the mayors are asked to keep the peace."; }}],
    press:[{t:"Lead with the poor", d:"Approval at home", run(){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + 2, 0, 100); return "You lead with the maternity floor and the Courier prints it."; }}, {t:"Lead with the budget", d:"Standing with the Standard", run(){ y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); return "You lead with the balance sheet."; }}]
  };
  const body = adv.map(a => '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)">' + officialHTML(a.o) + '<p style="margin:6px 0">“' + pcEsc(a.line) + '”</p>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap">' + acts[a.k].map((x, j) => '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-adv="' + a.k + ':' + j + '" title="' + pcEsc(x.d) + '">' + pcEsc(x.t) + '</button>').join("") +
    '<button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-why="' + a.k + '">Ask why</button></div><div class="dream" id="adv_' + a.k + '"></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("Morning briefing · " + (y.state || ""), "Your advisors, in their own words", "Each of them has their own line, and none of them is you. Act on one or none.", body, "gbrief");
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-why]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const k = b.getAttribute("data-why"), o = S.cab[k], cr = creedOf(o.creed), og = originOf(o.origin);
    el("adv_" + k).textContent = "“I am " + o.bg + ", of " + cr.t + ", and my people carry the grievance " + og.grievance + ". That is why I read it the way I do. Another adviser will read it differently, and you should let them.”"; }));
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-adv]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [k, j] = b.getAttribute("data-adv").split(":"); if(did[k]) return; did[k] = 1; spend(10, 1);
    const r = acts[k][+j].run(); el("adv_" + k).textContent = r; S.cab[k].warm = (S.cab[k].warm || 0) + 1; try{ tlog("You", r, "you"); }catch(e){} }));
  return null;
}
/* the budget: four agency heads, each with their own case and their own view */
function govBudget2(S){
  if(!S){ return "Nothing on the budget today."; }
  govStaff(S);
  const y = G.you, avail = govAvail(S), W = {};
  const reqs = Object.keys(GOV_AGENCIES).map(k => { const A = GOV_AGENCIES[k], o = S.agency[k], r = rng(seedOf("req:" + k + ":" + S.n + ":" + G.day)); const ask = Math.round((A.ask[0] + r() * (A.ask[1] - A.ask[0]))) * 1000; return {k, A, o, ask}; });
  const pitch = q => { const t = q.o.pos[q.A.ax] || 0, A = q.A; const X = DK_AXIS[A.ax], lean = Math.abs(t) > 20 ? "My own bent is toward " + (t > 0 ? X.hi.w : X.lo.w).toLowerCase() + ", and you should weigh my case knowing it; " + (t > 0 ? "I will still argue that " : "I will argue that ") + A.t.toLowerCase() + " cannot wait." : "I will not pretend I have a doctrine; I have a list.";
    return "We need " + curF(q.ask) + " for " + A.why + ". " + lean + " If you cannot do it all, half buys the first of it and I will come back in the spring."; };
  const body = '<p class="muted">Unallocated this week: <b>' + curF(avail) + '</b>. The four requests come to ' + curF(reqs.reduce((a, q) => a + q.ask, 0)) + '. You can fund one in full, or half of one and keep the rest.</p>' +
    reqs.map(q => '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)">' + officialHTML(q.o) + '<p style="margin:6px 0">“' + pcEsc(pitch(q)) + '”</p><div class="muted" style="font-size:12px">' + pcEsc(q.A.t) + ': unrest ' + (q.A.effect[0] > 0 ? "+" : "") + q.A.effect[0] + ', industry ' + (q.A.effect[1] > 0 ? "+" : "") + q.A.effect[1] + ', approval ' + (q.A.effect[2] > 0 ? "+" : "") + q.A.effect[2] + ' at full funding.</div>' +
      '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-bud="' + q.k + ':1"' + (q.ask > avail ? ' disabled title="More than the state has this week"' : '') + '>Fund in full ' + curF(q.ask) + '</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-bud="' + q.k + ':0.5">Half ' + curF(Math.round(q.ask / 2000) * 1000) + '</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-bud="' + q.k + ':0">Refuse</button></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("Agencies and the budget", "This week's money", "Four people who run four departments, each sure theirs is the one that cannot wait.", body, null);
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-bud]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const [k, f] = b.getAttribute("data-bud").split(":"), q = reqs.find(x => x.k === k), frac = +f; if(!q || W.done) return; W.done = 1; spend(30, 3);
    const e = q.A.effect; S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + Math.round(e[0] * frac), 0, 100); S.ind = clamp(S.ind + Math.round(e[1] * frac), 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval + Math.round(e[2] * frac), 0, 100);
    q.o.warm = (q.o.warm || 0) + (frac >= 1 ? 3 : frac > 0 ? 1 : -3);
    const react = reqs.map(x => { if(x.k === k) return x.o.name + (frac >= 1 ? ": “Thank you. You will see it on the first of the month.”" : frac > 0 ? ": “Half is a start. I will be back in the spring.”" : ": “I will put it in writing that you refused me.”"); x.o.warm = x.o.warm || 0; return x.o.name + ": “" + (frac > 0 ? "Noted. We will make do." : "At least you were even-handed.") + "”"; }).join("\n");
    el("gcSay").style.whiteSpace = "pre-line"; el("gcSay").textContent = (frac > 0 ? "You fund " + q.A.t.toLowerCase() + (frac < 1 ? " by half" : "") + ". " : "You refuse " + q.A.t.toLowerCase() + ". ") + "\n" + react;
    card.querySelectorAll("[data-bud]").forEach(x => x.disabled = true); try{ kMark("gbud"); }catch(e){}
    feed("Governor " + surname(y.name) + (frac > 0 ? " funded " + q.A.t.toLowerCase() + "." : " refused the " + q.A.t.toLowerCase() + " request."), frac > 0 ? "good" : "bad"); }));
  return null;
}
/* appointments: named people with views, who backs them, and the cost */
const APPT = {
  judge:{t:"a state judge", post:"Judge of the state bench", ax:"lib", ctx:"A seat on the state bench has fallen open. The bench rules on what the statehouse writes."},
  roads:{t:"a director of public works", post:GOV_AGENCIES.roads.head, ax:"econ", ctx:"The roads are a quarrel about whether the state builds or the market bids."},
  schools:{t:"a superintendent of schools", post:GOV_AGENCIES.schools.head, ax:"wel", ctx:"The schools are a quarrel about how much the state provides."},
  police:{t:"a chief of the constabulary", post:GOV_AGENCIES.police.head, ax:"lib", ctx:"The constabulary is a quarrel about order and liberty."},
  health:{t:"a commissioner of health", post:GOV_AGENCIES.health.head, ax:"wel", ctx:"The hospitals are a quarrel about thrift and provision."},
  cab:{t:"a cabinet secretary", post:"Secretary", ax:"econ", ctx:"A cabinet post has fallen open. The Senate will have to confirm whoever you name."}
};
function appointCard(kind){
  const y = G.you, S = (G.states || []).find(s => s.n === y.state), P = APPT[kind]; if(!P) return null;
  const cands = [0, 1, 2].map(i => { const o = mkOfficial("appt:" + kind + ":" + G.day + ":" + i, S, P.post);
    if(i === 0) o.pos[P.ax] = clamp(o.pos[P.ax] + 40, -100, 100); if(i === 1) o.pos[P.ax] = clamp(o.pos[P.ax] - 40, -100, 100);
    const backers = AXES.filter(a => Math.abs(o.pos[a.k]) > 25).sort((a, b) => Math.abs(o.pos[b.k]) - Math.abs(o.pos[a.k]))[0];
    const stake = backers ? (DK_STAKE[backers.k] || []).filter(x => x[1] * (o.pos[backers.k] || 0) > 0).map(x => x[0]) : [];
    const foes = backers ? (DK_STAKE[backers.k] || []).filter(x => x[1] * (o.pos[backers.k] || 0) < 0).map(x => x[0]) : [];
    const odds = Math.round(clamp(60 + (y.standing - 50) / 2 + (S && S.lean ? (o.pos.econ - S.lean) * -0.1 : 0) + (i === 1 ? -6 : 0), 20, 95));
    return {o, backers:stake, foes, odds}; });
  const body = cands.map((c, i) => '<div style="margin:10px 0;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--line-soft)">' + officialHTML(c.o) +
    '<p style="margin:6px 0;font-size:13px"><b>Who backs them:</b> ' + pcEsc(c.backers.length ? listify(c.backers) : "no organised group") + '. <b>Who objects:</b> ' + pcEsc(c.foes.length ? listify(c.foes) : "nobody in particular") + '. <b>Chance it is confirmed without a fight:</b> about ' + c.odds + '%.</p>' +
    '<div class="card__actions" style="flex-wrap:wrap"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-q="' + i + '">Interview</button><button type="button" class="btn" data-ap="' + i + '">Appoint ' + pcEsc(surname(c.o.name)) + '</button></div><div class="dream" id="aq_' + i + '"></div></div>').join("");
  govCardOpen("Appointments", "Who will be " + P.t + "?", P.ctx + " Three people have put their names forward.", body, null);
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-q]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const c = cands[+b.getAttribute("data-q")], a = AXES.find(x => x.k === P.ax), v = c.o.pos[P.ax] || 0;
    el("aq_" + b.getAttribute("data-q")).textContent = "“" + (Math.abs(v) < 14 ? "On " + a.n.toLowerCase() + " I follow the evidence and the room. I would rather tell you that than a doctrine." : v > 0 ? "I would push toward " + a.hi + ": a state that " + DK_AXIS[P.ax].hi.does + "." : "I would push toward " + a.lo + ": a state that " + DK_AXIS[P.ax].lo.does + ".") + " I will do what you ask, and I will say so in public if I disagree.”"; }));
  card.querySelectorAll("[data-ap]").forEach(b => b.addEventListener("click", () => { const c = cands[+b.getAttribute("data-ap")]; if(card.querySelector("[data-done]")) return;
    const av = apptVote(kind, c.o, S), ok = av.ok; spend(40, 4);
    if(kind === "cab" && ok){ try{ const post = cabOpenPost(); const p = cabInstall(post, c.o); if(p){ c.o.name = p.name; c._postTitle = post.t; } }catch(e){} }
    if(ok){ if(S && (GOV_AGENCIES[kind])){ govStaff(S); S.agency[kind] = c.o; } if(kind === "judge"){ y.approval = clamp(y.approval + ((c.o.pos.lib || 0) > 0 ? 1 : 0), 0, 100); } y.standing = clamp(y.standing + 1, 0, 100); try{ y.used = y.used || {}; y.used[kind === "judge" ? "appt" : kind === "cab" ? "cab" : "appt2"] = G.day; }catch(e){} }
    const postName = (kind === "cab" && c._postTitle) ? c._postTitle : P.post;
    const msg = ok ? c.o.name + " is confirmed as " + postName.toLowerCase() + " by " + av.body + ", " + av.aye + " to " + av.no + ". " + cap(viewWords(c.o.pos)) + "; you will hear it in how they advise you." : cap(av.body) + " rejects " + c.o.name + ", " + av.aye + " to " + av.no + ". The name is withdrawn and the seat stays open.";
    reactEmit("appoint", {kind, name:c.o.name, ok, post:P.post}); el("gcSay").textContent = msg; feed(msg, ok ? "good" : "bad"); card.querySelectorAll("[data-ap]").forEach(x => { x.disabled = true; x.setAttribute("data-done", "1"); }); }));
  return null;
}
const CASE_BILL = {bread:"the Bread Price Relief Act", order:"the Local Constabulary Aid Act", road:"the Rural Road and Culvert Act", school:"the Schoolhouse and Teachers Act", water:"the Municipal Water Compliance Act", plant:"the Local Industry Retention Act", ballots:"the Special Elections (Mail Ballot) Act", pension:"the Widows' Pension Notice Act"};
/* ── nothing you do stays yours: once it is out, the House, the Senate, the bench, the executive and the neighbours each have their own job to do about it ── */
function reactEmit(kind, data, delay){
  G.react = G.react || []; G.react.push({kind, data:data || {}, due:(G.day || 0) + (delay == null ? 1 : delay), from:G.day});
  const who = {actSigned:"the courts, the House and the press", actVetoed:"the Speaker and the Senate leader", stateBill:"the statehouse, the Union's attorney and the press", treaty:"the executive, their assembly and the hawks",
    confirm:"the bench and the minority", foreign:"the opposition, the rival realms and the press", appoint:"the legislature and the department", ruling:"Congress and the states", senVote:"the House and the President"}[kind] || "everyone concerned";
  try{ feed("Word is out. " + cap(who) + " will answer it tomorrow.", ""); }catch(e){}
}
function reactAct(title, pos, signed){ reactEmit(signed ? "actSigned" : "actVetoed", {title, pos:pos || null}); }
function reactState(S, b, signed){ try{ reactEmit("stateBill", {state:S ? S.n : (G.you && G.you.state), title:b.title, signed, ind:b.ind || 0, unrest:b.unrest || 0, dir:b.dir || 1, axis:b.axis || "econ"}); }catch(e){} }
function reactHolder(post, party){
  const m = (G.members || []).filter(x => x && !x.gone && x.kind === "member");
  return m.find(x => x.post === post) || (party ? m.find(x => x.party === party) : null) || m[Math.floor(Math.random() * Math.max(1, m.length))] || null;
}
function reactSay(m, text, news){
  try{ feed(text); journal(text); }catch(e){}
  try{ if(m){ voxInit(); voxAdd({id:G.vox.id++, by:m.id, t:text, k:"react", v:0, day:G.day, at:hhmm(), backs:Math.round(Math.random() * 40), hits:Math.round(Math.random() * 25), voices:[], mine:false}); } }catch(e){}
  if(news !== false){ G.reactNews = (G.reactNews || []).concat([{t:text, d:G.day}]).slice(-12); }
}
function reactFrac(pos, title){
  const bill = {pos:pos || {econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0}, title:title || "act", id:"r:" + title}, mem = (G.members || []).filter(m => m && !m.gone && m.kind === "member" && m.pos);
  let n = 0; mem.forEach(m => { try{ if(alignment(m, bill) > 0) n++; }catch(e){} }); return mem.length ? n / mem.length : 0.5;
}
function reactResolve(e){
  if(/^war/.test(e.kind)){ warReact(e); return; }
  if(/^gw/.test(e.kind)){ govWarReact(e); return; }
  if(e.kind === "lwVote"){ legWarReact(e); return; }
  const y = G.you, d = e.data, opp = pty => pty === "FED" ? "COM" : "FED";
  if(e.kind === "actVetoed"){
    const act = (G.lastActs || []).find(a => a.title === d.title), fr = reactFrac(d.pos, d.title), sp = reactHolder("speaker");
    const ok = chance(clamp((fr - 0.55) * 4, 0, 0.95));
    if(ok){ if(act){ act.vetoed = false; act.signed = true; act.overridden = true; } y.standing = clamp(y.standing - 2, 0, 100); reactSay(sp, (sp ? "Speaker " + surname(sp.name) + ": " : "") + "the House and Senate have overridden the veto of the " + d.title + ". It is law without a signature."); }
    else reactSay(sp, (sp ? "Speaker " + surname(sp.name) + ": " : "") + "the House tried to override the veto of the " + d.title + " and fell short of two thirds. The veto stands.");
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "actSigned"){
    const act = (G.lastActs || []).find(a => a.title === d.title), ct = courtTest({pos:d.pos || {econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0}, title:d.title, id:"c:" + d.title});
    const o = reactHolder("minority"), a = reactHolder("speaker");
    if(ct && !ct.ignored){ if(act) act.struck = true; y.approval = clamp(y.approval - 1, 0, 100); reactSay(null, "The bench has struck down the " + d.title + ", " + ct.strike + " to " + ((G.court || []).length - ct.strike) + ". It never took effect."); }
    else if(ct && ct.ignored) reactSay(null, "The bench objected to the " + d.title + " and was ignored. Nobody enforced the ruling.");
    else reactSay(null, "The " + d.title + " survives a challenge in the courts and goes into force.");
    if(o) reactSay(o, "Minority Leader " + surname(o.name) + ": the " + d.title + " " + (reactFrac(d.pos, d.title) > 0.5 ? "is a step, and we will watch how it is run." : "is the wrong answer to the right question."), false);
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "stateBill"){
    const S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === d.state); if(!S) return;
    if(d.signed){
      if(d.axis === "lib" || d.axis === "def" ? chance(0.3) : chance(0.1)){ G.cases = G.cases || []; G.cases.push({t:"the Union v. " + d.state, state:d.state, day:G.day, voted:[]}); reactSay(null, "The Union's attorney has filed against " + d.state + " over the " + d.title + ". It goes to the bench."); }
      else reactSay(null, "The " + d.title + " takes effect in " + d.state + ". " + (d.unrest > 0 ? "The counties are bracing." : "The counties are watching."));
      const rep = (G.members || []).find(m => m && !m.gone && m.state === d.state && m.kind === "member"); if(rep) reactSay(rep, "Representative " + surname(rep.name) + ": the governor signed the " + d.title + "; home will see what it does.", false);
    } else {
      const ok = chance(clamp(0.3 + (d.dir * (S.lean || 0)) / 200, 0.1, 0.8));
      if(ok){ S.ind = clamp(S.ind + d.ind, 0, 100); S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + d.unrest, 0, 100); y.approval = clamp(y.approval - 2, 0, 100); reactSay(null, "The " + d.state + " legislature overrode your veto of the " + d.title + ". It is law."); }
      else reactSay(null, "The " + d.state + " legislature tried to override your veto of the " + d.title + " and could not find the votes.");
    }
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "treaty"){
    const r = WORLD_POWERS.find(p => p.k === d.k), rel = G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}; if(!r) return;
    if(d.ok){
      const ex = G.exec && !G.exec.you ? G.exec : null;
      if(ex && chance(0.2)){ rel[d.k] = clamp((rel[d.k] || 0) - 4, -100, 100); reactSay(null, "The President declines to exchange instruments with " + r.t + ". The Senate has consented; the executive has not acted."); }
      else if(d.verb === "res" && chance(0.4)){ rel[d.k] = clamp((rel[d.k] || 0) - 6, -100, 100); reactSay(null, "The assembly of " + r.t + " refuses the Senate's reservation. The treaty is in doubt."); }
      else { rel[d.k] = clamp((rel[d.k] || 0) + 3, -100, 100); reactSay(null, "Instruments are exchanged with " + r.t + ". The treaty is in force."); }
      const h = reactHolder("armed"); if(h) reactSay(h, "Armed Services Chair " + surname(h.name) + ": the treaty with " + r.t + " will be read line by line, and the Chair will be asking what the garrisons get out of it.", false);
    } else if(d.verb === "no"){ rel[d.k] = clamp((rel[d.k] || 0) - 3, -100, 100); reactSay(null, (rel[d.k] < -20 ? cap(r.t) + " recalls its ambassador for consultations." : cap(r.t) + " asks for a meeting at the working level.")); }
    else reactSay(null, cap(r.t) + " says the Senate is stalling, and will say so at home.");
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "confirm"){
    if(d.confirmed){ const J = G.court || [], avg = J.length ? J.reduce((a, j) => a + ((j.pos && j.pos.econ) || 0), 0) / J.length : 0; const o = reactHolder("minority");
      reactSay(null, d.name + " takes the bench. The court now leans " + (avg > 8 ? "toward the market" : avg < -8 ? "toward the public" : "neither way") + " on the economy; its next opinions will show it.");
      if(o) reactSay(o, "Minority Leader " + surname(o.name) + ": the new justice will be judged by the opinions, not by the introductions.", false);
    } else reactSay(null, "The White House is said to be looking for another name after " + d.name + ". The seat stays open for now.");
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "foreign"){
    const r = WORLD_POWERS.find(p => p.k === d.k), rel = G.realmRel = G.realmRel || {}; if(!r) return;
    const o = reactHolder("minority");
    if(d.verb === "aid"){ if(o) reactSay(o, "Minority Leader " + surname(o.name) + ": money to " + r.t + " while the farm counties go short is a choice, and the House will ask for the figures."); if(G.world && G.world.foe && G.world.foe !== d.k){ const f = WORLD_POWERS.find(p => p.k === G.world.foe); rel[G.world.foe] = clamp((rel[G.world.foe] || 0) - 2, -100, 100); reactSay(null, f.t + " notes the aid to " + r.t + " and files it."); } else reactSay(null, cap(r.t) + " thanks the Union publicly and privately asks for more."); }
    else if(d.verb === "trade"){ reactSay(null, "Merchants in the harbour towns welcome the " + r.t + " schedule; the farm co-ops want to read it first."); }
    else if(d.verb === "warn" || d.verb === "press"){ if(G.world && G.world.foe === d.k) G.world.heat = clamp((G.world.heat || 0) + 2, 0, 100); reactSay(null, cap(r.t) + " " + (d.verb === "warn" ? "answers the warning with a statement for its own papers." : "gives a little ground and asks for something in return.")); }
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "appoint"){
    const s2 = reactHolder("speaker");
    reactSay(null, d.ok ? d.name + " takes up the post of " + String(d.post || "").toLowerCase() + ". The department's staff are reading everything they have written." : "The legislature rejected " + d.name + "; the post of " + String(d.post || "").toLowerCase() + " is still vacant.", true);
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "ruling"){
    const S = (G.states || []).find(x => x.n === d.state), h = reactHolder("judic");
    if(d.dual) reactSay(null, "The House is drafting an amendment on holding two offices, after the bench's ruling in " + d.t + ".");
    else if(d.forUnion){ if(S) S.unrest = clamp(S.unrest + 2, 0, 100); reactSay(null, "The governor of " + d.state + " says the state will comply, slowly, and that the legislature will ask Congress to revisit the mandate."); }
    else { reactSay(null, d.state + " keeps its money and its rules. The Union's attorney says the administration will study the opinion."); }
    if(h) reactSay(h, "Judiciary Chair " + surname(h.name) + ": the committee will look at the bench's reasoning in " + d.t + " before anything is written down.", false);
    return; }
  if(e.kind === "senVote"){
    const ex = G.exec, fit = ex && !ex.you ? alignment(ex, {pos:d.pos || {econ:0, lib:0, def:0, wel:0}, title:d.title}) : 0, sp = reactHolder("speaker");
    reactSay(sp, (sp ? "Speaker " + surname(sp.name) + ": " : "") + "the House will take up the Senate's action on the " + d.title + " this week.", false);
    if(ex && !ex.you) reactSay(null, "The White House " + (fit > 0 ? "signals the President would sign the " + d.title + "." : fit < -18 ? "issues a veto threat on the " + d.title + "." : "says the President is reading the " + d.title + "."));
    return; }
}
function reactDay(){
  const Q = G.react || []; if(!Q.length) return; const keep = [];
  Q.forEach(e => { if(e.due <= G.day){ try{ reactResolve(e); }catch(x){ try{ console.warn("react", x); }catch(e2){} } } else keep.push(e); });
  G.react = keep;
}
/* ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THE PURSE · one money for everyone
   You, a Senator, a baker and a clerk all keep the same kind of purse and play by
   the same rules: you earn, you pay for where you live, and the rest is yours to
   spend or keep, on your own time and by your own temper. A person who spends in
   public is seen, and everyone who sees it has an opinion and a choice about what
   to do with it, the player no differently from anybody else. The campaign's war
   chest, and anything taken from a donor, is not the purse: it cannot be spent on
   yourself, so there is nothing here to launder it through.
   ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
const PURSE_ITEMS = {
  coffee:{shop:"diner", t:"a coffee", price:2, show:0, min:10, energy:4, line:"A coffee, thanks."},
  lunch:{shop:"diner", t:"the lunch special", price:6, show:0, min:30, energy:10, line:"The lunch special, please."},
  round:{shop:"diner", t:"a round for the counter", price:30, show:2, min:25, appr:2, line:"This round is on me."},
  paper:{shop:"newsstand", t:"the morning paper", price:1, show:0, min:5, paper:1, line:"The Ledger, please."},
  book:{shop:"newsstand", t:"a book", price:12, show:0, min:20, infl:1, line:"I'll take that one."},
  groceries:{shop:"market", t:"groceries for a household", price:15, show:0, min:15, gift:"hh", line:"Put together a basket for somebody who needs it."},
  flowers:{shop:"market", t:"flowers", price:8, show:1, min:10, gift:"person", line:"Those flowers, wrapped."},
  coat:{shop:"market", t:"a tailored coat", price:140, show:2, min:30, style:2, line:"I'll have the coat taken in."},
  suit:{shop:"market", t:"a fine suit", price:380, show:3, min:45, style:3, line:"The best cloth you have, cut to me."},
  watch:{shop:"market", t:"a gold watch", price:900, show:3, min:20, style:4, line:"That one, in the case."},
  gate:{shop:"hardware", v:"Pay for", t:"mending a neighbour's gate", price:15, show:1, min:40, appr:2, line:"Hinges and a latch, please."},
  box:{shop:"church", v:"Put", t:"coins in the poor box", price:10, show:0, min:10, appr:1, line:""},
  rent:{shop:"church", v:"Pay", t:"a family's rent for the month", price:60, show:1, min:20, appr:3, line:""}
